{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_8", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/test/_helpers.py; ls -la bench/programs; cat cores/bench/LESSONS.md'", "aggregated_output": "\"\"\"Shared cocotb constants and runner helpers for unit tests.\n\nConstants mirror rtl/core_pkg.sv. If a localparam there changes, change\nthe matching value here.\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport os\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\n# cocotb 2.x moved the runner from cocotb.runner to cocotb_tools.runner.\nfrom cocotb_tools.runner import get_runner\n\n# ── ALU encodings (rtl/core_pkg.sv) ────────────────────────────────────────\nALU_ADD    = 0\nALU_SUB    = 1\nALU_AND    = 2\nALU_OR     = 3\nALU_XOR    = 4\nALU_SLT    = 5\nALU_SLTU   = 6\nALU_SLL    = 7\nALU_SRL    = 8\nALU_SRA    = 9\nALU_LUI    = 10\nALU_MUL    = 11\nALU_MULH   = 12\nALU_MULHU  = 13\nALU_MULHSU = 14\nALU_DIV    = 15\nALU_DIVU   = 16\nALU_REM    = 17\nALU_REMU   = 18\n\n# ── BranchOp encodings (= funct3 of BRANCH opcode) ─────────────────────────\nBR_BEQ  = 0\nBR_BNE  = 1\nBR_BLT  = 4\nBR_BGE  = 5\nBR_BLTU = 6\nBR_BGEU = 7\n\n# ── Paths ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nREPO_ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent\nRTL       = REPO_ROOT / \"rtl\"\nTEST_DIR  = REPO_ROOT / \"test\"\nSIM_BUILD = REPO_ROOT / \"sim_build\"\n\n\ndef run_cocotb(toplevel: str, sources: list[str], test_module: str) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Build the DUT under Verilator and run the given cocotb test_module.\n\n    `sources` is a list of bare filenames under rtl/. Order matters —\n    package files (e.g. core_pkg.sv) come first.\n    \"\"\"\n    sim = os.environ.get(\"SIM\", \"verilator\")\n    runner = get_runner(sim)\n    build_dir = SIM_BUILD / toplevel\n\n    runner.build(\n        sources=[str(RTL / s) for s in sources],\n        hdl_toplevel=toplevel,\n        build_dir=str(build_dir),\n        always=True,\n        build_args=[\"-Wall\", \"-Wno-fatal\", \"-Wno-style\"],\n    )\n    runner.test(\n        hdl_toplevel=toplevel,\n        test_module=test_module,\n        test_dir=str(TEST_DIR),\n        build_dir=str(build_dir),\n    )\ntotal 464\ndrwxrwx---+  3 nobody nogroup   4096 Nov 19 20:59 .\ndrwxrwx---+  3 nobody nogroup   4096 Nov 19 20:59 ..\n-rw-rw----+  1 nobody nogroup   2317 Nov 19 20:59 Makefile\ndrwxrwx\n…[7271 of 10343 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:22fac4f0b8de6e8c]…\noreMark cycle count in paired prototypes.\n- 2026-11-19 hyp-20261119-001-r9s0 (regression, +2.64%): Registering equality at load writeback let dependent BEQ/BNE instructions issue without a load-use bubble, saving 132,211 cycles over ten CoreMark iterations, but divider feedback limited median Fmax to 80.689 MHz, below the 82.23 MHz needed for acceptance.\n- 2026-11-19 hyp-20261119-002-r9s1 (regression, +4.87%): Parallel block-RAM probes at ID/EX, EX/MEM and MEM/WB avoided the load-use bubble on validated hits and saved 285,599 cycles over ten CoreMark iterations, but divider feedback limited median Fmax to 78.681 MHz and throughput to 245.13 iterations/s versus the round winner's 245.28.\n- 2026-11-19 hyp-20261119-003-r9s2 (improvement, +4.94%): Storing the instruction and predicted target in one PC-tagged row let fetch serve hits during instruction-bus waits and let EX validate a predicted-taken branch or JAL target with the same_word bit because the matching PC and instruction uniquely determine that target.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
