{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_96","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/implementation_notes.md'","aggregated_output":"# Reciprocal divider\n\nThe local FPGA fitness run measured **261.99 CoreMark iterations/s** at a median **89.447 MHz**, above the 87.594 MHz threshold. Ten iterations took 3,414,124 cycles between the MMIO markers with instruction and data stalls enabled. All five CRCs matched.\n\n| Gowin placement option | Fmax (MHz) |\n| --- | ---: |\n| 0 | 81.827 |\n| 1 | 89.447 |\n| 2 | 89.447 |\n\nThe median placement's longest path goes from fetch block RAM to the registered ALU immediate in decode. The resource tradeoff is four additional BSRAMs and four additional DSPs. Gowin reported 15 BSRAMs, six DSPs, 3,337 logic cells and 1,091 registers.\n\n## Implementation\n\nThe ALU captures the dividend magnitude, divisor magnitude minus one and result flags on issue. A synchronous 2,048-word ROM supplies a conservative reciprocal. The divider reuses one unsigned high-product datapath and one low-product datapath to estimate the quotient twice. The second estimate uses the residual from the first. A 33-bit subtraction selects the final correction in phase 7, and EX transfers the result on the eighth edge.\n\nTwo details differ from the proposed datapath.\n\n- ROM address zero holds `0xffffffff`. For divisor magnitude one and nonzero dividend magnitude A, the estimates are A−1 and zero. The final correction produces A and remainder zero. This eliminates the separate signed dividend bypass. Division by zero selects all ones, and the zero divisor naturally preserves the dividend for remainder operations.\n- Phase 4 signs the first quotient term. Phase 6 registers both possible signed quotients so the final comparison only selects between them. The second term uses eleven bits in this sum. The bucket test checks that the first residual is below 2,048 divisors. For divisors at least 2³¹, the original dividend is already below two divisors.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Verilator lint passed with all warnings enabled by the requested command. Yosys elaborated all 2,048 ROM words with their expected values.\n- The bench unit suite passed all 118 cocotb cases and the integer bound check for all 22,527 applicable buckets. Directed tests exercise all four division operations around bucket endpoints, powers of two and representable multiples. They change operands and operation after issue and check the exact busy and done edges.\n- The fast single-channel ALTOPS formal suite passed all 53 checks. The ALU tests exercise the hardware arithmetic and signed corner cases.\n- Co-simulation passed for selftest and three random instruction programs with and without bus stalls. Stalled CoreMark printed “Correct operation validated.” and completed without an out-of-bounds access.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
