{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"rg -n 'romstyle|block_rom|reciprocal|divider' cores/bench/LESSONS.md cores/bench/rtl; ls -l /opt/gowin/IDE\"","aggregated_output":"cores/bench/LESSONS.md:2:- 2026-11-19 hyp-20261119-002-r1s1 (improvement, +692.41%): Replacing combinational DIV/REM in EX with a shared six-round restoring divider shortened the critical path and raised median Gowin Fmax from 5.44 to 43.1 MHz, while timed CoreMark incurred no divider stalls because it executed neither operation.\ncores/bench/LESSONS.md:3:- 2026-11-19 hyp-20261119-003-r1s2 (regression, +7.76%): Correctly predicting a taken branch or JAL in fetch avoided a one-cycle EX redirect bubble, but the combinational DIV/REM path still limited CoreMark throughput to 13.06 iterations/s versus 96.04 with the six-round divider.\ncores/bench/LESSONS.md:6:- 2026-11-19 hyp-20261119-003-r2s2 (regression, +6.70%): Looking up branch, JAL and JALR targets in a 256-entry block-RAM BTB during fetch cut CoreMark cycles by about 7%, but the six-round divider still set Fmax, leaving throughput at 102.47 iterations/s versus 109.64 with the radix-8 divider.\ncores/bench/LESSONS.md:17:- 2026-11-19 hyp-20261119-001-r7s0 (regression, +4.69%): For nonzero divisor magnitudes below 2^17, two radix-8 stages need only 20-bit trial operands, while at or above 2^17 the top 17 dividend bits already form a valid remainder, so one full-width stage per cycle suffices and the prototype's critical path shifted from divider feedback to writeback through EX to the fetch PC.\ncores/bench/LESSONS.md:23:- 2026-11-19 hyp-20261119-001-r9s0 (regression, +2.64%): Registering equality at load writeback let dependent BEQ/BNE instructions issue without a load-use bubble, saving 132,211 cycles over ten CoreMark iterations, but divider feedback limited median Fmax to 80.689 MHz, below the 82.23 MHz needed for acceptance.\ncores/bench/LESSONS.md:24:- 2026-11-19 hyp-20261119-002-r9s1 (regression, +4.87%): Parallel block-RAM probes at ID/EX, EX/MEM and MEM/WB avoided the load-use bubble on validated hits and saved 285,599 cycles over ten CoreMark iterations, but divider feedback limited median Fmax to 78.681 MHz and throughput to 245.13 iterations/s versus the round winner's 245.28.\ncores/bench/LESSONS.md:26:- 2026-11-19 hyp-20261119-001-r10s0 (regression, +6.81%): Applying the same ROM reciprocal to the dividend and then its residual let registered DSP products replace the serial radix-8 trials, raising CoreMark throughput to 261.99 iterations/s at the same cycle count.\ncores/bench/rtl/alu.sv:24:  // Phase 0 accepts a request. Phases 1 through 6 run the divider.\ncores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv:183:      // These EX/MEM fields can hold them across the invalid divider slots.\ntotal 32\ndrwxr-xr-x   9 nobody nogroup 4096 Jul 10  2025 bin\ndrwxr-xr-x  10 nobody nogroup 4096 Jul 10  2025 data\ndrwxr-xr-x   5 nobody nogroup 4096 Jul 10  2025 doc\ndrwxr-xr-x 113 nobody nogroup 4096 Jul 10  2025 ipcore\ndrwxr-xr-x  12 nobody nogroup 4096 Jul 10  2025 lib\ndrwxr-xr-x   4 nobody nogroup 4096 Jul 10  2025 plugins\ndrwxr-xr-x   6 nobody nogroup 4096 Jul 10  2025 share\ndrwxr-xr-x   5 nobody nogroup 4096 Jul 10  2025 simlib\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_14", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"cat test/cosim/build.sh; cat bench/programs/Makefile; cat formal/checks_si.cfg; ls -d .toolchain; rg 'implementation_notes|sim_build|obj_dir|generated|\\\\.elf' .gitignore\"", "aggregated_output": "#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# Build the Verilator-based cosim binary that drives `core` against an ELF\n# program. Produces $OBJ_DIR/cosim_sim (default: test/cosim/obj_dir/cosim_sim).\n#\n# RTL_DIR (default: rtl/) is globbed dynamically (with core_pkg.sv forced\n# first because its compilation-unit-scope typedefs and localparams must be\n# visible before any module references them). Hypotheses are allowed to add,\n# rename, or delete files inside rtl/, so a hardcoded file list would\n# silently break restructuring hypotheses.\nset -euo pipefail\n\nREPO_ROOT=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"${BASH_SOURCE[0]}\")/../..\" && pwd)\"\nCOSIM_DIR=\"$REPO_ROOT/test/cosim\"\nif [ -z \"${RTL_DIR:-}\" ] || [ -z \"${OBJ_DIR:-}\" ]; then\n  echo \"ERROR: test/cosim/build.sh requires RTL_DIR and OBJ_DIR env vars.\" >&2\n  echo \"  Example: RTL_DIR=cores/v1/rtl OBJ_DIR=cores/v1/obj_dir bash test/cosim/build.sh\" >&2\n  exit 2\nfi\n\n# NRET picks which RVFI port set main.cpp expects on `core`.\n# 1 = single-issue (only `_0` ports); 2 = dual-channel (both `_0` and `_1`).\n# Default 2 preserves existing behavior; orchestrator sets to 1 for cores\n# whose core.yaml declares nret: 1.\nNRET=\"${NRET:-2}\"\n\n# Ensure OSS CAD Suite tools are on PATH for non-interactive shells.\nTOOLCHAIN=\"$REPO_ROOT/.toolchain\"\nif [ -d \"$TOOLCHAIN/oss-cad-suite/bin\" ]; then\n  export PATH=\"$TOOLCHAIN/oss-cad-suite/bin:$PATH\"\nfi\n\nmkdir -p \"$OBJ_DIR\"\n\n# Glob $RTL_DIR/*.sv. core_pkg.sv first; the rest in a stable lexicographic\n# order (modulo case-insensitive sort, which Verilator/gcc don't care\n# about). If core_pkg.sv is missing the build will catch that downstream\n# via undefined-typedef errors.\nRTL_FILES=()\n[ -f \"$RTL_DIR/core_pkg.sv\" ] && RTL_FILES+=(\"$RTL_DIR/core_pkg.sv\")\nfor f in \"$RTL_DIR\"/*.sv; do\n  [ \"$(basename \"$f\")\" = \"core_pkg.sv\" ] && continue\n  RTL_FILES+=(\"$f\")\ndone\n\nif [ ${#RTL_FILES[@]} -eq 0 ]; then\n  echo \"ERROR: no rtl/*.sv files found.\" >&2\n  exit 1\nfi\n\nverilator --cc --exe --build \\\n  -Mdir \"$OBJ_DIR\" \\\n  \"+incdir+$RTL_DIR\" \\\n  --top-module core \\\n  -Wall -Wno-fatal -Wno-style \\\n  -CFLAGS \"-DN\n…[3257 of 6329 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:5357c30efd10ae44]…\ne full rationale on what ALTOPS does and does not prove. M-extension\n# arithmetic correctness is covered by test/test_alu.py and `make formal-deep`.\n`define RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS\n\n[cover]\n# Sanity cover: the CPU must retire at least one non-trapping instruction.\nalways @* if (!reset) cover (rvfi_valid && !rvfi_trap);\n\n[verilog-files]\n# run_all.sh rebuilds this section from the actual rtl/ glob; the list\n# below is overwritten before genchecks runs. Kept as a placeholder so\n# the section is syntactically present for any reader inspecting the cfg.\n@basedir@/cores/@core@/core.sv\n@basedir@/cores/@core@/wrapper.sv\nls: cannot access '.toolchain': No such file or directory\n# Formal run output (regenerated per run; surfaced via stdout to the orchestrator).\ngenerated/\nsim_build/\ntest/cosim/obj_dir/\ntest/cosim/sim_build/\ntest/**/sim_build/\nbench/programs/*.elf\nbench/holdout/build/*.elf\n#   the latest state is always viewable from GitHub. Regenerated and\ncores/*/generated/\ncores/*/obj_dir/\ncores/*/implementation_notes.md\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
