{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_99","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"git status --short; git diff --check; git check-ignore cores/bench/implementation_notes.md; sed -n '1,40p' cores/bench/implementation_notes.md; date -u\"","aggregated_output":" M cores/bench/rtl/alu.sv\n M cores/bench/test/test_alu.py\ncores/bench/implementation_notes.md\n# Piecewise-linear reciprocal divider\n\nThe divider captures the operands and signs on issue. Phase 1 decodes the leading bit of `D-1` to select the intercept, slope, fraction, and scale in parallel. Phases 2 and 3 interpolate and round the reciprocal. Phases 4 and 5 share one unsigned 32×32 multiplier for the quotient estimate and its product with the divisor. Phase 6 registers the corrected quotient or remainder magnitude. EX applies the saved sign and consumes the result in phase 7. All four operations retain the eight-cycle schedule, including zero divisors and signed overflow.\n\nThree implementation details affect synthesis. A single 1,024-iteration initialization loop fills both halves of the intercept ROM and the slope ROM within Gowin's elaboration limit. The exact small-divisor path keeps the full 32-bit table word. The interpolated path uses a 24-bit adder because its value is below `4 × 2^32 / 1024`. The subtraction that forms `R-D` also supplies the borrow for the correction decision.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Verilator lint passed with `-Wall`. All 130 cocotb tests passed, including 27 ALU and 59 pipeline tests.\n- The added tests cover all four DIV/REM operations around reciprocal and power-of-two boundaries, signed and unsigned multiples near the limits, all three correction outcomes, and consecutive requests with changing operands. They check the busy and done edges on every division.\n- Local fast formal passed all 53 checks with ALTOPS.\n- A Verilated real-arithmetic sweep checked both endpoints of all 46,137,343 fractional bins. All 83,886,079 requests returned the expected unsigned result and satisfied `-D < M×D - 2^32 ≤ D`. The bound extends over each bin because `M` is constant there. With the dividend below `2^32`, the quotient estimate needs at most one correction.\n- Co-simulation matched the ISS for selftest and three random programs, each with and without bus stalls. Stalled CoreMark completed ten iterations in 3,182,385 bracketed cycles. All five CRCs matched and the UART reported successful validation.\n\n## FPGA result\n\nGowin placement options 0, 1, and 2 reached 86.170, 91.058, and 91.058 MHz. The median yields **286.13 iterations/s**, 7.19% above 266.94. The design uses 4,208 logic cells, 1,110 flip-flops, 16 BSRAMs, and four DSPs. The reciprocal tables occupy five BSRAMs. The median placement's worst path runs from the EX/MEM ALU opcode to the MEM/WB read-data register. Placement option 0 falls below the 88.86 MHz target on its own.\nThu Nov 19 21:09:04 UTC 2026\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
