{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_62","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'git diff --check; git status --short --untracked-files=all; cat cores/bench/implementation_notes.md'","aggregated_output":" M cores/bench/rtl/core.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/if_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py\n# One-word fall-through fetch buffer\n\nIF saves a ready instruction when a load/multiply interlock, data-memory wait, or busy divider holds decode. On release, decode can issue the saved instruction during an instruction-bus wait or refill the slot from a ready bus on the same edge. Decode, hazard detection, and forwarding all use the selected instruction. Reset and EX redirects clear the slot and the fence wait.\n\nThe buffer stores the instruction and ten PC bits, `pc[11:2]`. The last word of a 4 KiB page can only issue directly, so the buffered word and the bus PC always share the page number and alignment bits. Only a full, stalled slot needs to preserve its payload. This keeps the EX redirect off the wide payload register enables. FENCE.I also issues directly, and IF waits until it leaves EX before accepting the successor.\n\n## Local results\n\n| Check | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| Verilator lint | Passed with zero warnings |\n| Cocotb | 90 cases passed |\n| Single-retire ALTOPS formal | All 53 checks passed on the final RTL on the first attempt |\n| RVFI cosimulation | Selftest and three random programs matched the ISS with ready buses and with both buses stalling |\n| Stalled CoreMark | 10 iterations in 4,375,771 bracketed cycles, all five CRCs matched, validation message present |\n| Gowin Fmax, placement options 0 / 1 / 2 | 75.045 / 80.027 / 80.027 MHz |\n| Local fitness | 182.89 iterations/s, up 4.92% from 174.31 |\n| Placement 0 area | 3,384 logic cells and 752 registers, increases of 91 cells and 44 registers |\n\nThe four new pipeline tests check load-use release during a fetch wait, same-edge refill followed by a redirect over a buffered store, an interlock at PC 0xffc, and a stalled store that rewrites the instruction after FENCE.I. They check the retirement path, operand or result data, and accepted memory requests. Two existing tests now expect the one-word fetch advance during a stall.\n\nThe median Fmax clears the stated 79.783 MHz threshold by 0.244 MHz. Placement 0 falls below it. The worst reported path for each placement runs through the divider.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_63","type":"agent_message","text":"Implemented the one-word fetch buffer with a 10-bit page-local PC offset.\n\n**Local fitness reached 182.89 iterations/s, up 4.92%.** Ten stalled CoreMark iterations took 4,375,771 bracketed cycles. Median Gowin Fmax was 80.027 MHz, clearing the threshold by 0.244 MHz.\n\nLint, all 90 cocotb cases, all 53 formal checks, ISS cosimulation, and all five CoreMark CRCs passed. [Implementation notes](/srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6_2-astra_xhigh-v2-rep1/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20261119-001-r6s0/cores/bench/implementation_notes.md)"}}
