{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_6", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/rtl/if_stage.sv; cat cores/bench/LESSONS.md'", "aggregated_output": "// rtl/if_stage.sv\n//\n// Instruction fetch stage. Holds the PC register; the IF/ID payload\n// (pc + instr + valid) is *combinational* — there is no separate IF/ID\n// flop in this microarchitecture, the next-stage's ID/EX register\n// captures everything one cycle later.\n//\n// Decode uses the live instruction whenever imem is ready. After a BTB\n// hit or a short backward branch, recorded instructions can cover waits.\n//\n// Latency:        PC-reg update is synchronous; output is combinational.\n// RVFI fields:    feeds pc_rdata (via ID/EX/MEM/WB) and pc_wdata (via\n//                 EX-stage redirect).\nmodule if_stage (\n  input  logic              clock,\n  input  logic              reset,\n  input  logic              stall,\n  input  logic              recover_target,\n  input  logic              recover_fallthrough,\n  input  logic              taken,\n  input  logic [31:2]       target,\n  input  logic              train,\n  input  logic [1:0]        next_counter,\n  input  logic              short_back_branch,\n  input  logic              fence_i,\n  input  logic              issue_valid,\n  input  logic [31:2]       issue_pc,\n  input  logic [31:0]       issue_instr,\n  output logic [31:0]       imem_addr,\n  input  logic [31:0]       imem_data,\n  input  logic              imem_ready,\n  output if_id_t  out\n);\n\n  logic [31:2] normal_pc, target_q, fallthrough_q;\n  logic use_target, use_fallthrough;\n  wire recovering = use_target || use_fallthrough;\n  wire [31:2] pc_word = ({30{!recovering}} & normal_pc)\n                      | ({30{use_target}} & target_q)\n                      | ({30{use_fallthrough}} & fallthrough_q);\n  wire [31:0] pc = {pc_word, 2'b00};\n\n  // One write port for both EX training and the invalidation sweep. Fetch\n  // continues sequentially while the valid bits are being cleared.\n  typedef struct packed {\n    logic        valid;\n    logic [19:10] tag;\n    logic [1:0]  counter;\n    logic [19:2] target;\n  } btb_row_t;\n  (* syn_ramstyle = \"block_ram\" *) logic [30:0] btb [0:255];\n  btb_row_t lookup;\n  logic [29:0] \n…[8467 of 11539 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:031f5b9df22fa3a9]…\ncrease in CoreMark cycles.\n- 2026-11-19 hyp-20261119-001-r7s0 (regression, +4.69%): For nonzero divisor magnitudes below 2^17, two radix-8 stages need only 20-bit trial operands, while at or above 2^17 the top 17 dividend bits already form a valid remainder, so one full-width stage per cycle suffices and the prototype's critical path shifted from divider feedback to writeback through EX to the fetch PC.\n- 2026-11-19 hyp-20261119-002-r7s1 (regression, +6.26%): Probing a 128-entry replay table on every fetch let ID/EX accept saved controls and immediates at jump targets and loop exits during instruction-bus waits, cutting prototype CoreMark cycles by 4.98% versus replay limited to short backward loops.\n- 2026-11-19 hyp-20261119-003-r7s2 (improvement, +10.56%): Starting replay at the target or fall-through predicted by a BTB hit let fetch serve resident words during instruction-bus waits, saving 83,953 cycles across ten CoreMark iterations versus the same predictor with replay triggered only by short backedges.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
