{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_29", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -n 'critical_path|critical.*path|perturbations' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | tail -2 | cut -c1-3200; sed -n '1,190p' fpga/core_bench_si.sv; date -u\"", "aggregated_output": "24:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261119-002-r8s1\", \"title\": \"Read the next issued instruction one fetch ahead\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The champion takes 3,731,234 cycles for ten CoreMark iterations at\\n80.546 MHz. Its BTB can predict a frequently executed target whose\\ninstruction has already been evicted from the 64-word replay store.\\nThe preceding instruction's fetch cycle is available for a synchronous\\nRAM read, even across a correctly predicted jump.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The champion takes 3,731,234 cycles for ten CoreMark iterations at\\n80.546 MHz. Its BTB can predict a frequently executed target whose\\ninstruction has already been evicted from the 64-word replay store.\\nThe preceding instruction's fetch cycle is available for a synchronous\\nRAM read, even across a correctly predicted jump.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Record the next instruction observed after each advancing EX instruction.\\nWhen its predecessor is fetched again, read the record into a register.\\nOn the following cycle, a match with the actual fetch PC can supply the\\nword during an imem wait. The existing BTB chooses the address. Only the\\nraw instruction is replayed, so decode, operand reads, forwarding and\\nretirement run anew. A changed branch outcome or an index collision\\ncan lose a hit without issuing a word from a different address.\\n\\nKeep the address comparison on the valid path. On a bus wait, select\\nthe successor RAM output after initialization and the existing loop\\nreplay word during initialization. Compare operand tags on each source\\nin parallel, then qualify the matching source for the load-use interlock.\\nPutting the successor-address comparison ahead of the instruction mux\\nextended the path from block RAM through hazard detection to the BTB.\\n\\nA scratch prototype took 3,431,589 marker-bracketed cycles, 8.03% fewer\\nthan the champion, with all five canonical CRCs. Gowin placements reached\\n78.078, 78.032 and 78.032 MHz. The median gives 227.39 iterations/s, a\\n5.34% gain over 215.87. The 4.6% acceptance margin r\n…[7308 of 10380 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:0bcaca084f6517a9]…\nio_rvfi_ixl_0      (rvfi_ixl_0),\n    .io_rvfi_rs1_addr_0 (rvfi_rs1_addr_0),\n    .io_rvfi_rs1_rdata_0(rvfi_rs1_rdata_0),\n    .io_rvfi_rs2_addr_0 (rvfi_rs2_addr_0),\n    .io_rvfi_rs2_rdata_0(rvfi_rs2_rdata_0),\n    .io_rvfi_rd_addr_0  (rvfi_rd_addr_0),\n    .io_rvfi_rd_wdata_0 (rvfi_rd_wdata_0),\n    .io_rvfi_pc_rdata_0 (rvfi_pc_rdata_0),\n    .io_rvfi_pc_wdata_0 (rvfi_pc_wdata_0),\n    .io_rvfi_mem_addr_0 (rvfi_mem_addr_0),\n    .io_rvfi_mem_rmask_0(rvfi_mem_rmask_0),\n    .io_rvfi_mem_wmask_0(rvfi_mem_wmask_0),\n    .io_rvfi_mem_rdata_0(rvfi_mem_rdata_0),\n    .io_rvfi_mem_wdata_0(rvfi_mem_wdata_0)\n  );\n\n  // V2: observe only the memory-side outputs. Everything the core computes\n  // reaches the fetch address or a store, so the datapath stays in the\n  // netlist; logic that only drives RVFI (a verification port a deployed\n  // core would not have) is pruned and does not count toward Fmax or area.\n  assign led = ^{imem_addr, dmem_addr, dmem_wdata, dmem_wen, dmem_ren, dmem_rdata};\n\nendmodule\nThu Nov 19 19:04:45 UTC 2026\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
