{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_161","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"stat -c '%n %w' .agent.log; tail -3 formal/last_run-wTYbY5XO6.log; date -u; git diff --check; cat cores/bench/implementation_notes.md | tail -7\"","aggregated_output":".agent.log 2026-11-19 19:59:43.376727828 +0100\nSBY 20:25:32 [insn_sub_ch0] summary: engine_0 (smtbmc bitwuzla) returned pass\nSBY 20:25:32 [insn_sub_ch0] summary: engine_0 did not produce any traces\nSBY 20:25:32 [insn_sub_ch0] DONE (PASS, rc=0)\nThu Nov 19 19:28:05 UTC 2026\nThe directed pipeline tests cover lane selection and extension, either or both matching sources, both misprediction directions, a stale predicted target, instruction and data waits, trapped loads and branches, wrong-path stores, FENCE.I and division, and the remaining multiply and ordered-branch interlocks.\n\nCoreMark completed ten iterations in 3,363,206 marker-bracketed cycles with both buses stalling. All five canonical CRCs matched and UART reported “Correct operation validated.” Selftest and the three random programs matched the ISS with ready and stalled buses. The single-channel RVFI interface follows the target's declared `nret: 1`.\n\nGowin placement options 0, 1 and 2 reached 80.355, 80.689 and 80.689 MHz. The median gives 239.92 CoreMark iterations/s, a 2.64% gain over the supplied baseline. The 80.689 MHz median falls short of the 82.23 MHz acceptance threshold. The longest path on placement option 1 is divider feedback. Timing experiments with different divider result selection lowered Fmax, so the original divider is retained.\n\nVerilator lint and all 111 cocotb cases passed. Two earlier RTL revisions passed all 53 standard formal checks. The final ALTOPS run has passed 52 checks, with register consistency still running. No counterexample has been reported.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
