{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_50","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"git diff --check; git status --short; rg -n 'Warning|Error' \\\"\"'$TMPDIR/bench-cosim.log\" | head -4; cat cores/bench/implementation_notes.md'","aggregated_output":" M cores/bench/rtl/alu.sv\n M cores/bench/test/test_alu.py\n# Split divider at 4096\n\nThe divider captures both unsigned magnitudes, the result kind and the result sign on issue. For a divisor of at least 4096, it initializes the remainder from the top 12 dividend bits. Five radix-16 rounds each select one of 16 digit/remainder pairs from parallel trial differences. For divisors from 2 through 4095, a synchronous reciprocal ROM feeds two separately registered unsigned multipliers. A single residual comparison corrects a low estimate. Zero and unit divisors take the same eight EX cycles.\n\nThe datapaths follow the proposed phase schedule. The ROM initializer writes four 1024-word ranges in one 1024-iteration loop. The Gowin synthesis report attributes eight BSRAMs and both divider multipliers to the ALU.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Verilator passed the requested full-core lint command with zero warnings.\n- All five cocotb suites passed. The ALU tests check every reciprocal divisor at and just below a multiple, all 16 radix-16 digits in all five positions, signed and unsigned threshold cases, and consecutive requests alternating paths. Each request checks operand capture and the completion edge.\n- Co-simulation passed for selftest and three random programs with and without bus stalls. With both buses stalled, CoreMark ran ten iterations in 3,182,385 bracketed cycles and printed the validation message. The five CRCs were e9f5, e714, 1fd7, 8e3a and fcaf.\n\n## Gowin timing\n\n| Placement option | Fmax (MHz) |\n| --- | ---: |\n| 0 | 86.890 |\n| 1 | 90.977 |\n| 2 | 90.977 |\n\nThe 90.977 MHz median gives 285.88 CoreMark iterations/s, 7.10% above the 84.949 MHz baseline at the same cycle count. The median placement's worst setup path ran from MEM/WB writeback data to the replay register. Placement option 0 fell below the 88.86 MHz threshold. The design used 4,703 logic cells, 1,329 registers, 19 BSRAMs and five DSPs.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
