{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"rg --files cores/bench && rg -n 'implementation_notes|nret|invariant|RVFI' CLAUDE.md && ls -l formal\"","aggregated_output":"cores/bench/CORE_PHILOSOPHY.md\ncores/bench/core.yaml\ncores/bench/rtl/decoder.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/forward_unit.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/imm_gen.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/mem_stage.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/alu.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/if_stage.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/reg_file.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/hazard_unit.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/id_stage.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/wb_stage.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/core.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/core_pkg.sv\ncores/bench/LESSONS.md\ncores/bench/experiments/progress.png\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\ncores/bench/test/_helpers.py\ncores/bench/test/test_decoder.py\ncores/bench/test/test_reg_file.py\ncores/bench/test/test_alu.py\ncores/bench/test/conftest.py\ncores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py\ncores/bench/test/test_imm_gen.py\n1:# CLAUDE.md — non-negotiable invariants and don't-touch list\n7:## Hard invariants\n11:| 1 | Top module `core` exposes an RVFI port set selected by `cores/<target>/core.yaml`'s `nret` field (default 2). **nret=1**: only `io_rvfi_*_0` ports exist; the single retirement always lands on channel 0. **nret=2**: both `io_rvfi_*_0` and `io_rvfi_*_1` exist; channel 0 carries the older of two simultaneous retirements, channel 1 the younger; single-retire cycles MUST place the retirement on channel 0 with `io_rvfi_valid_1 = 0`; all channel-1 ports MUST be driven (no X/Z, tie unused fields to `'0`). | cocotb smoke test, `riscv-formal` wrapper (`wrapper.sv` for nret=2, `wrapper_si.sv` for nret=1) |\n58:`cores/<TARGET>/test/test_*.py`. The agent's `implementation_notes.md`\n59:lives at `cores/<TARGET>/implementation_notes.md` (gitignored). The\n63:The only top-level invariant on `rtl/core.sv` is that it exposes a port\n64:named `core` whose IO matches the RVFI wrapper's expectations: the\n67:`io_dmemREn`, `io_dmemRea