{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_175", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'git diff --check; git status --short; cat cores/bench/implementation_notes.md; for d in cores/bench/generated/timing/gowin_p?; do tail -2 \"$d/gw.log\"; done'", "aggregated_output": " M cores/bench/rtl/core.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/core_pkg.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/forward_unit.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/id_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/mem_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/wb_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py\n?? cores/bench/rtl/word_probe.sv\n# Registered-source load probes\n\nFour synchronous 512-word banks share one write port. Three follow the update enables and next values of ID/EX rs1, the EX/MEM forwarding result, and the registered architectural WB result. The fourth follows the effective-address register. Each row contains a valid bit, RAM address bits [19:2], and the unextended word.\n\nID registers the youngest matching writer for each operand. EX selects the corresponding row and extends its data using the effective byte offset. MEM checks the source tag and RAM range in parallel with the consumer. A rejected candidate falls back to the effective-address bank or the external bus. A dependent miss holds the consumer and the previous WB forwarding payload, captures the corrected word and result in EX/MEM once, then releases the consumer. An independent instruction advances on load completion.\n\nAccepted RAM reads and full-word stores fill all copies. Partial stores invalidate their index. Probe validity accounts for read/write collisions, writes during a hold, and the store leaving MEM. MMIO stays on the bus. EX suppresses memory and register writes on alignment faults. Reset invalidates all rows in 512 clocks while loads use the existing bus and load-use interlock. Multiplication retains its one-bubble interlock.\n\nThe target declares one retirement channel in core.yaml. RVFI reports the selected raw word, architectural byte masks, extended writeback value, and in-order retirement on channel 0.\n\nGowin timing also led to three changes in the result and recovery paths. The jump link, AUIPC result, and candidate load data feed EX in parallel with the ALU. MEM extracts the fallback RAM and bus values in parallel with tag validation. ID prepares the displacement and predicted-target terms used by EX to check the carries of the target sum, allowing redirect qualification to run alongside target addition.\n\n## Local checks\n\n- Verilator lint passed without warnings.\n- All 111 cocotb cases passed, including 41 pipeline cases. They cover each forwarding distance, an immediately dependent divide, a collision held across repair, and a stalled request crossing the end of a second reset sweep.\n- Co-simulation passed five ELFs. The stalled ten-iteration CoreMark run completed in 3,209,818 bracketed cycles with all five canonical CRCs and the validation message.\n- The first formal attempt stopped during Yosys parsing of a type argument to `$bits`. Replacing it with the explicit 51-bit RAM width let all 53 formal checks pass on the initial implementation. The timing-refined RTL is undergoing its separate full-suite run.\n- Gowin's `core_bench_syn_rsc.xml` attributes all eight probe block RAMs to `u_actual_probe` after synthesis. The three source probes and the actual-address probe have independent synchronous read addresses in RTL. The full design uses 17 SDPB block RAM primitives, including five for instruction fetch and four in the benchmark wrapper. The 32 distributed RAM primitives belong to the register file.\n- A separate 32-bit bit-vector equivalence check proved the parallel target comparison agrees with the architectural target addition for every aligned taken transfer.\n\nThe bounded formal checks end at cycle 20, during the data-store reset sweep. The post-sweep cocotb tests and stalled CoreMark run exercise warm hits, replacement, and repair.\nThu Nov 19 20:25:33 2026\n\n[70%] Routing Phase 1 completed\n[80%] Routing Phase 2 completed\n[70%] Routing Phase 1 completed\n[80%] Routing Phase 2 completed\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
