{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_15", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'tail -n 2 cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | cut -c1-4000; cat formal/wrapper_si.sv'", "aggregated_output": "{\"id\": \"hyp-20261119-002-r11s1\", \"title\": \"Split division at 12 divisor bits to remove the serial trial path\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The champion's reported worst path crosses 60 cells from quotient_q to\\nremainder_q. Its small-divisor mode resolves two dependent radix-8\\ndigits on that path. CoreMark executes zero DIV or REM instructions\\nbetween the markers, so a shorter feedback path can improve the clock\\nfor all 3,182,385 bracketed cycles. A median above 88.86 MHz would\\nclear the 4.6% acceptance margin at this cycle count.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The champion's reported worst path crosses 60 cells from quotient_q to\\nremainder_q. Its small-divisor mode resolves two dependent radix-8\\ndigits on that path. CoreMark executes zero DIV or REM instructions\\nbetween the markers, so a shorter feedback path can improve the clock\\nfor all 3,182,385 bracketed cycles. A median above 88.86 MHz would\\nclear the 4.6% acceptance margin at this cycle count.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Give the divider two operand-width-specific datapaths with a common\\neight-cycle EX handshake. For unsigned divisor magnitude D >= 4096,\\nthe upper 12 dividend bits already form a reduced remainder. Exactly\\n20 dividend bits remain. Consume one radix-16 digit per cycle for five\\ncycles. Each cycle tests fifteen multiples of D in parallel and selects\\nthe remainder for the largest multiple that fits.\\nThis removes the second dependent trial from the feedback loop.\\n\\nFor 2 <= D < 4096, read floor(2^32/D) from a synchronous 4096-word ROM.\\nThe high half of its unsigned product with dividend magnitude A gives\\na quotient estimate q. Since A < 2^32, reciprocal truncation loses\\nless than one quotient unit, so q is exact or one low. Form R = A - q*D.\\nIf R >= D, increment q and subtract D once. Place register boundaries\\nbetween the lookup, the two DSP products and correction. Both paths\\ndeliver their selected signed quotient or remainder at the existing\\ncompletion edge.\\n\\nA scratch implementation passed the ALU and pipeline \n…[7789 of 10861 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:bb2966bdbf77a6f7]…\ndirectly without\n        // slicing. No `_1` ports exist on the core's IO under nret=1.\n        .io_rvfi_valid_0    (rvfi_valid),\n        .io_rvfi_order_0    (rvfi_order),\n        .io_rvfi_insn_0     (rvfi_insn),\n        .io_rvfi_trap_0     (rvfi_trap),\n        .io_rvfi_halt_0     (rvfi_halt),\n        .io_rvfi_intr_0     (rvfi_intr),\n        .io_rvfi_mode_0     (rvfi_mode),\n        .io_rvfi_ixl_0      (rvfi_ixl),\n        .io_rvfi_rs1_addr_0 (rvfi_rs1_addr),\n        .io_rvfi_rs1_rdata_0(rvfi_rs1_rdata),\n        .io_rvfi_rs2_addr_0 (rvfi_rs2_addr),\n        .io_rvfi_rs2_rdata_0(rvfi_rs2_rdata),\n        .io_rvfi_rd_addr_0  (rvfi_rd_addr),\n        .io_rvfi_rd_wdata_0 (rvfi_rd_wdata),\n        .io_rvfi_pc_rdata_0 (rvfi_pc_rdata),\n        .io_rvfi_pc_wdata_0 (rvfi_pc_wdata),\n        .io_rvfi_mem_addr_0 (rvfi_mem_addr),\n        .io_rvfi_mem_rmask_0(rvfi_mem_rmask),\n        .io_rvfi_mem_wmask_0(rvfi_mem_wmask),\n        .io_rvfi_mem_rdata_0(rvfi_mem_rdata),\n        .io_rvfi_mem_wdata_0(rvfi_mem_wdata)\n    );\n\nendmodule\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
