{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_93","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'git diff --check && git status --short --ignored && cat cores/bench/implementation_notes.md'","aggregated_output":" M cores/bench/rtl/core.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/core_pkg.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/id_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/if_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py\n!! .agent.last\n!! .agent.log\n!! cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\n!! formal/riscv-formal\n# Direct control-transfer prediction\n\nThe stalled ten-iteration CoreMark run took **4,193,225 bracketed cycles**. The three Gowin placement options reached 5.146, 5.478, and 5.478 MHz. The median gives **13.06 iterations/s**, about **7.8% above** the supplied 12.12 iterations/s baseline.\n\n## Implementation\n\nFetch indexes 256 two-bit saturating counters with `PC[9:2]`. The counter RAM has an asynchronous read and a synchronous EX write. Reset clears the valid bitmap. A cold entry supplies binary `10` for a negative displacement and `01` otherwise. The counter MSB selects the direction for legal conditional branches. JAL predicts taken. Both use fall-through if the direct target is misaligned or outside the first MiB. JALR always resolves in EX.\n\nThe ID/EX register carries the selected direction and counter snapshot through stalls. EX resolves the instruction using forwarded operands. A direction miss flushes the younger fetch and selects the resolved target or fall-through. A held branch trains when the older data access completes. RVFI receives the resolved successor, including PC+4 for a misalignment trap.\n\nFetch and ID share the existing immediate generator through the combinational IF/ID bundle, so prediction and resolution use the same displacement. The existing hazard unit already holds fetch until ID can accept an instruction and bubbles ID on recovery. Its redirect input now receives the qualified prediction miss. The interface follows the bench core's declared single retirement channel.\n\nBranches separated by 1 KiB share a counter. A same-index lookup concurrent with training captures the pre-write state. Either can affect prediction accuracy. EX checks the direction for each instruction independently.\n\n## Local verification\n\n- Verilator passed `--lint-only -Wall -Wno-MULTITOP`.\n- The single-channel ALTOPS formal suite passed all 53 checks. All formal runs passed without counterexamples.\n- All 83 cocotb cases passed. Directed pipeline tests check counter saturation and hysteresis, consecutive target retirement, loop-exit store squashing, legal and trapping transfers, and exact fetch and RVFI sequences under imem, dmem, and load-use stalls.\n- Cosimulation matched selftest and three random programs against the ISS both with and without bus stalls. Stalled CoreMark reported `Correct operation validated.` and matched the five canonical CRCs in seed, list, matrix, state, and final order (`e9f5`, `e714`, `1fd7`, `8e3a`, `fcaf`).\n- Gowin reported 12,967 logic cells, 719 registers and 24 LUT-RAM cells. The worst setup path for placement option 0 runs through writeback and the EX ALU into data memory.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
