{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_4", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"cat cores/bench/core.yaml cores/bench/LESSONS.md; rg --files --hidden -g '\"'!**/.git'\"' -g 'AGENTS.md' -g '*test*' -g '*gowin*'; ls -l formal; printenv | cut -d= -f1 | rg 'FORMAL|GOWIN|TARGET|RISCV|BENCH'\"", "aggregated_output": "name: bench\ndescription: Frozen LLM-benchmark fixture core. Identical RTL to baseline at the bench-fixture-v1\n  freeze point. The benchmark matrix clones from the bench-fixture-v1 orphan branch\n  and operates only on this directory.\nisa: rv32im\nnret: 1\ntarget_fpga: tang-nano-20k\ntargets:\n  fmax_mhz: 135\n  lut4: 10000\n  coremark_iter_s: 300\n  coremark_per_mhz: 2.2\ncurrent:\n  fmax_mhz: 49.243\n  lut4: 3260\n  ff: 663\n  coremark_iter_s: 2.0e-06\n  coremark_per_mhz: 0.0\n  source_id: hyp-20261119-002-r2s1\n  updated: '2026-11-19T15:03:10.022292Z'\n- 2026-11-19 hyp-20261119-001-r1s0 (regression, +476.16%): CoreMark executes no divide or remainder between its timing markers, so chaining eight restoring steps per cycle saved no benchmark cycles over six and lowered median Gowin Fmax from 43.1 to 31.4 MHz.\n- 2026-11-19 hyp-20261119-002-r1s1 (improvement, +692.41%): Replacing combinational DIV/REM in EX with a shared six-round restoring divider shortened the critical path and raised median Gowin Fmax from 5.44 to 43.1 MHz, while timed CoreMark incurred no divider stalls because it executed neither operation.\n- 2026-11-19 hyp-20261119-003-r1s2 (regression, +7.76%): Correctly predicting a taken branch or JAL in fetch avoided a one-cycle EX redirect bubble, but the combinational DIV/REM path still limited CoreMark throughput to 13.06 iterations/s versus 96.04 with the six-round divider.\n- 2026-11-19 hyp-20261119-001-r2s0 (regression, +10.42%): Replacing six serial restoring steps with three radix-4 digits per full round raised median Gowin Fmax from 43.1 to 47.6 MHz at the same CoreMark cycle count and shifted the critical path from remainder_q feedback to the register-file read through EX to data memory.\n- 2026-11-19 hyp-20261119-002-r2s1 (improvement, +14.16%): Registering 3D, 5D and 7D during the two-bit opening round let each later round resolve six quotient bits in two radix-8 stages of parallel trial subtraction and selection, raising median Gowin Fmax from 43.1 to 49.2 MHz at the same CoreMark cycle count.\n- 2026-11-19 hyp-20261119-003-r2s2 (regression, +6.70%): Looking up branch, JAL and JALR targets in a 256-entry block-RAM BTB during fetch cut CoreMark cycles by about 7%, but the six-round divider still set Fmax, leaving throughput at 102.47 iterations/s versus 109.64 with the radix-8 divider.\nbench/programs/selftest.S\ntools/agents/test_hypothesis.py\ntools/agents/test_static_agent.py\ntools/agents/test_hypothesis_workspace.py\ntools/agents/test_quota.py\ntools/agents/test_scribe.py\ntools/agents/test_random_agent.py\ntools/agents/test_agent_scope_live.py\ncores/bench/test/test_imm_gen.py\ncores/bench/test/conftest.py\ncores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py\ncores/bench/test/test_decoder.py\ncores/bench/test/test_reg_file.py\ncores/bench/test/test_alu.py\ntools/eval/gowin.py\ntools/eval/test_gate_sanity.py\ntools/eval/test_holdout.py\ntools/eval/test_formal_workdir_cleanup.py\ntools/eval/test_rvfi_lint.py\ntools/eval/test_process_reaper.py\ntools/eval/test_formal_reclassify.py\ntools/eval/test_remove_path.py\ntools/eval/test_subprocess_pgroup.py\ntools/eval/test_slots.py\ntools/eval/test_bench_stall_gen.py\ntools/eval/test_fpga_report.py\ntools/eval/test_formal_nret.py\ntest/conftest.py\ntotal 40\n-rw-rw----+ 1 nobody nogroup  2630 Nov 19 16:15 checks-deep.cfg\n-rw-rw----+ 1 nobody nogroup  2658 Nov 19 16:15 checks.cfg\n-rw-rw----+ 1 nobody nogroup  1455 Nov 19 16:15 checks_si.cfg\nlrwxrwxrwx+ 1 nobody nogroup    68 Nov 19 16:15 riscv-formal -> /srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6_2-astra_xhigh-v2-rep1/formal/riscv-formal\n-rwxrwx---+ 1 nobody nogroup 10597 Nov 19 16:15 run_all.sh\n-rw-rw