{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_5", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'rg --files cores/bench && cat cores/bench/core.yaml && cat formal/run_all.sh'", "aggregated_output": "cores/bench/core.yaml\ncores/bench/rtl/decoder.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/forward_unit.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/imm_gen.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/mem_stage.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/alu.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/if_stage.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/reg_file.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/hazard_unit.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/id_stage.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/wb_stage.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/core.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/core_pkg.sv\ncores/bench/LESSONS.md\ncores/bench/CORE_PHILOSOPHY.md\ncores/bench/test/test_imm_gen.py\ncores/bench/test/conftest.py\ncores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py\ncores/bench/test/_helpers.py\ncores/bench/test/test_decoder.py\ncores/bench/test/test_reg_file.py\ncores/bench/test/test_alu.py\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\ncores/bench/experiments/progress.png\nname: bench\ndescription: Frozen LLM-benchmark fixture core. Identical RTL to baseline at the bench-fixture-v1\n  freeze point. The benchmark matrix clones from the bench-fixture-v1 orphan branch\n  and operates only on this directory.\nisa: rv32im\nnret: 1\ntarget_fpga: tang-nano-20k\ntargets:\n  fmax_mhz: 135\n  lut4: 10000\n  coremark_iter_s: 300\n  coremark_per_mhz: 2.2\ncurrent:\n  fmax_mhz: 78.925\n  lut4: 3293\n  ff: 708\n  coremark_iter_s: 2.0e-06\n  coremark_per_mhz: 0.0\n  source_id: hyp-20261119-002-r5s1\n  updated: '2026-11-19T16:28:06.991498Z'\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# Run riscv-formal checks against the current $RTL_DIR/*.sv.\n# Requires: formal/riscv-formal cloned (manual clone or `git submodule init`).\n#\n# Stages every $RTL_DIR/*.sv plus wrapper.sv + the chosen checks config under\n# the riscv-formal tree, then runs sby -> bitwuzla via the framework's\n# generated makefile. Tallies PASS/FAIL by inspecting each task's\n# logfile.txt.\n#\n# Usage: bash formal/run_all.sh [checks-cfg-path]\n#   default: formal/checks.cfg       (fast, ALTOPS, used by orchestrator)\n#   deep   : formal/checks-deep.cfg  (no ALTOPS, proves M-ext arithmetic)\n#\n# Env vars (orchestrator-driven, override $1 and defaults):\n#   WRAPPER     — path to wrapper SV (default formal/wrapper.sv)\n#   CHECKS_CFG  — path to checks config (default formal/\n…[8790 of 11862 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:ddfe83fbebfba9bd]…\nheses make the assumption satisfiable, so this\n        # branch never matches and the regular DONE (PASS branch covers it.\n        PASS=$((PASS+1))\n    else\n        FAIL=$((FAIL+1)); FAILED+=(\"$name\")\n    fi\ndone\nTOTAL=$((PASS+FAIL))\nif [ $TOTAL -eq 0 ]; then\n    FAIL=1\n    FAILED+=(\"no_checks_generated\")\nfi\n\necho \"\"\necho \"Formal: $PASS passed, $FAIL failed\"\nif [ $FAIL -gt 0 ]; then\n    echo \"Failed: ${FAILED[*]}\"\n    # Surface the FIRST failing check's logfile tail. tools/eval/formal.py\n    # captures this script's stdout/stderr into formal['detail'] and the\n    # orchestrator now records that in experiments/log.jsonl, so what we\n    # print here is what shows up as the diagnostic for the failed run.\n    first=\"${FAILED[0]}\"\n    if [ -f \"$first/logfile.txt\" ]; then\n        echo \"\"\n        echo \"--- $first/logfile.txt (last 30 lines) ---\"\n        tail -30 \"$first/logfile.txt\"\n    fi\n    echo \"\"\n    echo \"Full run log: $LOG\"\n    echo \"Per-check logs in: $CORE_DIR/checks/<check>/logfile.txt\"\nfi\n[ $FAIL -eq 0 ]\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_4", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"cat cores/bench/rtl/if_stage.sv cores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv && rg -n 'stall|redirect' cores/bench/rtl/core.sv && rg -n 'implementation_notes|sim_build|\\\\.tmp' .gitignore && printenv TMPDIR\"", "aggregated_output": "// rtl/if_stage.sv\n//\n// Instruction fetch stage. Holds the PC register; the IF/ID payload\n// (pc + instr + valid) is *combinational* — there is no separate IF/ID\n// flop in this microarchitecture, the next-stage's ID/EX register\n// captures everything one cycle later.\n//\n// Decode sees the raw memory word while EX resolves a branch. ID/EX\n// records whether the word was ready and survived a redirect or replay.\n//\n// Latency:        PC-reg update is synchronous; output is combinational.\n// RVFI fields:    feeds pc_rdata (via ID/EX/MEM/WB) and pc_wdata (via\n//                 EX-stage redirect).\nmodule if_stage (\n  input  logic              clock,\n  input  logic              reset,\n  input  logic              stall,\n  input  logic              redirect,         // EX has resolved a branch/jump\n  input  logic [31:0]       redirect_target,\n  output logic [31:0]       imem_addr,\n  input  logic [31:0]       imem_data,\n  input  logic              imem_ready,\n  output if_id_t  out\n);\n\n  localparam logic [31:0] RESET_PC = 32'h0000_0000;\n\n  logic [31:0] pc;\n\n  // Redirect must override stall: a BRANCH/JAL/JALR in EX may fire\n  // redirect on the same cycle as imem_stall or dmem_stall — without\n  // this priority the redirect target would be silently dropped, the\n  // PC would hold its old (wrong-path) value, and execution would\n  // resume on the wrong path once the bus unstalls. Verified by the\n  // VexRiscv-binary CoreMark sweep with --istall enabled.\n  always_ff @(posedge clock) begin\n    if      (reset)    pc <= RESET_PC;\n    else if (redirect) pc <= redirect_target;\n    else if (!stall)   pc <= pc + 32'd4;\n  end\n\n  assign imem_addr = pc;\n\n  always_comb begin\n    out.pc    = pc;\n    out.instr = imem_data;\n    out.valid = imem_ready;\n  end\n\nendmodule\n// rtl/ex_stage.sv\n//\n// Execute stage. Resolves the operand muxes (forwarding from EX/MEM and\n// MEM/WB), runs the ALU, resolves branches, computes the redirect\n// target. Owns the EX/MEM pipeline register.\n//\n// Each source has independent EX/MEM (bit 0) and MEM/WB (bit \n…[5912 of 8984 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:9ad8a02ea5ac0c05]…\nll,\n20://                 redirect).\n30:  // V0 default). Drive 0 to stall sequential fetch. An advancing ID/EX\n32:  // Used by test/cosim/vex_main.cpp's --istall mode to match VexRiscv's\n80:  logic       stall_if, stall_id, bubble_id;\n81:  logic       stall_ex_mem, hold_mem_wb;\n85:  // EX redirect\n86:  logic        redirect;\n87:  logic [31:0] redirect_target;\n102:    .stall           (stall_if),\n103:    .redirect        (redirect),\n104:    .redirect_target (redirect_target),\n115:    .stall    (stall_id),\n141:    .stall           (stall_ex_mem),\n149:    .redirect        (redirect),\n150:    .redirect_target (redirect_target)\n181:    .redirect       (redirect),\n186:    .stall_if       (stall_if),\n187:    .stall_id       (stall_id),\n189:    .stall_ex_mem   (stall_ex_mem),\n195:    .stall_id    (stall_id),\n201:    // A dmem stall clears WB valid but keeps the forwarding payload live.\n52:sim_build/\n54:test/cosim/sim_build/\n55:test/**/sim_build/\n87:cores/*/implementation_notes.md\n/srv/hwebench/tmp/800f6bc6/952f5315\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
