{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_8", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"cat cores/bench/core.yaml; cat .gitignore; rg -n 'GOWIN|gw_sh|toolchain' tools/eval/gowin.py; ls -l formal; ls -a cores/bench; git rev-parse --show-toplevel\"", "aggregated_output": "name: bench\ndescription: Frozen LLM-benchmark fixture core. Identical RTL to baseline at the bench-fixture-v1\n  freeze point. The benchmark matrix clones from the bench-fixture-v1 orphan branch\n  and operates only on this directory.\nisa: rv32im\nnret: 1\ntarget_fpga: tang-nano-20k\ntargets:\n  fmax_mhz: 135\n  lut4: 10000\n  coremark_iter_s: 300\n  coremark_per_mhz: 2.2\ncurrent:\n  fmax_mhz: 87.399\n  lut4: 4661\n  ff: 1104\n  coremark_iter_s: 3.0e-06\n  coremark_per_mhz: 0.0\n  source_id: hyp-20261119-003-r11s2\n  updated: '2026-11-19T21:39:56.711163Z'\n# Python\n__pycache__/\n*.pyc\n*.pyo\n.pytest_cache/\n.mypy_cache/\n\n# Toolchain (downloaded by setup.sh)\n.toolchain/\n\n# Vendored as submodule (initialized in Phase 4). No trailing slash so the\n# pattern matches both the cloned directory in the main repo AND the\n# symlink that worktree.py creates inside each worktree (otherwise git\n# status flags the symlink as untracked and sandbox check trips).\nformal/riscv-formal\n\n# Formal run output (regenerated per run; surfaced via stdout to the orchestrator).\n# Glob covers both the legacy single-file path and the PID-suffixed variants\n# emitted by run_all.sh after the concurrent-rm-race fix (formal/run_all.sh\n# writes last_run-<pid>.log so simultaneous invocations don't truncate each\n# other). Without the glob, `git status` lists the per-PID logs as untracked\n# and the scribe-phase sandbox check rolls back the scribe's commit.\nformal/last_run*.log\n\n# Orchestrator-emitted per-rep summary. Phase-2 contract output written\n# by tools/orchestrator.py:write_run_summary after every round and at\n# end of main(). Derivable from log.jsonl; not worth tracking in git.\n# Without this entry, `git status` between rounds shows it as untracked\n# (since the orchestrator never `git add`s it), and the hypothesis-phase\n# sandbox check in tools/agents/hypothesis.py rolls back the next slot's\n# turn with \"modified off-limits paths: ['.../run_summary.json']\".\n# Caught live during the gpt-5.5 effort sweep — slot 2 in round 2 of\n# every rep was hypothesis_gen_failed fo\n…[4559 of 7631 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:278366929721ed11]…\nOWIN_VERSION = \"1.9.11.03 Education\"\n35:    libs = [GOWIN_HOME / \"deps/root/usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu\", GOWIN_HOME / \"IDE/lib\"]\n128:def _run_gw_sh(outdir: Path, log: Path, env: dict) -> bool:\n133:        proc = subprocess.Popen([str(GOWIN_HOME / \"IDE/bin/gw_sh\"), \"build.tcl\"], cwd=outdir,\n158:    timed_out = _run_gw_sh(outdir, log, gowin_env(env, outdir))\ntotal 40\n-rw-rw----+ 1 nobody nogroup  2630 Nov 20 01:21 checks-deep.cfg\n-rw-rw----+ 1 nobody nogroup  2658 Nov 20 01:21 checks.cfg\n-rw-rw----+ 1 nobody nogroup  1455 Nov 20 01:21 checks_si.cfg\nlrwxrwxrwx+ 1 nobody nogroup    68 Nov 20 01:21 riscv-formal -> /srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6_2-astra_xhigh-v2-rep1/formal/riscv-formal\n-rwxrwx---+ 1 nobody nogroup 10597 Nov 20 01:21 run_all.sh\n-rw-rw----+ 1 nobody nogroup  4615 Nov 20 01:21 wrapper.sv\n-rw-rw----+ 1 nobody nogroup  2863 Nov 20 01:21 wrapper_si.sv\n.\n..\nCORE_PHILOSOPHY.md\nLESSONS.md\ncore.yaml\nexperiments\nrtl\ntest\n/srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6_2-astra_xhigh-v2-rep1/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20261120-001-r14s0\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
