{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_11", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261119-001-r10s0.yaml'", "aggregated_output": "id: hyp-20261119-001-r10s0\ntitle: Replace serial divider trials with two reciprocal quotient estimates\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The champion's placement-0 worst path runs from quotient_q to\n  remainder_q through 72 cells. At its median placement a divider\n  feedback path is within 0.001 ns of the worst fetch RAM path.\n  CoreMark executes no divides between its markers. A shorter divider\n  path can raise the clock for all 3,414,124 measured cycles. At that\n  cycle count the acceptance threshold is 87.594 MHz.\nhypothesis: |\n  Estimate an unsigned quotient twice with the same conservative\n  reciprocal, first on the dividend and then on the residual. Two\n  registered DSP products per estimate replace the pair of serial\n  radix-8 trial banks. A 2,048-word reciprocal ROM bounds the error\n  tightly enough that one final comparison gives the exact quotient\n  and remainder. Keep the eight-cycle EX handshake.\n\n  Let H = 2^32 and let A and D be the operand magnitudes. For D >= 2,\n  choose the smallest shift s such that j = (D-1) >> s fits in 11 bits.\n  Read floor(H/(j+1)) from ROM and shift the word right by s to obtain M.\n  This equals floor(H/U) for U = (j+1) << s, the upper endpoint of D's\n  bucket. Each estimate q = high32(x*M) is a lower bound on floor(x/D).\n  Apply it to x=A, subtract q0*D, then apply it to that residual and\n  subtract q1*D. If the final residual is at least D, subtract D once\n  and increment q0+q1. Apply the architectural sign to the selected result.\n\n  A scratch implementation reached 86.266, 92.151 and 92.151 MHz across\n  Gowin's three placement options. Stalled CoreMark passed all five CRCs\n  in 3,414,124 bracketed cycles. The median gives 269.91 iterations/s,\n  10.04% above the champion. The design used 15 BSRAMs and six DSPs,\n  up from 11 and two. The median placement's worst path now runs from\n  writeback to the EX/MEM ALU result. The ALU and pipeline suites and\n  directed reciprocal-boundary tests passed on the scratch RTL.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 10\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n    description: |\n      Capture A, D-1 and the sign and remainder flags on issue. D-1 is\n      ~b for a negative signed divisor and b-1 otherwise. In phase 1\n      reconstruct D, synchronously read the 2048x32 block ROM and\n      register s. Select j and s together by priority on the highest\n      set bit of D-1, defaulting to its low 11 bits and shift zero.\n      Initialize ROM constants with 64-bit arithmetic in two blocks\n      of 1024 entries. Index zero can store zero because D=1 is handled\n      explicitly. Register M in phase 2.\n\n      Use one unsigned high-product datapath for phases 3 and 5 and one\n      low-product datapath for phases 4 and 6. Register q0, A-q0*D,\n      q1, then the final residual R and sum Q=q0+q1 on successive edges.\n      Register -Q and -R alongside Q and R in phase 6. In phase 7 use\n      the borrow of a 33-bit R-D to select the signed candidates for\n      Q or Q+1 and R or R-D. Precompute -A in phase 1 for the D=1 and\n      D=0 selections. Preserve signed truncation, INT_MIN/-1, DIV by\n      zero returning all ones, and REM by zero returning rs1. Retain the\n      existing ALTOPS operations, operand capture and completion edge.\n  - file: test/test_alu.py\n    description: |\n      Compare all four DIV/REM results with an integer reference around\n      powers of two, ROM bucket endpoints and representable multiples of\n      D. Include maximum dividends, both correction outcomes, both signs,\n      and alternating consecutive requests, checking the exact done edge.\n\n      Check the one-correction bound for each ROM bucket with integer\n      arithmetic. For 2 <= D < H/2, e=H-M*D is nonnegative and one\n      estimate leaves a residual less than x*e/H+D. Two estimates\n      therefore leave R/D < 1+e*(e+D)/(H*D). The extra term decreases\n      with D inside a bucket. Assert e*(e+D) < H*D at its smallest\n      applicable D. All 22,527 applicable buckets passed this check.\n      For D >= H/2 the original A is already less than 2D.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
