{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_13", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'tail -1 cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'", "aggregated_output": "{\"id\": \"hyp-20261119-003-r9s2\", \"title\": \"Return the instruction and its predicted successor from one tagged lookup\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"The champion looks up the same fetch PC in a 256-entry BTB and a\\nseparate 512-word replay store. A BTB hit predicts a successor but\\ncannot supply a missing instruction. Conversely, a resident instruction\\ncan wait for imemReady once a miss has ended replay permission. A single\\ntagged row can supply both answers. Recording the instruction alongside\\nits target also gives EX a cheaper way to verify a direct prediction.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The champion looks up the same fetch PC in a 256-entry BTB and a\\nseparate 512-word replay store. A BTB hit predicts a successor but\\ncannot supply a missing instruction. Conversely, a resident instruction\\ncan wait for imemReady once a miss has ended replay permission. A single\\ntagged row can supply both answers. Recording the instruction alongside\\nits target also gives EX a cheaper way to verify a direct prediction.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Use a direct-mapped 1024-row predictor indexed by word PC. Each row\\nholds a valid bit, source PC tag, raw instruction, two-bit direction\\ncounter and aligned 18-bit target. Train from every valid advancing EX\\ninstruction in the low 1 MiB. A normal-PC hit supplies the saved word\\non an imem wait and steers the next fetch according to the counter.\\nA ready bus always supplies the live word. Read the same table at the\\nregistered taken-recovery PC in parallel to cover waits after a miss.\\n\\nOn a direct branch or JAL, the tagged source PC and identical instruction\\nuniquely determine the target recorded during training. Carry one bit\\nrecording word equality into EX. On a taken direct transfer, that bit\\nverifi