{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/run_summary.json cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261119-001-r2s0.yaml'","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"iterations\": 4,\n  \"accepted\": 2,\n  \"rejected\": 2,\n  \"broken\": 0,\n  \"broken_by_class\": {},\n  \"baseline_fitness\": 12.12,\n  \"final_fitness\": 96.04,\n  \"best_fitness\": 96.04,\n  \"best_round\": 3,\n  \"delta_pct\": 692.4092409240925,\n  \"best_lut4\": 2747,\n  \"best_ff\": 565,\n  \"best_fmax_mhz\": 43.135,\n  \"best_iterations\": 10,\n  \"best_cycles\": 4491485,\n  \"best_ipc_coremark\": 2e-06\n}\nid: hyp-20261119-001-r2s0\ntitle: \"Halve the divider feedback depth with radix-4 quotient digits\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The champion's worst Gowin path runs from remainder_q back to remainder_q\n  through 186 cells. Eight serial restoring steps per clock gave 31.365 MHz,\n  while six gave 43.135 MHz. Both runs used 4,491,485 timed cycles for ten\n  CoreMark iterations. The measured region executes zero divides or remainders,\n  so the divider matters to fitness through its effect on the clock period.\nhypothesis: |\n  Keep the existing issue cycle, six arithmetic rounds and result transfer.\n  In each full round, generate six quotient bits as three radix-4 digits.\n  For each digit, subtract D, 2D and 3D from the shifted partial remainder\n  in parallel. Use the borrow flags to select the largest fitting multiple\n  and its already computed difference. This cuts the feedback path from six\n  dependent carry chains to three. The leading four padding bits in the\n  current 36-bit dividend leave just two real bits for round one, so that\n  round can also prepare 3D for use in rounds two through six.\n\n  At the champion's cycle count, 52 MHz would yield about 116 iterations/s.\n  Acceptance requires just over 45.1 MHz. The main uncertainty is how much\n  of the saved carry delay Gowin spends routing the parallel differences\n  and selecting the next remainder.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 20\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n    description: |\n      In the real DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU datapath, take unsigned magnitudes on\n      issue as today. In phase 1, consume the top two dividend bits with two\n      restoring bit steps from zero and register 3D = D + (D << 1) in\n      parallel. In phases 2 through 6, consume three pairs of dividend bits\n      per clock, appending each selected two-bit digit to the quotient.\n      Widen D before forming multiples. For each pair form the 34-bit value\n      T = 4R + pair and use 35-bit zero-extended unsigned subtractions to\n      distinguish borrow for all three candidates. Select digit zero and T\n      if all borrow. Preserve RV32M sign correction, the all-ones quotient\n      and original dividend remainder for D = 0, and INT_MIN / -1 semantics.\n      Reuse the existing busy/done phases and ALTOPS behavior so the existing\n      six-round arithmetic and stalled-pipeline tests exercise the same\n      completion and forwarding contract.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
