maximum below 257. Truncating to a multiple of 64 gives floor(A/D)-64P <= 320. This bounds the correction for the tabulated range. In the zero-prefix range the correction is at most 511.\n\n  Start the first trial at the 26-bit residual high part. Each trial s\n…[1026 of 4098 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:eff746acbaed9dc1]…\nnd signed-mode flags. Read the synchronous ROM and register Z in phase 1 using fixed slices selected by the leading bit of D-1. For e<11 fill the vacated low index bits with ones when normalizing D-1. Register P in phase 2 and its residual high part in phase 3 using separate unsigned products. Precompute 35-bit divisor multiples beside the estimate. In phases 4 through 6 reuse one bank of parallel trial differences with a balanced digit and remainder selector. Register the final magnitude on phase 6. Preserve the eight-cycle handshake, reset cancellation and ALTOPS behavior. Initialize the ROM in two banks of 1,024 constants using 64-bit integer arithmetic.\n  - file: test/test_alu.py\n    description: |\n      Verify the endpoint inequality with integers. Check signed and unsigned quotient and remainder at powers of two, adjacent buckets, exact multiples, zero, signed overflow and maximal dividends. Include A=0xffffffff and D=4099, which needs a correction of 320. Retain the busy, done and input-change checks.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
