{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_13", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -i '4,136,096|4136096|121\\\\.01|mhz|critical path|fmax' .tmp/agent-logs/impl.hyp-20261119-002-r3s1.log | tail -c 5000\"", "aggregated_output": "an): 50.052 MHz\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_40\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -c 'python3 -c \\\"f=50.052e6*10/4136096; print(f, (f/109.64-1)*100, 100*355389/(355389+4136096))\\\"'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_40\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -c 'python3 -c \\\"f=50.052e6*10/4136096; print(f, (f/109.64-1)*100, 100*355389/(355389+4136096))\\\"'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"121.0126650832089 10.372733567319315 7.912505552172611\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_48\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/implementation_notes.md'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"# EX-cycle target fetch\\n\\nAn aligned taken branch, JAL or JALR drives the instruction address in EX. ID samples the selected PC and instruction together. IF records that PC as its fetch base. An increment flag selects the following word after acceptance or the same target after a stall. Back-to-back transfers can therefore retire on consecutive cycles.\\n\\nThe implementation shares one resolved target and alignment check between fetch, the misalignment trap and RVFI next-PC reporting. JALR clears bit zero before the check. A misaligned taken transfer retires with a trap, suppresses the link write and continues at PC+4.\\n\\nID/EX holds during a blocked data access or divider wait. On an advancing edge, fetch readiness and the load-use interlock determine ID/EX validity. EX masks controls from invalid entries and divider bubbles. The held WB bypass keeps branch operands available throughout a data stall.\\n\\n## Local verification\\n\\n- Verilator passed the requested lint command with zero warnings.\\n- All 53 single-retire ALTOPS formal checks passed on the final logic, with zero failures or corrective retries.\\n- All 85 cocotb cases passed. The pipeline tests cover consecutive branch and target retirements, a dependent JAL-to-JALR chain and bo\n…[1924 of 4996 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:f4cab55bb65f3a7d]…\na98cc/bench-ex-fetch/cores/bench/generated/timing/gowin_p1/impl/pnr/core_bench.tr\\nplace_option 2: Fmax 50.052 MHz, 13 logic levels; logic 3226, registers 664, LUT-RAM 8, BSRAM 6, DSP 6\\n  path 1: 25.274 ns, 13 cells, cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s -> dmem_1_dmem_1_0_0_s\\n          through: clock_ibuf > cpu/u_id > cpu/u_ex > cpu/u_ex/u_alu > cpu/u_ex\\n  full report: /srv/hwebench/tmp/800f6bc6/521a98cc/bench-ex-fetch/cores/bench/generated/timing/gowin_p2/impl/pnr/core_bench.tr\\nscore Fmax (median): 50.052 MHz\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_51\",\"type\":\"agent_message\",\"text\":\"[Implementation notes and verification results](/srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6_2-astra_xhigh-v2-rep1/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20261119-002-r3s1/cores/bench/implementation_notes.md)\\n\\n**121.01 CoreMark iterations/s (+10.37%)** from 4,136,096 bracketed cycles and 50.052 MHz median Gowin Fmax. Lint, all 53 formal checks, all 85 cocotb tests, RVFI cosimulation, and CoreMark CRC validation passed.\"}}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
