{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_14", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261119-002-r7s1.yaml'", "aggregated_output": "id: hyp-20261119-002-r7s1\ntitle: \"Add a decoded instruction replay path directly into ID/EX\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The champion reuses an issued word only after a short taken backward\n  branch. Returning to a function or re-entering code through a jump\n  can therefore leave ID idle on an instruction-bus wait. Even on a\n  replay hit, the word goes back through opcode and immediate decode.\n  Ten CoreMark iterations take 4,106,616 cycles at 80.180 MHz.\nhypothesis: |\n  Give ID/EX a second dispatch path carrying the original instruction,\n  validated decoder controls and expanded immediate from an earlier\n  issue at the same PC. Index this path on every fetch. A ready bus\n  feeds the live decoder and immediate generator directly. During a bus\n  wait, an exact hit can issue a complete decode result in that cycle,\n  including at a resolved jump target or on the fall-through of a loop.\n  Both paths read the current register file and use normal forwarding.\n\n  In a 128-entry scratch prototype, ten iterations took 3,901,903\n  bracketed cycles with all five CRCs matching, a 4.98% cycle reduction.\n  Gowin measured 77.872, 81.613 and 81.613 MHz across its three placement\n  options. The median gives 209.16 iterations/s, 7.13% above 195.25.\n  At this cycle count the 4.6% acceptance threshold requires 79.69 MHz.\n  Placement 0 used 4,991 logic cells. The main risk is routing the wide\n  replay record into ID/EX.\n\n  The prototype passed 92 cocotb cases, including replay on a second\n  subroutine call, a 512-byte tag alias and a FENCE.I that changes both\n  opcode function and immediate. Selftest and the three random programs\n  matched the reference ISS with ready buses and with both buses stalled\n  by the standard generator.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 7\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: |\n      Extend IF/ID with the live bus word, recorded ctrl_t, recorded\n      32-bit immediate and replay-source select. The existing instruction\n      field carries the selected raw word for operand tags and RVFI.\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Write instruction, ctrl_t and immediate together from valid ID/EX\n      slots to parallel 128-entry distributed RAMs with asynchronous\n      reads indexed by PC[8:2]. Use PC[8:6] to select one of eight\n      PC[31:9] tags and a 16-bit word-presence mask. On tag replacement\n      set only the written word's bit. Reset and FENCE.I clear the masks\n      with priority over fills. Drop the loop-active and tail registers.\n      On a bus wait assert fetch valid only for a matching full tag and\n      present word. The ready bus takes priority for all fields.\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: |\n      Feed registered ID/EX.ctrl and ID/EX.imm to IF alongside its existing\n      issue PC, instruction and validity. Remove the short-backward-branch\n      qualification. Keep the resolved redirect and FENCE.I synchronization\n      connected to fetch.\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Connect the decoder and immediate generator to the live bus word.\n      At the ID/EX capture edge, select the corresponding live or recorded\n      controls and immediate together. Preserve decoder legality and the\n      multiply-result mux selection in the record. Use the selected raw\n      instruction for both register addresses, load-use detection and rd.\n      Apply the existing hold, bubble and valid gating to both sources.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Exercise a second call to the same routine with imemReady low and\n      a store on the unaccepted bus. Check replay of an illegal word,\n      a multiply, a dependent load/store sequence and an indirect return\n      against RVFI order, operands, results and accepted memory writes.\n      Check a recorded loop exit and a backward displacement beyond 256\n      bytes. Use PCs 512 bytes apart to exercise actual tag replacement\n      and a same-sector absent word. Check live-bus priority and FENCE.I\n      invalidation of the complete decode result.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
