{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor l in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').open():\n d=json.loads(l)\n if 'r8s1' in l or 'r8s0' in l:\n  print({k:v for k,v in d.items() if len(str(v))<1800})\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"{'id': 'hyp-20261119-001-r8s0', 'title': 'Pack issued-word replay into address-registered block RAM', 'category': 'micro_opt', 'motivation': 'The existing 64-word replay buffer shares a tag among 16 words. Writing\\na conflicting sector can evict instructions that have different word\\nindices. A 512-row block-RAM layout can keep more of those words resident\\nduring instruction-bus waits. The existing normal and recovery PC registers\\nalready provide two read addresses in time for decode. Simply enlarging\\nthe distributed arrays to 512 words reached 64.379 MHz on Gowin placement\\noption 1. Packing the tag and word together and reading both registered\\naddresses reached 79.197 MHz on the same option.\\n', 'expected_impact': {'fitness_delta_pct': 5, 'confidence': 'medium'}, 'changes': [{'file': 'rtl/if_stage.sv', 'description': 'Infer a 512x41 block-RAM table indexed by PC[10:2]. Write PC[19:11]\\nand the 32-bit issued word together for valid issue PCs in low 1 MiB\\ninstruction RAM. Set one presence bit per row on fill and clear all\\npresence bits on reset or FENCE.I. Read at normal_pc[10:2] and\\ntarget_q[10:2], allowing RAM replication. For each port require\\npresence, a matching nine-bit tag and zero PC[31:20]. Select target\\ndata and hit on use_target, normal data and hit on ordinary fetch,\\nand use the live bus on a fall-through correction. Keep the existing\\nenables and priorities for prediction, replay permission and PC holds.\\n'}, {'file': 'test/test_pipeline.py', 'description': 'Exercise two PCs 256 bytes apart that both remain resident, then\\nreplace a row with a PC 2 KiB away. Check the displaced word waits\\nfor the bus and an adjacent word survives. In the existing conflict\\ntest, jump to PC 2108 to evict PC 60 while PC 64 stays resident.\\nCheck replay termination and restart, live-bus priority, FENCE.I,\\nordered retirement and the exact sequence of accepted stores.\\n'}], 'outcome': 'improvement', 'fitness': 233.74, 'delta_pct': 8.28, 'vs_baseline': 1828.55, 'fmax_mhz': 81.702, 'ipc_coremark': 3e-06, 'cycles': 3495417, 'iterations': 10, 'lut4': 4667, 'ff': 1392, 'seeds': [75.297, 81.702, 81.702], 'perturbations': [[0, 75.297, 14], [1, 81.702, 14], [2, 81.702, 14]], 'lutram': 32, 'bsram': 9, 'dsp': 2, 'critical_path': {'from': 'cpu/u_mem/reg_q.ctrl.mem_to_reg_s0', 'to': 'cpu/u_if/write_payload_18_s0', 'slack_ns': -8.281, 'arrival_ns': 18.575, 'logic_cells': 39, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_wb', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu']}, 'logic_levels': 14, 'formal_passed': True, 'cosim_passed': True, 'error': None, 'implementation_notes': '', 'timestamp': '2026-11-19T18:32:04.346856Z', 'slot': 0, 'round_id': 8, 'lesson': '- 2026-11-19 hyp-20261119-001-r8s0 (improvement, +8.28%): Packing each PC tag with its instruction in a 512-row block RAM limited a conflicting replay fill to one eviction, while parallel reads at the registered normal and recovery PCs kept the recovery mux off both RAM address paths.'}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
