 fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Look up the direction counter by PC, form the aligned in-range direct\n      target from raw imem_data, and drive the PC register on acceptance.\n      Use a resettable 256-bit valid bitmap and an asynchronously read,\n      synchronously wri\n…[1128 of 4200 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:a3107271a7b42072]…\n once when the older dmem operation advances.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Check consecutive retirement on warmed taken branches, loop-exit recovery\n      with a wrong-path store, and exact RVFI PC/order across an imem wait or\n      an older stalled load. Exercise aligned JAL, JALR, and misaligned direct\n      targets, including an untaken branch whose target is outside RAM.\nWrote and schema-validated the [hypothesis YAML](/srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6_2-astra_xhigh-v2-rep1/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20261119-003-r1s2-hypgen/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261119-003-r1s2.yaml). It proposes a 256-entry, two-bit fetch-stage predictor for conditional branches, with direct JAL targets computed in fetch.\n\nA temporary RTL prototype achieved **12.88 CoreMark iterations/s**, 6.29% above baseline and above the 4.6% acceptance margin. It completed ten iterations in 4,193,225 cycles at a median Gowin Fmax of 5.402 MHz. All five CoreMark CRCs matched. Formal verification remains pending.", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
