{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_12", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'tail -4 cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'", "aggregated_output": "{\"id\": \"hyp-20261119-002-r4s1\", \"title\": \"Move multiplication to MEM and forward the registered product from WB\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"A placement-1 Gowin run reproduced the champion's 57.213 MHz. Its worst\\nsetup path starts at a register-file BSRAM output, crosses the rs2 bypass\\nmuxes and the signed multiplier DSP, then crosses six LUTs to the EX/MEM\\nresult register. The next path crosses the unsigned multiplier. The timed\\nCoreMark trace has 93,960 MULs but only 35,640 are followed immediately\\nby an instruction that reads their destination.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"A placement-1 Gowin run reproduced the champion's 57.213 MHz. Its worst\\nsetup path starts at a register-file BSRAM output, crosses the rs2 bypass\\nmuxes and the signed multiplier DSP, then crosses six LUTs to the EX/MEM\\nresult register. The next path crosses the unsigned multiplier. The timed\\nCoreMark trace has 93,960 MULs but only 35,640 are followed immediately\\nby an instruction that reads their destination.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Execute all four multiply operations in the MEM slot. EX already captures\\nthe two forwarded register operands in EX/MEM. Feed these registered values\\nto one signed 33-by-33 multiplier. Select sign or zero extension of each\\noperand from the operation and select the required 32 product bits before\\nthe MEM/WB edge. This puts a register between the forwarding muxes and\\nthe DSP and removes product selection from the ordinary EX result path.\\nIndependent instructions, including independent multiplies, can still\\nissue on consecutive clocks. Treat a multiply destination like a load\\ndestination for the existing one-cycle RAW interlock. A dependent consumer\\ngets the registered product through the existing WB bypass.\\n\\nA scratch implementation completed ten stalled CoreMark iterations in\\n4,527,760 bracketed cycles, up 0.81% from 4,491,485. All five CRCs matched.\\nGowin measured 60.310, 63.007 and 63.007 MHz across its three placement\\noptions, with DSP usage falling from six to two. The med\n…[29190 of 32262 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:7a9cf9c98fe87580]…\nine.py\", \"description\": \"Use consecutive writers of distinct values to the same register,\\nfollowed by a consumer that reads it on both ports. Check youngest\\npriority and both RVFI operands. Exercise a separate WB bypass into\\na consumer held behind a stalled store, including the release cycle.\\n\"}], \"outcome\": \"improvement\", \"fitness\": 174.31, \"delta_pct\": 18.16, \"vs_baseline\": 1338.2, \"fmax_mhz\": 78.925, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4527760, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 3293, \"ff\": 708, \"seeds\": [78.911, 78.925, 78.925], \"perturbations\": [[0, 78.911, 17], [1, 78.925, 14], [2, 78.925, 14]], \"lutram\": 32, \"bsram\": 4, \"dsp\": 2, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu/quotient_q_30_s1\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu/remainder_q_0_s0\", \"slack_ns\": -7.673, \"arrival_ns\": 17.967, \"logic_cells\": 74, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 17, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-19T16:21:06.805018Z\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 5}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20261119-003-r5s2.last'","aggregated_output":"Wrote and schema-validated the [predictor hypothesis](./cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261119-003-r5s2.yaml). It gives predicted fetches and branch recovery separate PC registers, so a late branch decision only selects between two registered addresses.\n\nThe scratch prototype reached **169.49 CoreMark iterations/s**, **14.89% above the champion** and clear of the 4.6% acceptance margin. It completed ten iterations in 4,224,275 bracketed cycles at a median Gowin Fmax of 71.598 MHz.\n\nAll five canonical CRCs matched. The prototype passed 53 formal checks, 86 cocotb cases, and eight ISS trace comparisons.","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
