{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_10", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261120-001-r14s0.yaml'", "aggregated_output": "id: hyp-20261120-001-r14s0\ntitle: \"Share the MEM multiplier and finish division with an 11-bit quotient correction\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The champion takes 3,033,815 cycles for ten CoreMark iterations. It executes\n  zero DIV or REM instructions between the markers, yet divider feedback limits\n  the 87.399 MHz median placement. The acceptance threshold at this cycle\n  count is 91.42 MHz. Previous reciprocal dividers approached that clock while\n  instantiating product hardware alongside the core's MEM multiplier. During\n  a divide, EX already sends invalid slots to MEM for six consecutive rounds.\nhypothesis: |\n  Use those slots for the first three unsigned products on the architectural multiply\n  datapath. Register divider operands alongside the architectural operands in\n  EX/MEM. A registered ownership bit selects the pair at the DSP inputs.\n  This removes the radix-8 feedback banks. Give the final residual its own\n  multiply-subtract with an 11-bit multiplier input.\n\n  Let H = 2^32, A be the unsigned dividend magnitude and D the unsigned divisor\n  magnitude. For D >= 2 choose the smallest s for which j = (D-1) >> s fits\n  11 bits. Read floor(H/(j+1)) from a 2048-word synchronous ROM and shift\n  it right by s to obtain M. In rounds 3 through 6 compute q0 = high32(A*M),\n  R0 = A-low32(q0*D), q1 = high32(R0*M), and R1 = R0-low32(q1*D).\n  After two estimates, 0 <= R1 < 2D, so at most one correction is needed.\n  For each bucket with lower endpoint L below H/2, check E*(E+L) < H*L\n  with E=H-M*L. This bounds the two-estimate error throughout the bucket.\n  For D >= H/2, A itself is less than 2D.\n\n  Register Q=q0+q1 in round 5. In round 6 precompute signed candidates\n  for Q and Q+1 alongside the residual. In round 7 compare R1 against D\n  while computing R1-D, -R1 and D-R1 in parallel. The comparison, sign\n  and operation select the result on the existing transfer edge.\n\n  The older MEM instruction gets the multiplier through the divide issue\n  edge. Division products start only after it drains, with spec\n…[2158 of 5230 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:7ecef09f4872e7ef]…\nect registered unsigned multiplier operands for each occupied divider slot, consume the raw MEM product, and retain the original architectural rs1 and rs2 for DIV/REM retirement.\"\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: \"Compute architectural and division products from the common registered operands, expose the product to EX, and keep retirement, memory accesses and forwarding qualified by their original instruction controls.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Connect the MEM product back to the divider and select the shared implementation for the integrated core.\"\n  - file: test/test_alu.py\n    description: \"Exercise the reciprocal bound across ROM buckets, both residual corrections, signed edge cases and input changes after request under the existing eight-cycle protocol.\"\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: \"Check dependent MUL to DIV and DIV to MUL sequences, an older stalled load, a squashed DIV, and all four multiply modes for exact data, instruction order and single retirement.\"\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
