hake, reset cancellation and ALTOPS behavior. Initialize the ROM in two banks of 1,024 constants using 64-bit integer arithmetic.\\n'}, {'file': 'test/test_alu.py', 'description': 'Verify the endpoint inequality with integers. Check signed and unsigned quotient and remainder at powers of two, adjacent buckets, exact multiples, zero, signed overflow and maximal dividends. Include A=0xffffffff and D=4099, which needs a correction of 320. Retain the busy, done and input-change c\n…[11047 of 14119 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:9b56bb59a8929c8f]…\nand exactly one in-order retirement each.\\n'}]\noutcome regression\nfitness 289.24\ndelta_pct 0.4\nvs_baseline 2286.47\nfmax_mhz 87.749\nipc_coremark 3e-06\ncycles 3033815\niterations 10\nlut4 5400\nff 1451\nseeds [84.887, 87.749, 87.749]\nperturbations [[0, 84.887, 15], [1, 87.749, 10], [2, 87.749, 10]]\nlutram 32\nbsram 18\ndsp 2\ncritical_path {'from': 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu/quotient_q_18_s0', 'to': 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu/remainder_q_13_s0', 'slack_ns': -6.78, 'arrival_ns': 17.075, 'logic_cells': 40, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu']}\nlogic_levels 15\nformal_passed True\ncosim_passed True\nerror None\nimplementation_notes \ntimestamp 2026-11-20T01:01:37.926407Z\nslot 1\nround_id 14\nlesson - 2026-11-20 hyp-20261120-002-r14s1 (regression, +0.40%): Truncating wide divisors to 16 bits with exponent-dependent shifts kept the radix-16 quotient estimate at most one high, so one multiply-back correction sufficed, but the path from writeback through EX to fetch target selection limited median Fmax to 87.749 MHz against the 91.42 MHz target.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
