{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor r in map(json.loads,open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl')):\n if r['id'].endswith(('r7s0','r9s0','r9s1','r9s2','r2s1','r1s1')):\n  print(r['id'],r['cycles'], r['fmax_mhz'],r['seeds'],str(r['critical_path'])[:2000],r['implementation_notes'])\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"hyp-20261119-002-r1s1 4491485 43.135 [44.337, 43.135, 43.135] {'from': 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu/remainder_q_0_s0', 'to': 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu/remainder_q_0_s0', 'slack_ns': -17.555, 'arrival_ns': 27.849, 'logic_cells': 186, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu']} \nhyp-20261119-002-r2s1 4491485 49.243 [49.236, 49.243, 49.243] {'from': 'cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s0', 'to': 'cpu/u_id/reg_q.pc_7_s0', 'slack_ns': -15.311, 'arrival_ns': 25.605, 'logic_cells': 48, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_id', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_if', 'cpu/u_hazard', 'cpu/u_id']} # Two radix-8 digits per divider clock\n\nGowin measured a median of **49.243 MHz** across placements of 49.236, 49.243, and 49.243 MHz. CoreMark completed 10 iterations in 4,491,485 bracketed cycles, yielding **109.64 iterations/s**. The median exceeds the 45.12 MHz acceptance threshold.\n\nThe real divider captures operand magnitudes and sign controls at issue. Its first round consumes two bits from a zero remainder and registers 3D, 5D, and 7D. Each of the five following rounds resolves two radix-8 digits. Each digit uses seven parallel 36-bit trial subtractions and a balanced mux tree. The first round's remainder arithmetic needs only one and two bits because it starts at zero. Both comparisons use the full divisor. The result transfer occurs on the eighth EX cycle in both real and ALTOPS builds.\n\nThe ALU tests sweep all eight digit thresholds at offsets of −1, 0, and +1 in both digit positions, and include unsigned divisors up to 0xffffffff. The suite also checks operand capture, exact completion, consecutive requests, division by zero, and signed overflow.\n\nVerilator lint passed without warnings. All 81 cocotb cases passed. The local ALTOPS formal gate passed on the first run with 53 checks and zero failures. Selftest cosimulation and stalled CoreMark CRC validation passed with `NRET=1`, as declared by the core. The standalone cosimulation command initially defaulted to two RVFI channels and required that build setting.\n\nGowin reported 3,260 logic cells and 663 registers for placement 0, up from 2,747 and 565 in the baseline. The worst setup path now runs from the register file to the ID-stage PC register through execute and hazard logic.\n\nhyp-20261119-001-r7s0 4106616 83.943 [73.746, 83.943, 83.943] {'from': 'cpu/u_fwd/rs1_match_q_0_s0', 'to': 'cpu/u_if/pc_word_6_s1', 'slack_ns': -8.56, 'arrival_ns': 18.854, 'logic_cells': 39, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_if']} \nhyp-20261119-001-r9s0 3363206 80.689 [80.355, 80.689, 80.689] {'from': 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu/quotient_q_30_s1', 'to': 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu/remainder_q_0_s0', 'slack_ns': -7.445, 'arrival_ns': 17.739, 'logic_cells': 75, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu']} \nhyp-20261119-002-r9s1 3209818 78.681 [77.969, 78.681, 78.681] {'from': 'cpu/u_mem/reg_q.result_0_s0', 'to': 'cpu/u_actual_probe/words_words_0_1_s0', 'slack_ns': -7.826, 'arrival_ns': 18.12, 'logic_cells': 12, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_ex']} \nhyp-20261119-003-r9s2 3414124 83.741 [81.36, 83.741, 83.741] {'from': 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu/quotient_q_30_s1', 'to': 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu/remainder_q_0_s0', 'slack_ns': -7.291, 'arrival_ns': 17.585, 'logic_cells': 72, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu']} \n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
