{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_10", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor r in map(json.loads,open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl')):\n if r['id'].endswith(('r7s0','r9s1','r9s0')): print(r['id'],r['hypothesis'],r['changes'])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261119-001-r7s0 {'motivation': \"The champion's reported 73-cell setup path runs from remainder_q back to\\nremainder_q through two serial radix-8 digits. Ten CoreMark iterations took\\n4,106,616 bracketed cycles, and the measured kernel executes zero DIV or REM\\ninstructions. At that cycle count, a median of 83.88 MHz clears the\\nacceptance margin over 195.25 iterations/s.\\n\", 'hypothesis': \"Use the unsigned divisor magnitude to bound the work in each feedback path.\\nFor 0 < D < 2^17, a restored remainder is at most 17 bits. Keep the existing\\ntwo-bit opening round and compute two radix-8 digits per later clock with\\n20-bit trial operands. For D >= 2^17, the upper 17 dividend bits are already\\na valid remainder because their value is strictly below D. Load them in\\nthe opening round and consume the remaining 15 bits in five clocks, one\\nfull-width radix-8 digit per clock. This removes a full-width subtraction\\nand selection from the wide feedback path and shortens both carry chains\\nin the narrow path. Both schedules deliver the result on the existing edge.\\n\\nA scratch prototype passed the ALU tests, including cases around the\\ndivisor cutoff. Stalled CoreMark passed its CRC checks in 4,106,616\\nbracketed cycles. Gowin placements reached 81.444, 84.410 and 84.410 MHz,\\nyielding 205.55 iterations/s at the median, a 5.28% gain. The median\\nplacement's worst path now runs from writeback through EX to the fetch PC.\\n\", 'expected_impact': {'fitness_delta_pct': 5, 'confidence': 'medium'}, 'changes': [{'file': 'rtl/alu.sv', 'description': \"In phase 1 register the wide and zero flags and the existing odd\\nmultiples of D. Specialize the balanced radix8_digit function for\\n20-bit operands, 21-bit trial differences and a 17-bit remainder.\\nInitialize its remainder from prefix_rem. Initialize the full-width\\nremainder from dividend[31:15] and its 32-bit quotient shift register\\nfrom {dividend[14:0], 17'b0}, where dividend is the captured magnitude.\\nIn phases 2 through 6 advance both recurrences in parallel with\\nsepara\n…[14397 of 17469 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:41466b3664e0c382]…\neplay\\nstate updates during a repair. Preserve the multiply-use interlock.\\n'}, {'file': 'rtl/mem_stage.sv', 'description': 'Verify the early candidate, then select actual-address RAM data or\\nan accepted bus response for a miss. Drive RVFI with the actual raw\\nword and byte masks. Select and register the final architectural\\nwriteback value here so the WB probe starts at a register.\\n'}, {'file': 'rtl/wb_stage.sv', 'description': 'Drive register-file writes and WB forwarding from the registered result, retaining write enable, valid and x0 handling.'}, {'file': 'test/test_pipeline.py', 'description': 'After warmup, exercise each producer distance, both forwarding matches\\nat once, a nonzero displacement, and distinct addresses at one index.\\nForce a held dependent branch on a miss and check its resolved PC,\\nRVFI order and exact bus transaction count. Immediately follow\\npartial stores with signed and unsigned loads and check the raw word,\\nextended value and masks. Include misalignment and MMIO bypass.\\n'}]\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
