 with quotient all ones and the original dividend as remainder.\n      Preserve signed truncation, overflow, and the real and ALTOPS\n      request, busy and done schedule.\n  - file: test/test_alu.py\n    description: |\n      Check quotient and remainder for divisors 4095, 4096 and 4097, and\n      at representable multiples of each wide digit from 0 through 15\n      with offsets of minus one, zero and plus one. Include high-bit-set\n      operands and alternate divisor classes on consecutive requests.\n      Check the existing completion edge and signed corner cases.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
