{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nds=list(map(json.loads,open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl')))\nd=ds[-2]\nfor k,v in d.items():\n print(k,str(v)[:800] if not isinstance(v,dict) else list(v))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"id hyp-20261119-002-r10s1\ntitle Issue load and multiply consumers before their operands reach writeback\ncategory structural\nmotivation The champion spends 3,414,124 cycles on ten CoreMark iterations. Its\ndecode interlock charges an immediate consumer a cycle even when it needs\nthe missing value only for a comparison, an addition or store data. In a\nscratch run, 136,574 deferred branches were BEQ/BNE and 36,934 deferred\ninteger operations were adds. Dependent loads accounted for a further\n61,104 interlocked cycles after specializing for these frequent consumers.\n\nhypothesis ['motivation', 'hypothesis', 'expected_impact', 'changes']\nexpected_impact ['fitness_delta_pct', 'confidence']\nchanges [{'file': 'rtl/core_pkg.sv', 'description': 'Carry source tags, the available operand, both-sources-late flag and deferred branch prediction and successor information through EX/MEM.'}, {'file': 'rtl/if_stage.sv', 'description': 'Determine which sources must be ready in EX for each fetch candidate\\nalongside its rd comparisons. Accept the registered late branch\\ncorrection with oldest priority and retain its exact PC until fetched.\\n'}, {'file': 'rtl/core.sv', 'description': 'Interlock each actual early source against load, multiply and deferred\\nadd producers. Register a valid, writing aligned LW and its nonzero rd\\nmatch with the incoming rs1 under the forwarding enable. Supply WB and the raw load return to their\\nrespective consumers. Give a resolving deferred branch priority at the\\npr\noutcome improvement\nfitness 266.94\ndelta_pct 8.83\nvs_baseline 2102.48\nfmax_mhz 84.949\nipc_coremark 3e-06\ncycles 3182385\niterations 10\nlut4 4050\nff 1046\nseeds [81.467, 84.949, 84.949]\nperturbations [[0, 81.467, 16], [1, 84.949, 16], [2, 84.949, 16]]\nlutram 32\nbsram 11\ndsp 2\ncritical_path ['from', 'to', 'slack_ns', 'arrival_ns', 'logic_cells', 'modules']\nlogic_levels 16\nformal_passed True\ncosim_passed True\nerror None\nimplementation_notes \ntimestamp 2026-11-19T20:40:56.031407Z\nslot 1\nround_id 10\nlesson - 2026-11-19 hyp-20261119-002-r10s1 (improvement, +8.83%): Feeding WB results to dependent ADD/ADDI, BEQ/BNE and store-data logic in MEM avoided load-use and multiply-use bubbles, while letting the next load add a nonzero offset to a forwarded aligned LW result saved another 30,917 cycles over ten CoreMark iterations in the prototype.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
