{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_16", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor r in map(json.loads,open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl')):\n if r['id'].endswith(('r11s0','r12s1','r12s2')):\n  print(r['id'],r['motivation'],r['changes'][0])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261119-001-r11s0 The champion's median Gowin placement has a 60-cell divider feedback\npath. Its late forwarding completes ten CoreMark iterations in 3,182,385\ncycles. The marked kernel executes zero DIV or REM instructions, so the\nopportunity is clock frequency. At this cycle count 88.86 MHz clears\nthe acceptance margin. The previous reciprocal experiment used two\nserial quotient estimates and left its last correction on the EX result path.\n {'file': 'rtl/alu.sv', 'description': 'Implement the following for unsigned magnitudes A and D >= 2, with\\nH = 2^32. On issue capture A, D-1 and the sign and operation flags.\\nD-1 is ~b for a negative signed divisor and b-1 otherwise. In phase\\n1 reconstruct D and use a leading-one priority encoder on D-1 to\\nselect j = (D-1) >> s, with the smallest s for which j fits in 11\\nbits. Let K = j+1. Read a synchronous 2048x32 intercept ROM at j\\nand a 1024x14 slope ROM at its low ten bits. Use block RAM and\\n64-bit integer constants for ROM initialization.\\n\\nFor j < 1024 the intercept C is floor(H/K), the fraction f is zero\\nand scale is zero. The D=1 bypass makes ROM entry zero unused.\\nFor j >= 1024 use C=floor(4H/K), S=floor(4H/K^2) and scale=s+2.\\nLatch f=floor(4096*(K-D/2^s)) alongside the ROM read. It consists\\nof the twelve bits immediately below j in D-1, inverted, with zero\\npadding on the right when s<12. This needs only bit selection.\\n\\nIn phase 2 register P = C + ((S*f) >> 12), using the exact table\\nword directly for small j. In phase 3 register M = (P >> scale)+1.\\nDrive both input muxes of one unsigned 32x32 multiplier with\\nphase_q == 5. Feed (A,M) in phase 4 and (q,D) in phase 5.\\nRegister q = high32(A*M), then R = A - low33(q*D) in 33 bits. In\\nphase 6 select (q-1,R+D) when R[32] is set, (q+1,R-D) when R[31:0]\\nis at least D and the sign bit is clear, or (q,R) otherwise. Register\\nthe requested magnitude, then apply its sign in phase 7. Bypass D=0\\nand D=1 at the magnitude register and return the RV32M results for\\ndivide by zero and signed overflow. Prese\n…[1929 of 5001 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:eab90150c0b80218]…\n phase 7. Preserve signed remainder, signed overflow, zero\\ndivisor results, reset cancellation and the ALTOPS completion edge.\\n\"}\nhyp-20261119-003-r12s2 The champion retired 2,922,016 instructions in 3,033,815 timed cycles. At one retirement per cycle, even eliminating every bubble would gain only 3.83% at the current clock. The data-side presence RAM currently returns its bit in MEM, where it selects the load word and the pointer forwarded to a dependent load. An isolated source-prediction prototype with late squash took 3,034,455 cycles and reached 82.499 MHz median. It preserved throughput per cycle but missed the clock target. Fetching the evidence for the prediction earlier would avoid adding a pipeline flush to this path.\n {'file': 'rtl/core.sv', 'description': 'Implement the PC-indexed sector predictor, decode-stage mask snapshot, presence updates and invalidation. Register the candidate source with the data RAM read and integrate it with existing load validation, collision handling and bus retry.'}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
