{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_113","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261119-001-r13s0.yaml'","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261119-001-r13s0\ntitle: Square the reciprocal error while refining the division quotient\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The champion retires 2,922,016 instructions in 3,033,815 bracketed\n  cycles. At one retirement per cycle, eliminating every bubble could\n  gain only 3.83% at 87.399 MHz. The median placement has a path through\n  two dependent radix-8 trials. DIV and REM execute zero times inside\n  the markers, so a smaller, faster divider can improve the clock for\n  every timed instruction. The previous 7,162-word reciprocal design\n  reached 91.086 MHz, just below the 91.42 MHz acceptance threshold.\nhypothesis: |\n  Use two fixed-point Goldschmidt refinements on the quotient estimate.\n  Squaring the reciprocal error alongside the first refinement lets the\n  second refinement use the fourth-power error bound of a much smaller\n  seed table. Use unsigned magnitudes A and D and H = 2^32. For D >= 2\n  a synchronous ROM supplies M = floor(H/U), where U is the inclusive\n  upper endpoint of D's bucket. Store M at its final scale. In phase 2\n  register q0 = floor(A*M/H) and E = H-D*M. In phase 3 register\n  q1 = q0 + floor(q0*E/H) and T = floor(E*E/H) in parallel. In phase 4\n  register q2 = q1 + floor(q1*T/H). All estimates are lower bounds.\n  In phase 5 form R = A-q2*D. In phase 6 find the greatest k in 0..7\n  with k*D <= R and register the requested q2+k or R-k*D. Restore its\n  sign on the existing result-transfer cycle. Group the seed ROM by\n  divisor exponent with power-of-two bucket widths and widen the\n  buckets as D grows.\n\n  Check the bucket endpoints with integer arithmetic before emitting\n  the ROM. With f = 1-D*M/H, full-precision refinement leaves a\n  quotient error (A/D)*f^4. Accounting for all four truncations gives\n  an upper bound (H/D)*f^4 + (2+f)*(1+f*f) + 1 + 1/D. Within a bucket\n  this bound is largest at its lower endpoint. Choose widths for which\n  the bound is below 8, so the last selection always recovers the exact\n  quotient and remainder. Time the design across all three placements\n  and compare the median with 91.42 MHz at the champion's cycle count.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n    description: |\n      Replace the real divider's serial trial feedback with the\n      registered seed lookup, unsigned DSP products, estimate updates\n      and final residual correction. Schedule the estimate products on\n      one multiplier and the independent error products on a second.\n      Retain overflow bits on multiples of D. Capture sign and mode on\n      issue, bypass D=0 and D=1, and preserve reset, the eight-cycle\n      handshake, signed overflow and the ALTOPS results.\n  - file: test/test_alu.py\n    description: |\n      Check all four division operations around seed bucket boundaries\n      and immediately below, at and above exact multiples. Include\n      large unsigned values, every reachable residual correction, and\n      back-to-back sign changes using the existing latency assertions.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
