ersus 109.64 with the radix-8 divider.\n- 2026-11-19 hyp-20261119-001-r3s0 (improvement, +16.18%): Clearing only ID/EX valid on a bubble let load-use detection read the raw fetch word in parallel with EX redirect, while registering the JALR adder's sum for loads and stores bypassed the ALU result mux on the memory address path.\n- 2026-11-19 hyp-20261119-002-r3s1 (regression, +10.37%): Fetching the resolved branch or jump target in EX let a ready target enter ID/EX without a bubble, cutting CoreMark cycles by 7.91%, but the register-file path through EX to data memory limited median Fmax to 50.052 MHz and throughput to 121.01 iterations/s versus the champion's 127.38.\n- 2026-11-19 hyp-20261119-003-r3s2 (regression, +10.89%): Counting agreement with the displacement sign lets taken backward branches and untaken forward branches reinforce the same counter, so 64 entries preserved the 256-entry predictor’s roughly 7% CoreMark cycle savings, though throughput trailed the round winner at 121.58 versus 127.38 iterations/s.\n4\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
