{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_9", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"cat fpga/core_bench_si.sv && cat Makefile | rg -C 6 'timing:|gowin' && ls -a cores/bench/test\"", "aggregated_output": "// fpga/core_bench_si.sv\n//\n// FPGA Fmax wrapper for single-issue (`nret 1`) cores. Same shape as\n// core_bench.sv but instantiates `core` with only the channel-0 RVFI port\n// set — no `_1` ports. Selected by the orchestrator (via BENCH env var in\n// synth.tcl) when cores/<target>/core.yaml declares nret: 1.\n//\n// See core_bench.sv for the rationale on LFSR-driven imem, the dmem\n// model, the V2 stall generator, and why the LED observes only the\n// memory-side outputs (RVFI-only logic is pruned).\nmodule core_bench (\n  input  logic clock,\n  input  logic reset,\n  output logic led\n);\n\n  logic [31:0] lfsr;\n  always_ff @(posedge clock or posedge reset)\n    if (reset) lfsr <= 32'h1;\n    else       lfsr <= {lfsr[30:0], lfsr[31] ^ lfsr[21] ^ lfsr[1] ^ lfsr[0]};\n\n  logic [31:0] dmem [0:2047];\n  logic [31:0] dmem_rdata;\n  logic [31:0] dmem_addr;\n  logic [31:0] dmem_wdata;\n  logic [3:0]  dmem_wen;\n  logic        dmem_ren;\n\n  always_ff @(posedge clock) begin\n    if (dmem_wen[0]) dmem[dmem_addr[12:2]][7:0]   <= dmem_wdata[7:0];\n    if (dmem_wen[1]) dmem[dmem_addr[12:2]][15:8]  <= dmem_wdata[15:8];\n    if (dmem_wen[2]) dmem[dmem_addr[12:2]][23:16] <= dmem_wdata[23:16];\n    if (dmem_wen[3]) dmem[dmem_addr[12:2]][31:24] <= dmem_wdata[31:24];\n  end\n  assign dmem_rdata = dmem[dmem_addr[12:2]];\n\n  logic [31:0] imem_addr;\n  // Single-channel RVFI port set (NRET=1 contract). Connected for\n  // elaboration only; nothing observes it, so synthesis prunes it.\n  logic        rvfi_valid_0;\n  logic [63:0] rvfi_order_0;\n  logic [31:0] rvfi_insn_0, rvfi_pc_rdata_0, rvfi_pc_wdata_0;\n  logic [31:0] rvfi_rd_wdata_0, rvfi_rs1_rdata_0, rvfi_rs2_rdata_0;\n  logic [31:0] rvfi_mem_addr_0, rvfi_mem_rdata_0, rvfi_mem_wdata_0;\n  logic [4:0]  rvfi_rs1_addr_0, rvfi_rs2_addr_0, rvfi_rd_addr_0;\n  logic [3:0]  rvfi_mem_rmask_0, rvfi_mem_wmask_0;\n  logic [1:0]  rvfi_mode_0, rvfi_ixl_0;\n  logic        rvfi_trap_0, rvfi_halt_0, rvfi_intr_0;\n\n  // V2: memory-ready signals come from the same stall sequence the\n  // CoreMark simulation uses, so stall-handling logic\n…[1718 of 4790 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:4f76240e8af539ee]…\n a deployed\n  // core would not have) is pruned and does not count toward Fmax or area.\n  assign led = ^{imem_addr, dmem_addr, dmem_wdata, dmem_wen, dmem_ren, dmem_rdata};\n\nendmodule\n\tbash formal/run_all.sh formal/checks-deep.cfg\n\nbench:\n\t$(MAKE) -f bench/programs/Makefile all\n\n# FPGA timing and area come from the vendor flow, Gowin EDA\n# (tools/eval/gowin.py); V2 does not synthesize with Yosys.\nfpga: cosim-build bench/programs/coremark.elf\n\tpython3 -m tools.eval.fpga . $(TARGET)\n\ntiming:\n\tpython3 -m tools.eval.gowin $(TARGET)\n\nbench/programs/coremark.elf: bench/programs/Makefile bench/programs/crt0.S \\\n                              $(wildcard bench/programs/coremark/*.c) \\\n                              $(wildcard bench/programs/coremark/*.h) \\\n                              $(wildcard bench/programs/coremark/baremetal/*.c) \\\n                              $(wildcard bench/programs/coremark/baremetal/*.h)\n.\n..\n_helpers.py\nconftest.py\ntest_alu.py\ntest_decoder.py\ntest_imm_gen.py\ntest_pipeline.py\ntest_reg_file.py\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor d in map(json.loads,open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl')):\n if d.get('category')=='micro_opt': print(d['title'], d.get('hypothesis',{}).get('hypothesis','')[:600])\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor d in map(json.loads,open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl')):\n if d.get('category')=='micro_opt': print(d['title'], d.get('hypothesis',{}).get('hypothesis','')[:600])\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"Baseline retest for cores/bench \nCompute RV32M division eight quotient bits per cycle Share one unsigned restoring divider across DIV, DIVU, REM and REMU. Latch\nforwarded operand magnitudes on issue and compute eight quotient bits per\ncycle for four cycles. Each bit shifts in the next dividend bit and uses\nthe borrow from one trial subtraction to select the next remainder. The\npartial remainder and quotient registers break the 32-step feedback path.\nOnly a valid divide or remainder occupies EX for extra cycles. With near\nbaseline cycle count, a median Fmax above 5.70 MHz clears the 4.6% margin.\n\nHalve the divider feedback depth with radix-4 quotient digits Keep the existing issue cycle, six arithmetic rounds and result transfer.\nIn each full round, generate six quotient bits as three radix-4 digits.\nFor each digit, subtract D, 2D and 3D from the shifted partial remainder\nin parallel. Use the borrow flags to select the largest fitting multiple\nand its already computed difference. This cuts the feedback path from six\ndependent carry chains to three. The leading four padding bits in the\ncurrent 36-bit dividend leave just two real bits for round one, so that\nround can also prepare 3D for use in rounds two through six.\n\nAt the champion's cycle count,\nRemove the EX redirect from the ID/EX payload path Decode the raw instruction and compare its source fields in parallel with\nbranch resolution. Represent a discarded fetch with the ID/EX valid bit.\nLet PC, operands, immediate and decoded fields clock into ID/EX even on a\nbubble. Only a data-memory wait or an active divider wait holds this\npayload. Qualify side effects with registered validity. This removes the\nserial redirect-to-NOP-to-hazard path and the late flush of the wide\npayload without adding a cycle to taken branches or load-use replay.\n\nAt the champion's 4,491,485 bracketed cycles for ten iterations, about\n51.51 MHz clears the accept\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
