{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_50", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"s=/srv/hwebench/tmp/800f6bc6/94704985/r5micro\nrg -n 'early_tag' \\\"\"'$s/orgunit/test/test_pipeline_runner.result.xml\"\nrg '\"'FAIL|ERROR' \\\"\"'$s/orgformal.out\" | tail -5\nls -1 \"$s/formal/riscv-formal/cores/bench-Operand/checks/\"*/PASS | wc -l\ncat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261119-001-r5s0.yaml'", "aggregated_output": "18:    <testcase name=\"early_tag_priority_with_trap_and_wait\" classname=\"test_pipeline\" file=\"/srv/hwebench/tmp/800f6bc6/94704985/r5micro/orgunit/test/test_pipeline.py\" lineno=\"533\" time=\"0.0005357265472412109\" sim_time_ns=\"191.0\" ratio_time=\"356525.1731197152\" />\n52\nid: hyp-20261119-001-r5s0\ntitle: Read operands and compare forwarding tags in decode\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  At the champion's 66.794 MHz median placement, two nearly tied paths\n  start at a register-file block RAM and end at EX/MEM.alu_result and the\n  fetch PC. The RAM takes 2.260 ns from clock to data. Both paths then\n  cross operand selection in EX. In a scratch build, distributed RAM\n  alone reached 68.977 MHz. Its limiting path started at a WB destination\n  tag, so accelerating the register read also requires earlier bypass selection.\nhypothesis: |\n  Move source operand lookup to the decode side of ID/EX. Read distributed\n  RAM and compare each raw source tag with the two older destination tags\n  in parallel. On the ID/EX capture edge, latch the register-file values\n  and four nonzero tag matches. In EX, qualify the saved matches with the\n  producers' actual write controls and select each operand with a masked OR.\n  This removes both the block-RAM launch and the five-bit comparisons\n  from the EX operand path while preserving instruction latency.\n\n  A scratch prototype reached 76.538, 78.852 and 78.852 MHz across the\n  three Gowin placement options. Ten CoreMark iterations with both buses\n  stalling took 4,527,760 marker-bracketed cycles, equal to the champion,\n  with all five canonical CRCs. The median gives 174.15 iterations/s,\n  18.05% above 147.52. The acceptance threshold at this cycle count is\n  69.87 MHz. Divider feedback is now among the limiting paths.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 18\n  confidence: high\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/reg_file.sv\n    description: |\n      Mark the 32 x 32 data array with syn_ramstyle = \"distributed_ram\".\n      Reset a 32-bit written mask. On an enabled nonzero write outside\n      reset, update the word and set its written bit. On each asynchronous\n      read port, return zero for x0, then prioritize the same-cycle WB\n      bypass, then return the stored word if written or zero otherwise.\n  - file: rtl/forward_unit.sv\n    description: |\n      On each edge with stall_id low, capture two comparisons per decode\n      source. Bit 0 matches a nonzero source to ID/EX.rd and bit 1 matches\n      it to EX/MEM.rd. Hold the bits with ID/EX during dmem and divider\n      waits. In the following cycle, enable MEM bypass on bit 0 and\n      EX/MEM.ctrl.reg_write. Enable WB bypass on bit 1 and\n      MEM/WB.ctrl.reg_write only when MEM bypass is inactive. This lets\n      an older writer supply the operand if the younger match traps.\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: |\n      Wire clock, stall_id, the raw decode read addresses and both older\n      rd tags to the forwarding unit. Supply the two registered reg_write\n      controls for late qualification. Use MEM/WB.ctrl.reg_write even\n      when MEM/WB.valid clears during a dmem hold, since its payload is\n      still the bypass source for the consumer held in EX.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Form each source as the bitwise OR of three masked words. Enable\n      the EX/MEM word with select bit 0, the WB word with select bit 1,\n      and the ID/EX register-file word when both bits are zero. Use this\n      same resolved value for ALU, branch, store and RVFI operand capture.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Check both source operands when successive writers target x5 and\n      when the younger writer is a misaligned JAL to x5. Hold another\n      consumer behind a stalled store for four cycles while its WB source\n      loses valid. Check source values, destination data and retirement order.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
