{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_9", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor l in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n d=json.loads(l)\n if d['id'].endswith('r1s1') or d['id'].endswith('r2s1'):\n  print(d['hypothesis']['hypothesis'],d['implementation_notes'],d['changes'])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "Give DIV, DIVU, REM and REMU one shared, blocking divider. Capture the\nforwarded operands and their unsigned magnitudes at issue. Zero-extend\nthe dividend magnitude to 36 bits and process six bits per clock using\nsix unrolled radix-2 restoring steps. Register the partial remainder and\nquotient after each of the six rounds. A final cycle selects quotient or\nremainder, applies its sign and transfers it to EX/MEM. This gives eight\nEX cycles including issue, within the existing formal progress window.\nOther instructions retain their existing EX latency and forwarding paths.\n\nExpect the timed cycle count to stay near 4,491,485. At that count a\nmedian Fmax of 8.16 MHz gives about 18.2 iterations/s, a 50% gain.\nCompare Gowin median Fmax and marker-to-marker cycles separately. The\nmain timing risk is that a multiply or forwarding path limits the clock\nonce the full combinational division is removed.\n  [{'file': 'rtl/alu.sv', 'description': 'Replace the combinational / and % arms with a clocked divider and\\nrequest/result handshake. Each restoring step shifts in a dividend bit\\nand uses a widened trial subtraction to select the next remainder and\\nquotient bit. Preserve the dividend for REM by zero, return all ones\\nfor DIV by zero, and handle INT_MIN / -1 and its zero remainder.\\nUnder RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS carry the existing per-op substitute through\\nthe same issue, busy and completion sequence.\\n'}, {'file': 'rtl/ex_stage.sv', 'description': 'Start only a valid decoded division when the older MEM request can\\nadvance. Snapshot both forwarded source values for RVFI as well as\\narithmetic. While waiting, send empty EX/MEM entries with all\\nside-effect controls clear. On completion transfer the held instruction\\nand result exactly once through the existing EX/MEM forwarding path.\\n'}, {'file': 'rtl/hazard_unit.sv', 'description': 'Hold PC and ID/EX from division issue through the last arithmetic round.\\nLet older EX/MEM and MEM/WB entries drain. Give an older stalled memory\\nrequest priority so its address, data and enable\n…[3662 of 6734 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:ddba00189e067731]…\ne radix-8 rounds\\nin the real divider. Use 35-bit unsigned values for T and all divisor\\nmultiples, with an extra borrow bit for each trial subtraction. Form\\n3D as 2D+D, 5D as 4D+D and 7D as 8D-D. Obtain 2D, 4D and 6D by\\nwiring shifts from D and registered 3D. Use a balanced digit/result\\nselection tree. With D=0 every trial succeeds, yielding 32 ones in\\nthe quotient and the dividend magnitude in the remainder. Reuse the\\nexisting sign control for REM by zero and signed overflow, and keep\\nthe existing request, busy and done phases for real and ALTOPS builds.\\n'}, {'file': 'test/test_alu.py', 'description': 'Extend the real-divider vectors with dividends (8p+k)*D plus offsets\\n-1, 0 and +1, choosing p and D so the inputs fit in 32 bits. Sweep\\nk=0..7 to exercise adjacent digit thresholds and quotients with a\\nnonzero preceding digit. Include unsigned divisors near 0xffffffff\\nto catch truncated multiples. Retain the exact completion-cycle,\\noperand-capture, signed corner-case and back-to-back checks.\\n'}]\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
