{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_10", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor x in map(json.loads,open(\\\"cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\\\")):\n if x['id'].endswith(('r1s0','r1s1','r2s0','r2s1')): print(x['title'],x['hypothesis'])\nPY\ncat tools/eval/gowin.py | head -200\"", "aggregated_output": "Compute RV32M division eight quotient bits per cycle {'motivation': 'Gowin reports a 199.837 ns, 156-cell path through forwarding and the EX ALU.\\nThe single-cycle signed and unsigned division and remainder operators are\\nthe likely source of its depth. The canonical 2K, -O3 CoreMark ELF contains\\nfive DIVU instructions, all in main outside the measured kernel. Additional\\ndivide latency should therefore cost few, if any, of the 4,491,485 baseline\\nbracketed cycles.\\n', 'hypothesis': 'Share one unsigned restoring divider across DIV, DIVU, REM and REMU. Latch\\nforwarded operand magnitudes on issue and compute eight quotient bits per\\ncycle for four cycles. Each bit shifts in the next dividend bit and uses\\nthe borrow from one trial subtraction to select the next remainder. The\\npartial remainder and quotient registers break the 32-step feedback path.\\nOnly a valid divide or remainder occupies EX for extra cycles. With near\\nbaseline cycle count, a median Fmax above 5.70 MHz clears the 4.6% margin.\\n', 'expected_impact': {'fitness_delta_pct': 50, 'confidence': 'medium'}, 'changes': [{'file': 'rtl/alu.sv', 'description': 'Replace the four real divide/remainder operators with the four-cycle\\nmagnitude recurrence and a request/result handshake. Use a 33-bit trial\\nsubtraction. Restore quotient sign from the operand signs and remainder\\nsign from the dividend. Preserve all-ones quotient and original dividend\\nremainder for a zero divisor, and INT_MIN quotient and zero remainder\\nfor signed overflow. Run the existing ALTOPS formulas through the same\\ncapture, latency and completion controls. Keep the other ALU ops combinational.\\n'}, {'file': 'rtl/ex_stage.sv', 'description': 'Issue once from a valid DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU when the older MEM stage can\\nadvance. Capture both forwarded source values for RVFI at issue. Insert\\nan empty EX/MEM bundle while EX waits, then transfer exactly one result\\nwith the held instruction metadata via the usual EX/MEM forwarding path.\\nRetain a completed result until EX/MEM accepts it and cle\n…[17244 of 20316 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:cbf7edbc09568b4e]…\nt options; every option must fit (the flow\n    is deterministic, so a failure is a property of the design).\"\"\"\n    failed = [r for r in results if r[\"placement_failed\"]]\n    if failed:\n        return {\"placement_failed\": True,\n                \"seeds\": [r.get(\"fmax_mhz\") for r in results],\n                \"reason\": failed[0].get(\"reason\")}\n    ref = next(r for r in results if r[\"place_option\"] == PLACE_OPTIONS[0])\n    return {\n        \"placement_failed\": False,\n        \"fmax_mhz\": round(statistics.median(r[\"fmax_mhz\"] for r in results), 3),\n        \"seeds\": [r[\"fmax_mhz\"] for r in results],\n        \"perturbations\": [[r[\"place_option\"], r[\"fmax_mhz\"], r[\"levels\"]] for r in results],\n        \"lut4\": ref[\"logic\"], \"ff\": ref[\"regs\"], \"lutram\": ref[\"lutram\"],\n        \"bsram\": ref[\"bsram\"], \"dsp\": ref[\"dsp\"], \"logic_levels\": ref[\"levels\"],\n        \"critical_path\": (ref.get(\"critical_paths\") or [None])[0],\n    }\n\n\ndef main(argv=None) -> int:\n    \"\"\"`make timing TARGET=<core>`: the vendor timing the evaluator scores,\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
