{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_6", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'tail -1 cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | python -m json.tool'", "aggregated_output": "{\n    \"id\": \"hyp-20261119-003-r7s2\",\n    \"title\": \"Use branch target buffer hits to predict and replay recurring paths\",\n    \"category\": \"predictor\",\n    \"motivation\": \"Loop replay supplies words during imem waits, but every taken branch or\\njump still discards a fetch slot, even when its target word is present.\\nThe round-two target buffer saved 313,598 cycles on a core without\\nreplay. On the current champion, a scratch target predictor with the\\noriginal short-loop replay policy took 3,815,187 cycles. Letting a\\ntrained branch also start replay along its predicted successor saved\\nanother 83,953 cycles with the same predictor and stall generators.\\n\",\n    \"hypothesis\": {\n        \"motivation\": \"Loop replay supplies words during imem waits, but every taken branch or\\njump still discards a fetch slot, even when its target word is present.\\nThe round-two target buffer saved 313,598 cycles on a core without\\nreplay. On the current champion, a scratch target predictor with the\\noriginal short-loop replay policy took 3,815,187 cycles. Letting a\\ntrained branch also start replay along its predicted successor saved\\nanother 83,953 cycles with the same predictor and stall generators.\\n\",\n        \"hypothesis\": \"Read a tagged 256-entry branch target buffer (BTB) at the registered\\nfetch PC, in parallel with the bus and the existing 64-word replay\\nstore. A hit predicts the cached target or PC+4 using a two-bit\\nsaturating counter. Accepting either prediction enables replay at the\\nsuccessor. Continue along resident words until an accepted word misses\\nthe replay store or EX corrects the path. A fresh BTB hit can start\\nanother run. On each fetch the live bus has priority, and replay on a\\nbus wait requires both the full sector tag and that word's presence bit.\\n\\nTrain legal conditional branches in both directions, and remember the\\nlast aligned target of JAL and JALR. Preserve the champion's replay\\non a cold short backedge. In EX check the saved prediction against\\nthe full resolved successor. Register the taken target \n…[7974 of 11046 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:de29c775e3f3ed39]…\n   1,\n            80.546,\n            17\n        ],\n        [\n            2,\n            80.546,\n            17\n        ]\n    ],\n    \"lutram\": 76,\n    \"bsram\": 5,\n    \"dsp\": 2,\n    \"critical_path\": {\n        \"from\": \"cpu/u_fwd/rs1_match_q_0_s0\",\n        \"to\": \"cpu/u_if/use_target_s1\",\n        \"slack_ns\": -9.287,\n        \"arrival_ns\": 19.581,\n        \"logic_cells\": 19,\n        \"modules\": [\n            \"clock_ibuf\",\n            \"cpu/u_ex\",\n            \"cpu/u_if\"\n        ]\n    },\n    \"logic_levels\": 14,\n    \"formal_passed\": true,\n    \"cosim_passed\": true,\n    \"error\": null,\n    \"implementation_notes\": \"\",\n    \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-19T17:46:27.422993Z\",\n    \"slot\": 2,\n    \"round_id\": 7,\n    \"lesson\": \"- 2026-11-19 hyp-20261119-003-r7s2 (improvement, +10.56%): Starting replay at the target or fall-through predicted by a BTB hit let fetch serve resident words during instruction-bus waits, saving 83,953 cycles across ten CoreMark iterations versus the same predictor with replay triggered only by short backedges.\"\n}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
