{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_42","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor s in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n d=json.loads(s)\n if d['id'].endswith('r6s0'): print(d['hypothesis'])\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_42", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor s in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n d=json.loads(s)\n if d['id'].endswith('r6s0'): print(d['hypothesis'])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "{'motivation': 'A load-use interlock, data-memory wait or busy divider can hold decode\\nwhile the instruction bus presents a ready word. The champion keeps\\nthe fetch PC on that word and retries it. Capturing the ready response\\nlets fetch move one word ahead and lets decode use the saved word even\\nif instruction memory stalls on the release cycle.\\n', 'hypothesis': 'Add one fall-through buffer for an instruction and its PC in IF. With\\nthe buffer empty, decode sees the bus directly. A backend hold captures\\none ready word into the buffer. When decode resumes, it consumes the\\nbuffered word and a ready bus response can refill the slot on the same\\nedge. Reset and EX redirect discard the buffered word. Limit lookahead\\nto the current 4 KiB page. Issue FENCE.I directly and accept its\\nsuccessor after it leaves EX, so an older store can finish first.\\n\\nA scratch prototype ran ten stalled CoreMark iterations in 4,375,771\\nbracketed cycles, down from 4,527,760, and passed the five CRC checks.\\nGowin placements 0, 1 and 2 reached 79.247, 80.896 and 80.896 MHz.\\nThe median gives 184.87 iterations/s, 6.06% above 174.31. At this\\ncycle count the implementation needs more than 79.783 MHz to clear\\nthe acceptance margin. Placement 0 used 3,373 logic cells and 774\\nregisters, up from 3,293 and 708. All 90 cocotb cases and all 53\\nsingle-retire ALTOPS formal checks passed. Selftest and three random traces\\nmatched the ISS with ready buses and with both buses stalling.\\n', 'expected_impact': {'fitness_delta_pct': 6, 'confidence': 'high'}, 'changes': [{'file': 'rtl/if_stage.sv', 'description': \"Keep the bus PC register. Add a full bit, a saved PC and a saved\\ninstruction. Drive decode from the saved pair when full and from\\nthe bus otherwise. Define ready = imem_ready && !fence_wait.\\nDecode valid is full || ready. A raw bus word is eligible for\\nbuffering when pc[11:2] differs from 10'h3ff and the word is\\nnot FENCE.I (opcode 0x0f, funct3 1).\\n\\nTake a ready word on a direct issue (!stall && !full), or when\\nit is eligible and (!stall || !full). On a take, capture the\\nbus PC and word and advance the bus PC by four. Hold a full slot\\nwhile stalled. Otherwise set full to ready && eligible && (full || stall).\\nOn an unstalled edge set fence_wait to !full && ready && raw_fence_i.\\nHold fence_wait during a backend stall. Reset and EX redirect take\\npriority, clear both flags and install the reset vector or target PC.\\n\"}, {'file': 'rtl/hazard_unit.sv', 'description': 'Drive stall_if from load_use_hazard, dmem_stall and div_wait.\\nLet IF handle instruction-bus readiness locally so a buffered\\ninstruction can advance while the bus waits. Retain the ID/EX\\nbubble for a load or multiply dependency and for an EX redirect.\\n'}, {'file': 'rtl/core.sv', 'description': 'Remove the instruction-ready input connection to the hazard unit.\\nKeep io_imemReady connected to IF. Feed decode and its source-tag\\ncomparisons from the selected IF output so the interlock follows\\nthe oldest fetched instruction.\\n'}, {'file': 'test/test_pipeline.py', 'description': 'Update the two fetch-address expectations affected by reading one\\nword ahead. During wb_forward_behind_stalled_store the four store\\nobservations have fetch addresses 16, 20, 20, 20. During the four\\nwaits in multiply_forwarding_with_bus_stalls the fetch address is\\n44. Continue checking the exact data requests and retirement gaps.\\nHold a dependent instruction behind LW with fetch ready, then\\ndeassert imemReady at the following PC. Check the saved instruction\\nretires once with the loaded value. Exercise simultaneous drain and\\nrefill, then redirect while the slot contains a wrong-path store.\\nCheck a load-use interlock on the last word of a page and a stalled\\nstore that modifies the instruction after FENCE.I. Check ordered\\nPCs, register data and accepted writes.\\n'}]}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
