end\n\t\t\tif (trig) begin\n\t\t\t\tassume(rvfi_valid[`RISCV_FORMAL_CHANNEL_IDX]);\n\t\t\t\tassume(!rvfi_halt[`RISCV_FORMAL_CHANNEL_IDX]);\n\t\t\t\tassume(insn_order == rvfi_order[64*`RISCV_FORMAL_CHANNEL_IDX +: 64]);\n\t\t\tend\n\t\t\tif (check) begin\n\t\t\t\tassert(found_next_insn);\n\t\t\tend\n\t\tend\n\tend\nendmodule\n\nasync def _check(dut, op, a, b, expected):\n    \"\"\"Drive op/a/b and check the combinational result.\"\"\"\n    dut.op.value = op\n    dut.a.value  = a & MASK32\n    dut.b.value  = b & MASK32\n    await Timer(1, \"ns\")\n    actual = int(dut.out.value) & MASK32\n    assert actual == (expected & MASK32), (\n        f\"op={op} a=0x{a & MASK32:08x} b=0x{b & MASK32:08x} \"\n        f\"expected=0x{expected & MASK32:08x} got=0x{actual:08x}\"\n    )\n\n\nasync def _check_div(du\n…[2465 of 5537 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:ad8f812104057df4]…\ntions. All five CRCs\nmatched. Division can therefore take extra cycles with no direct stall\ncost in the scored loop.\n Give DIV, DIVU, REM and REMU one shared, blocking divider. Capture the\nforwarded operands and their unsigned magnitudes at issue. Zero-extend\nthe dividend magnitude to 36 bits and process six bits per clock using\nsix unrolled radix-2 restoring steps. Register the partial remainder and\nquotient after each of the six rounds. A final cycle selects quotient or\nremainder, applies its sign and transfers it to EX/MEM. This gives eight\nEX cycles including issue, within the existing formal progress window.\nOther instructions retain their existing EX latency and forwarding paths.\n\nExpect the timed cycle count to stay near 4,491,485. At that count a\nmedian Fmax of 8.16 MHz gives about 18.2 iterations/s, a 50% gain.\nCompare Gowin median Fmax and marker-to-marker cycles separately. The\nmain timing risk is that a multiply or forwarding path limits the clock\nonce the full combinational division is removed.\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
