{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_132", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261119-001-r9s0.yaml')\np.write_text(\\\"\\\"\\\"id: hyp-20261119-001-r9s0\ntitle: Register load-to-branch equality alongside load writeback\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  In ten bracketed CoreMark iterations, 134,571 cycles interlocked a load\n  followed by a dependent BEQ or BNE. Both instructions need only one bit\n  of comparison result for control flow. A scratch implementation captured\n  that bit at load completion and trained the BTB on the actual outcome.\n  It took 3,363,206 cycles with both buses stalling and all five CRCs\n  correct, down from 3,495,417. At that count the acceptance threshold\n  requires a median clock above 82.23 MHz.\nhypothesis: |\n  Issue a dependent BEQ or BNE directly behind its load. While the load is\n  in MEM and the branch is in EX, compare the returned value with the\n  branch's other forwarded operand. Capture equality, the saved prediction\n  and the recovery information on the edge that accepts the load. Resolve\n  this one dependency from registers in the following cycle. A correct\n  prediction lets the younger instruction continue. A wrong prediction\n  squashes it before it can issue a request or change architectural state.\n\n  For the timing implementation, compare candidate byte and halfword lanes\n  in parallel with lane selection. Check the other operand's upper bits\n  against the required sign or zero extension. Compute the target-match\n  and alignment checks in EX and register both correction addresses.\n  This puts a register between the memory comparison and fetch recovery.\n  A direct combinational equality bypass took 3,360,915 cycles but reached\n  only 67.198 MHz on placement option 1. The clock path through recovery\n  is the main risk to the projected gain.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: |\n      Exempt only a valid load followed by BEQ or BNE from the load-use\n      interlock. Wire the MEM load comparison to EX and give an older\n      registered correction priority over younger redirects, divider issue,\n      FENCE.I, predictor training and instruction replay fills. Arbitrate\n      BTB training using the branch's saved PC, counter and actual outcome.\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Compare the raw returned lanes against the forwarded comparison operand.\n      Select equality using the load width, byte offset and extension mode.\n      Qualify the bypass with an aligned load writing a nonzero rd. For RVFI\n      substitute the accepted extended load value on each matching branch\n      source and report the branch's resolved successor and trap status.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Recognize either source dependency and handle both sources matching\n      the same load as equal. A trapped load supplies neither source. Use\n      normal older forwarding for the unaffected operand or a trapped producer.\n      Hold the pair through dmem waits. Latch equality, funct3 polarity,\n      alignment, target-match and predicted direction as the pair advances.\n      Suppress side effects of a younger instruction on a late correction\n      by clearing its validity and side-effect controls at the stage boundary.\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: |\n      Carry the deferred-comparison valid bit, source-hit flags, comparison\n      and prediction metadata with the branch through EX/MEM. Reuse the\n      existing branch target and PC fields for recovery and retirement.\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Capture target and fall-through in parallel for the deferred branch.\n      A registered mismatch selects the proper saved address with priority\n      over younger fetch decisions. Hold it through an instruction-bus wait.\n      Accept separate BTB training PC and target for the resolved branch.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Check consecutive retirement for correctly predicted load-to-BEQ/BNE\n      pairs across byte lanes, signed halfwords and words. Exercise either\n      or both sources matching, a newer trapped load shadowing an older\n      writer, changing unaccepted dmem data, and both misprediction directions.\n      Check the RVFI operands, next PC, order, misaligned taken-target trap\n      and that a squashed store or divide has no effect.\n\\\"\\\"\\\")\nPY\npython - <<'PY'\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema,pathlib\np=pathlib.Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261119-001-r9s0.yaml')\nh=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text()); jsonschema.validate(h,json.load(open('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json')))\nassert h['id']==p.stem and all((p.parents[2]/f['file']).is_file() for f in h['changes'])\nprint(233.74*1.046*3363206/1e7, 'MHz required')\nPY\ngit status --short\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
