{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_135","type":"agent_message","text":"Wrote and schema-validated [hyp-20261119-001-r9s0.yaml](cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261119-001-r9s0.yaml).\n\nThe proposal registers load-to-branch equality so a dependent BEQ or BNE can issue immediately behind its load. A scratch prototype reduced ten-iteration CoreMark cycles by **3.78%**, from 3,495,417 to 3,363,206, and matched all five CRCs.\n\nAt that cycle count, acceptance requires a median Fmax above **82.23 MHz**. Timing for the proposed lane-parallel comparison remains unverified, so the projected **5% fitness gain** carries low confidence."}}
