{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_10", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json,pprint\nfor l in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n r=json.loads(l)\n if r['id'].endswith(('r9s1','r7s0','r9s2','r8s0','r9s0','r4s1')):\n  print(r['id'])\n  for k in ['motivation','hypothesis','critical_path','logic_levels','seeds','perturbations','cycles','ipc_coremark']: print(k,r.get(k))\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261119-002-r4s1\nmotivation A placement-1 Gowin run reproduced the champion's 57.213 MHz. Its worst\nsetup path starts at a register-file BSRAM output, crosses the rs2 bypass\nmuxes and the signed multiplier DSP, then crosses six LUTs to the EX/MEM\nresult register. The next path crosses the unsigned multiplier. The timed\nCoreMark trace has 93,960 MULs but only 35,640 are followed immediately\nby an instruction that reads their destination.\n\nhypothesis {'motivation': \"A placement-1 Gowin run reproduced the champion's 57.213 MHz. Its worst\\nsetup path starts at a register-file BSRAM output, crosses the rs2 bypass\\nmuxes and the signed multiplier DSP, then crosses six LUTs to the EX/MEM\\nresult register. The next path crosses the unsigned multiplier. The timed\\nCoreMark trace has 93,960 MULs but only 35,640 are followed immediately\\nby an instruction that reads their destination.\\n\", 'hypothesis': 'Execute all four multiply operations in the MEM slot. EX already captures\\nthe two forwarded register operands in EX/MEM. Feed these registered values\\nto one signed 33-by-33 multiplier. Select sign or zero extension of each\\noperand from the operation and select the required 32 product bits before\\nthe MEM/WB edge. This puts a register between the forwarding muxes and\\nthe DSP and removes product selection from the ordinary EX result path.\\nIndependent instructions, including independent multiplies, can still\\nissue on consecutive clocks. Treat a multiply destination like a load\\ndestination for the existing one-cycle RAW interlock. A dependent consumer\\ngets the registered product through the existing WB bypass.\\n\\nA scratch implementation completed ten stalled CoreMark iterations in\\n4,527,760 bracketed cycles, up 0.81% from 4,491,485. All five CRCs matched.\\nGowin measured 60.310, 63.007 and 63.007 MHz across its three placement\\noptions, with DSP usage falling from six to two. The median gives 139.16\\niterations/s, 9.25% above 127.38. At the measured cycle count, 60.33 MHz\\nclears the 4.6% margin. The limiting path\n…[25135 of 28207 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:30cd4af4d6190190]…\nnd both registered MEM/WB\\nresult candidates to the JALR target check. Retain correction and FENCE.I squashes\\nacross older data-memory waits.\\n'}, {'file': 'test/test_pipeline.py', 'description': 'Warm the table before testing learned words. Withhold imem on a\\nsequential resident word after a cold incoming jump. Exercise a\\nsame-row alias 4 KiB away, a ready bus replacing a trained JAL with\\nanother JAL to a different target, changed and misaligned JALRs,\\na corrected target held behind a store, and a patch across FENCE.I.\\nCheck instruction bits, links, RVFI order and each accepted store.\\nDuring the sweep check that cold bus fetch and retirement progress.\\n'}]}\ncritical_path {'from': 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu/quotient_q_30_s1', 'to': 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu/remainder_q_0_s0', 'slack_ns': -7.291, 'arrival_ns': 17.585, 'logic_cells': 72, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu']}\nlogic_levels 16\nseeds [81.36, 83.741, 83.741]\nperturbations [[0, 81.36, 16], [1, 83.741, 10], [2, 83.741, 10]]\ncycles 3414124\nipc_coremark 3e-06\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
