{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_6", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor line in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n d=json.loads(line)\n if any(x in d[\\\"id\\\"] for x in ['-r10s','-r7s0','-r9s1']):\n  print(d.keys() if '-r10s0' in d['id'] else '',d['id'])\n  for k in d:\n   if k in ('implementation_notes','motivation','hypothesis','result','timing','metrics','fitness'):\n    print(k,str(d[k])[:5800])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": " hyp-20261119-001-r7s0\nmotivation The champion's reported 73-cell setup path runs from remainder_q back to\nremainder_q through two serial radix-8 digits. Ten CoreMark iterations took\n4,106,616 bracketed cycles, and the measured kernel executes zero DIV or REM\ninstructions. At that cycle count, a median of 83.88 MHz clears the\nacceptance margin over 195.25 iterations/s.\n\nhypothesis {'motivation': \"The champion's reported 73-cell setup path runs from remainder_q back to\\nremainder_q through two serial radix-8 digits. Ten CoreMark iterations took\\n4,106,616 bracketed cycles, and the measured kernel executes zero DIV or REM\\ninstructions. At that cycle count, a median of 83.88 MHz clears the\\nacceptance margin over 195.25 iterations/s.\\n\", 'hypothesis': \"Use the unsigned divisor magnitude to bound the work in each feedback path.\\nFor 0 < D < 2^17, a restored remainder is at most 17 bits. Keep the existing\\ntwo-bit opening round and compute two radix-8 digits per later clock with\\n20-bit trial operands. For D >= 2^17, the upper 17 dividend bits are already\\na valid remainder because their value is strictly below D. Load them in\\nthe opening round and consume the remaining 15 bits in five clocks, one\\nfull-width radix-8 digit per clock. This removes a full-width subtraction\\nand selection from the wide feedback path and shortens both carry chains\\nin the narrow path. Both schedules deliver the result on the existing edge.\\n\\nA scratch prototype passed the ALU tests, including cases around the\\ndivisor cutoff. Stalled CoreMark passed its CRC checks in 4,106,616\\nbracketed cycles. Gowin placements reached 81.444, 84.410 and 84.410 MHz,\\nyielding 205.55 iterations/s at the median, a 5.28% gain. The median\\nplacement's worst path now runs from writeback through EX to the fetch PC.\\n\", 'expected_impact': {'fitness_delta_pct': 5, 'confidence': 'medium'}, 'changes': [{'file': 'rtl/alu.sv', 'description': \"In phase 1 register the wide and zero flags and the existing odd\\nmultiples of D. Specialize the balanced radix8_digit fun\n…[21217 of 24289 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:b37cb268e611de46]…\nterlock on a failed check\\nin MEM if either operand depends on it. Hold the consumer through\\nbus waits and the edge retiring the missed load. Preserve the\\nmultiply-use bubble and give older memory operations priority.\\n'}, {'file': 'rtl/forward_unit.sv', 'description': 'On the repair edge recode each held EX/MEM source match to select\\nthe just-arriving MEM/WB load value. Release the other source to\\nits saved operand. Handle both sources matching the same load.\\n'}, {'file': 'test/test_pipeline.py', 'description': 'Check consecutive retirements on a warmed load-to-load-to-branch\\nchain. Force an XOR carry miss, a full-tag alias, a held partial\\nstore, signed subwords, MMIO and a trapped producer. Check that a\\nwrong pointer cannot issue a store, redirect or start a divide.\\nIn the existing stalled-store replay loop check load-use gaps of\\n[2, 1, 2] for the cold, successful and colliding reads. Keep\\nits register, retirement and exact store-transaction assertions.\\n'}]}\nfitness 262.63\nimplementation_notes \n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
