{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_27", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json\nfor l in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n r=json.loads(l)\n if r['id'].endswith('r10s0') or r['id'].endswith('r11s0'):\n  print(r['id'],r['hypothesis']['changes'])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261119-001-r10s0 [{'file': 'rtl/alu.sv', 'description': 'Capture A, D-1 and the sign and remainder flags on issue. D-1 is\\n~b for a negative signed divisor and b-1 otherwise. In phase 1\\nreconstruct D, synchronously read the 2048x32 block ROM and\\nregister s. Select j and s together by priority on the highest\\nset bit of D-1, defaulting to its low 11 bits and shift zero.\\nInitialize ROM constants with 64-bit arithmetic in two blocks\\nof 1024 entries. Index zero can store zero because D=1 is handled\\nexplicitly. Register M in phase 2.\\n\\nUse one unsigned high-product datapath for phases 3 and 5 and one\\nlow-product datapath for phases 4 and 6. Register q0, A-q0*D,\\nq1, then the final residual R and sum Q=q0+q1 on successive edges.\\nRegister -Q and -R alongside Q and R in phase 6. In phase 7 use\\nthe borrow of a 33-bit R-D to select the signed candidates for\\nQ or Q+1 and R or R-D. Precompute -A in phase 1 for the D=1 and\\nD=0 selections. Preserve signed truncation, INT_MIN/-1, DIV by\\nzero returning all ones, and REM by zero returning rs1. Retain the\\nexisting ALTOPS operations, operand capture and completion edge.\\n'}, {'file': 'test/test_alu.py', 'description': 'Compare all four DIV/REM results with an integer reference around\\npowers of two, ROM bucket endpoints and representable multiples of\\nD. Include maximum dividends, both correction outcomes, both signs,\\nand alternating consecutive requests, checking the exact done edge.\\n\\nCheck the one-correction bound for each ROM bucket with integer\\narithmetic. For 2 <= D < H/2, e=H-M*D is nonnegative and one\\nestimate leaves a residual less than x*e/H+D. Two estimates\\ntherefore leave R/D < 1+e*(e+D)/(H*D). The extra term decreases\\nwith D inside a bucket. Assert e*(e+D) < H*D at its smallest\\napplicable D. All 22,527 applicable buckets passed this check.\\nFor D >= H/2 the original A is already less than 2D.\\n'}]\nhyp-20261119-001-r11s0 [{'file': 'rtl/alu.sv', 'description': 'Implement the following for unsigned magnitudes A and D >= 2, with\\nH = 2^32. On issue capture A, D-1 and the sign and operation flags.\\nD-1 is ~b for a negative signed divisor and b-1 otherwise. In phase\\n1 reconstruct D and use a leading-one priority encoder on D-1 to\\nselect j = (D-1) >> s, with the smallest s for which j fits in 11\\nbits. Let K = j+1. Read a synchronous 2048x32 intercept ROM at j\\nand a 1024x14 slope ROM at its low ten bits. Use block RAM and\\n64-bit integer constants for ROM initialization.\\n\\nFor j < 1024 the intercept C is floor(H/K), the fraction f is zero\\nand scale is zero. The D=1 bypass makes ROM entry zero unused.\\nFor j >= 1024 use C=floor(4H/K), S=floor(4H/K^2) and scale=s+2.\\nLatch f=floor(4096*(K-D/2^s)) alongside the ROM read. It consists\\nof the twelve bits immediately below j in D-1, inverted, with zero\\npadding on the right when s<12. This needs only bit selection.\\n\\nIn phase 2 register P = C + ((S*f) >> 12), using the exact table\\nword directly for small j. In phase 3 register M = (P >> scale)+1.\\nDrive both input muxes of one unsigned 32x32 multiplier with\\nphase_q == 5. Feed (A,M) in phase 4 and (q,D) in phase 5.\\nRegister q = high32(A*M), then R = A - low33(q*D) in 33 bits. In\\nphase 6 select (q-1,R+D) when R[32] is set, (q+1,R-D) when R[31:0]\\nis at least D and the sign bit is clear, or (q,R) otherwise. Register\\nthe requested magnitude, then apply its sign in phase 7. Bypass D=0\\nand D=1 at the magnitude register and return the RV32M results for\\ndivide by zero and signed overflow. Preserve the ALTOPS branch and\\nthe request, busy and done edges.\\n'}, {'file': 'test/test_alu.py', 'description': 'Check all four operations against integer division around reciprocal\\nbucket boundaries, powers of two and the largest representable\\nmultiples of D. Include unsigned (A,D) pairs (0xffffffff,2),\\n(0xfffffffe,2) and (0xffffffff,2049) for downward, zero and upward\\nquotient corrections respectively. Exercise alternating signed\\nrequests with changing live operands and check the existing done edge.\\n'}]\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
