{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_96","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261119-002-r12s1.yaml'","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261119-002-r12s1\ntitle: Divide in two halfword steps with a shared short reciprocal\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The champion takes 3,033,815 cycles for ten CoreMark iterations. Gowin\n  placement 0 reports an EX-to-fetch path, but placement 1, which supplies\n  the scored 87.399 MHz median, runs through both serial radix-8 trial\n  subtractors in the divider. CoreMark executes no DIV or REM inside the\n  markers. At this cycle count a median above 91.422 MHz clears acceptance.\nhypothesis: |\n  Compute the unsigned quotient in base 65536. Use an underestimating\n  reciprocal with about 18 significant bits for both quotient digits.\n  Estimate the high digit from the upper half of the dividend. Subtract\n  its product with the divisor from that half and append the low 16 bits.\n  Estimate the low digit from this remainder. A high digit one too small\n  is harmless if the low digit can exceed 65535 and its carry goes into\n  the high digit. This removes the intermediate correction from the\n  feedback loop and permits the two steps to share a DSP product path.\n\n  Use directed integer rounding for the reciprocal and certify a relative\n  shortfall below 2^-17. The high prefix quotient is below 65536, so its\n  estimate is at most one low. The second quotient is below 131072, so\n  it too is at most one low. One final comparison and subtraction of D\n  gives an exact quotient and remainder. Measure the three Gowin placements\n  at the champion's cycle count. Forwarding and memory backpressure can\n  become the clock limit after removing the divider recurrence.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n    description: |\n      Keep the request capture and phase-7 transfer. For nonzero magnitude D,\n      normalize D and retain its exponent. In phase 1 read a block ROM of\n      reciprocal intercepts and slopes, and in phase 2 form a conservative\n      fixed-point reciprocal by linear interpolation. In phases 3 and 5\n      use high-product plus exponent shift for the two estimates. In phases\n      4 and 6 multiply each estimate back by D and subtract. Keep 17 bits\n      of low digit, add the two digit contributions, and perform the final\n      unit correction and sign restoration on transfer. Preserve divide by\n      zero, INT_MIN/-1, reset cancellation and ALTOPS on the same edges.\n  - file: test/test_alu.py\n    description: |\n      Check the reciprocal error at both ends of each constant-coefficient,\n      constant-output interval with integer inequalities. Exercise a high\n      digit underestimate that makes the low digit carry, both final\n      correction outcomes, exact multiples and neighboring dividends for\n      all four operations. Retain the existing busy and completion checks.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
