{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_109","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'tail -4 \"$TMPDIR/structural_r12/bank/timing/gowin_p1/gw.log\" && tail -2 \"$TMPDIR/structural_r12/bank/tests.log\" && cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261119-002-r12s1.yaml | head -35'","aggregated_output":"Running placement......\n[10%] Placement Phase 0 completed\n[20%] Placement Phase 1 completed\n[30%] Placement Phase 2 completed\n..                                                                       [100%]\n2 passed in 10.35s\nid: hyp-20261119-002-r12s1\ntitle: Estimate the quotient with one DSP and finish division with a radix-8 correction\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The champion runs ten CoreMark iterations in 3,033,815 bracketed cycles.\n  Placement 0 reports a branch-recovery path, but the scored 87.399 MHz\n  median placement is limited by the two serial radix-8 divider stages.\n  CoreMark executes no divisions inside the timing markers. At this cycle\n  count acceptance requires more than 91.4185 MHz.\nhypothesis: |\n  Replace the five rounds of quotient-digit feedback with a feed-forward\n  divider. A ROM interpolates a lower bound M on 2^32/D directly in the\n  units consumed by a 32x32 multiplier. Use the same DSP datapath twice,\n  first for q = high32(A*M), then for the product q*D. Register R = A-q*D.\n  In the last arithmetic round select the greatest k in 0..7 for which\n  k*D <= R. The exact unsigned quotient is q+k and the remainder is R-k*D.\n  Adjust the sign on the existing result-transfer cycle.\n\n  Vary the ROM bucket width with divisor magnitude so its output needs no\n  variable shift. Across 261,374 constant-output intervals covering every\n  D from 2 to 0xffffffff, integer endpoint checks gave\n  0 <= 2^32/D-M <= 20568/4417, below five. Since A < 2^32, the correction\n  fits in one radix-8 digit even after quotient truncation. This leaves\n  room for inexpensive interpolation and lets operand capture occur before\n  magnitude conversion, away from the main forwarding path.\n\n  A scratch prototype passed the existing ALU and pipeline suites and all\n  five stalled CoreMark CRCs in 3,033,815 bracketed cycles. Placement 1\n  reached 91.067 MHz, equivalent to 300.17 iterations/s. This is close\n  to the 301.33 iterations/s acceptance threshold.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
