{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_11", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor d in map(json.loads,open(\\\"cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\\\")):\n if d['id'].endswith('r10s0') or d['id'].endswith('r7s0'):\n  print(d['hypothesis']['hypothesis'], d['changes'])\nPY\ncat test/cosim/build.sh; cat cores/bench/test/conftest.py; cat tools/eval/_slots.py | head -140; ls -la /tmp | head\"", "aggregated_output": "Use the unsigned divisor magnitude to bound the work in each feedback path.\nFor 0 < D < 2^17, a restored remainder is at most 17 bits. Keep the existing\ntwo-bit opening round and compute two radix-8 digits per later clock with\n20-bit trial operands. For D >= 2^17, the upper 17 dividend bits are already\na valid remainder because their value is strictly below D. Load them in\nthe opening round and consume the remaining 15 bits in five clocks, one\nfull-width radix-8 digit per clock. This removes a full-width subtraction\nand selection from the wide feedback path and shortens both carry chains\nin the narrow path. Both schedules deliver the result on the existing edge.\n\nA scratch prototype passed the ALU tests, including cases around the\ndivisor cutoff. Stalled CoreMark passed its CRC checks in 4,106,616\nbracketed cycles. Gowin placements reached 81.444, 84.410 and 84.410 MHz,\nyielding 205.55 iterations/s at the median, a 5.28% gain. The median\nplacement's worst path now runs from writeback through EX to the fetch PC.\n [{'file': 'rtl/alu.sv', 'description': \"In phase 1 register the wide and zero flags and the existing odd\\nmultiples of D. Specialize the balanced radix8_digit function for\\n20-bit operands, 21-bit trial differences and a 17-bit remainder.\\nInitialize its remainder from prefix_rem. Initialize the full-width\\nremainder from dividend[31:15] and its 32-bit quotient shift register\\nfrom {dividend[14:0], 17'b0}, where dividend is the captured magnitude.\\nIn phases 2 through 6 advance both recurrences in parallel with\\nseparate remainder registers and separate 32-bit quotient registers.\\nSelect the mode at the result mux. This register organization matters\\nfor routing. A prototype with a 15-bit wide-mode quotient register\\nreached 76.478 MHz median. Capture the original rs1 on issue for\\nREM by zero and return all ones for DIV by zero. Preserve signed\\nresult correction, INT_MIN/-1 and the issue, busy and done timing\\nin both real and ALTOPS modes.\\n\"}, {'file': 'test/test_alu.py', 'description': 'Add exact quo\n…[7743 of 10815 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:da240f8014923583]…\n(f, fcntl.LOCK_UN)\n                f.close()\n            return\n        if not told:\n            print(f\"  [eval] {what}: waiting for a host eval slot ({n} busy)\", flush=True)\n            told = True\n        time.sleep(5)\n\n\ndef eval_jobs(default: str | None = None) -> str | None:\n    \"\"\"make -j for a formal run holding a slot (HARNESS_EVAL_JOBS).\"\"\"\n    return os.environ.get(\"HARNESS_EVAL_JOBS\") or default\ntotal 116628\ndrwxrwxrwt 161 nobody   nogroup       3280 Nov 19 23:52 .\ndrwxr-xr-x  20 nobody   nogroup       4096 Sep 28 01:00 ..\ndrwxrwxrwt   2 nobody   nogroup         40 Sep 28 01:00 .ICE-unix\ndrwxrwxrwt   2 nobody   nogroup         40 Sep 28 01:00 .X11-unix\ndrwxrwxrwt   2 nobody   nogroup         40 Sep 28 01:00 .XIM-unix\ndrwxrwxrwt   2 nobody   nogroup         40 Sep 28 01:00 .font-unix\ndrwxr-xr-x   3 nobody   nogroup         60 Oct  4 01:50 .sbt\ndrwxr-xr-x   3 nobody   nogroup         60 Oct  4 01:50 .sbtf6ce0720\n-rw-r--r--   1 nobody   nogroup          0 Nov 19 14:44 auto-arch-tournament.formal.lock\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
