{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_6", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor l in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n d=json.loads(l)\n if d.get('category')=='structural':\n  for k,v in d.items():\n   print(k,str(v)[:16000])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "id hyp-20261119-002-r1s1\ntitle Move divide and remainder into a six-round EX divider\ncategory structural\nmotivation At 5.442 MHz the baseline takes 4,491,485 cycles for ten timed iterations.\nIts reported 199.837 ns path crosses forwarding and the EX ALU. The\nsingle-cycle divide and remainder operators are the likely source of that\ndepth. A reference-ISS run of the canonical 2K, -O3 binary counted\n2,922,015 instructions strictly between the timing markers. It executed\n93,960 MULs and zero DIV, DIVU, REM or REMU instructions. All five CRCs\nmatched. Division can therefore take extra cycles with no direct stall\ncost in the scored loop.\n\nhypothesis {'motivation': 'At 5.442 MHz the baseline takes 4,491,485 cycles for ten timed iterations.\\nIts reported 199.837 ns path crosses forwarding and the EX ALU. The\\nsingle-cycle divide and remainder operators are the likely source of that\\ndepth. A reference-ISS run of the canonical 2K, -O3 binary counted\\n2,922,015 instructions strictly between the timing markers. It executed\\n93,960 MULs and zero DIV, DIVU, REM or REMU instructions. All five CRCs\\nmatched. Division can therefore take extra cycles with no direct stall\\ncost in the scored loop.\\n', 'hypothesis': 'Give DIV, DIVU, REM and REMU one shared, blocking divider. Capture the\\nforwarded operands and their unsigned magnitudes at issue. Zero-extend\\nthe dividend magnitude to 36 bits and process six bits per clock using\\nsix unrolled radix-2 restoring steps. Register the partial remainder and\\nquotient after each of the six rounds. A final cycle selects quotient or\\nremainder, applies its sign and transfers it to EX/MEM. This gives eight\\nEX cycles including issue, within the existing formal progress window.\\nOther instructions retain their existing EX latency and forwarding paths.\\n\\nExpect the timed cycle count to stay near 4,491,485. At that count a\\nmedian Fmax of 8.16 MHz gives about 18.2 iterations/s, a 50% gain.\\nCompare Gowin median Fmax and marker-to-marker cycles separately. The\\nmain timing risk is that a multipl\n…[4116 of 7188 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:2aa9842394ae4df9]…\nder bus stalls. Check RVFI operands,\\nresult, order, and exactly one accepted store.\\n'}]\noutcome improvement\nfitness 96.04\ndelta_pct 692.41\nvs_baseline 692.41\nfmax_mhz 43.135\nipc_coremark 2e-06\ncycles 4491485\niterations 10\nlut4 2747\nff 565\nseeds [44.337, 43.135, 43.135]\nperturbations [[0, 44.337, 36], [1, 43.135, 36], [2, 43.135, 36]]\nlutram 8\nbsram 6\ndsp 6\ncritical_path {'from': 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu/remainder_q_0_s0', 'to': 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu/remainder_q_0_s0', 'slack_ns': -17.555, 'arrival_ns': 27.849, 'logic_cells': 186, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu']}\nlogic_levels 36\nformal_passed True\ncosim_passed True\nerror None\nimplementation_notes \ntimestamp 2026-11-19T14:20:11.741184Z\nslot 1\nround_id 1\nlesson - 2026-11-19 hyp-20261119-002-r1s1 (improvement, +692.41%): Replacing combinational DIV/REM in EX with a shared six-round restoring divider shortened the critical path and raised median Gowin Fmax from 5.44 to 43.1 MHz, while timed CoreMark incurred no divider stalls because it executed neither operation.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
