{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_1", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -n 'structural|hyp-20261119-002-r2s1' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"", "aggregated_output": "3:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261119-002-r1s1\", \"title\": \"Move divide and remainder into a six-round EX divider\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"At 5.442 MHz the baseline takes 4,491,485 cycles for ten timed iterations.\\nIts reported 199.837 ns path crosses forwarding and the EX ALU. The\\nsingle-cycle divide and remainder operators are the likely source of that\\ndepth. A reference-ISS run of the canonical 2K, -O3 binary counted\\n2,922,015 instructions strictly between the timing markers. It executed\\n93,960 MULs and zero DIV, DIVU, REM or REMU instructions. All five CRCs\\nmatched. Division can therefore take extra cycles with no direct stall\\ncost in the scored loop.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"At 5.442 MHz the baseline takes 4,491,485 cycles for ten timed iterations.\\nIts reported 199.837 ns path crosses forwarding and the EX ALU. The\\nsingle-cycle divide and remainder operators are the likely source of that\\ndepth. A reference-ISS run of the canonical 2K, -O3 binary counted\\n2,922,015 instructions strictly between the timing markers. It executed\\n93,960 MULs and zero DIV, DIVU, REM or REMU instructions. All five CRCs\\nmatched. Division can therefore take extra cycles with no direct stall\\ncost in the scored loop.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Give DIV, DIVU, REM and REMU one shared, blocking divider. Capture the\\nforwarded operands and their unsigned magnitudes at issue. Zero-extend\\nthe dividend magnitude to 36 bits and process six bits per clock using\\nsix unrolled radix-2 restoring steps. Register the partial remainder and\\nquotient after each of the six rounds. A final cycle selects quotient or\\nremainder, applies its sign and transfers it to EX/MEM. This gives eight\\nEX cycles including issue, within the existing formal progress window.\\nOther instructions retain their existing EX latency and forwarding paths.\\n\\nExpect the timed cycle count to stay near 4,491,485. At that count a\\nmedian Fmax of 8.16 MHz gives about 18.2 iterations/s, a 50% gain.\\nCompare Gowin median Fmax and marker-to-marker cycles separately. T\n…[11576 of 14648 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:18d783aaae05decb]…\nro, and signed overflow.\\n\\nVerilator lint passed without warnings. All 81 cocotb cases passed. The local ALTOPS formal gate passed on the first run with 53 checks and zero failures. Selftest cosimulation and stalled CoreMark CRC validation passed with `NRET=1`, as declared by the core. The standalone cosimulation command initially defaulted to two RVFI channels and required that build setting.\\n\\nGowin reported 3,260 logic cells and 663 registers for placement 0, up from 2,747 and 565 in the baseline. The worst setup path now runs from the register file to the ID-stage PC register through execute and hazard logic.\\n\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-19T14:38:03.541875Z\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 2, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-11-19 hyp-20261119-002-r2s1 (improvement, +14.16%): Registering 3D, 5D and 7D during the two-bit opening round let each later round resolve six quotient bits in two radix-8 stages of parallel trial subtraction and selection, raising median Gowin Fmax from 43.1 to 49.2 MHz at the same CoreMark cycle count.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
