{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_4", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -n '\\\"structural\\\"|hyp-20261119-001-r4s0' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"", "aggregated_output": "3:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261119-002-r1s1\", \"title\": \"Move divide and remainder into a six-round EX divider\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"At 5.442 MHz the baseline takes 4,491,485 cycles for ten timed iterations.\\nIts reported 199.837 ns path crosses forwarding and the EX ALU. The\\nsingle-cycle divide and remainder operators are the likely source of that\\ndepth. A reference-ISS run of the canonical 2K, -O3 binary counted\\n2,922,015 instructions strictly between the timing markers. It executed\\n93,960 MULs and zero DIV, DIVU, REM or REMU instructions. All five CRCs\\nmatched. Division can therefore take extra cycles with no direct stall\\ncost in the scored loop.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"At 5.442 MHz the baseline takes 4,491,485 cycles for ten timed iterations.\\nIts reported 199.837 ns path crosses forwarding and the EX ALU. The\\nsingle-cycle divide and remainder operators are the likely source of that\\ndepth. A reference-ISS run of the canonical 2K, -O3 binary counted\\n2,922,015 instructions strictly between the timing markers. It executed\\n93,960 MULs and zero DIV, DIVU, REM or REMU instructions. All five CRCs\\nmatched. Division can therefore take extra cycles with no direct stall\\ncost in the scored loop.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Give DIV, DIVU, REM and REMU one shared, blocking divider. Capture the\\nforwarded operands and their unsigned magnitudes at issue. Zero-extend\\nthe dividend magnitude to 36 bits and process six bits per clock using\\nsix unrolled radix-2 restoring steps. Register the partial remainder and\\nquotient after each of the six rounds. A final cycle selects quotient or\\nremainder, applies its sign and transfers it to EX/MEM. This gives eight\\nEX cycles including issue, within the existing formal progress window.\\nOther instructions retain their existing EX latency and forwarding paths.\\n\\nExpect the timed cycle count to stay near 4,491,485. At that count a\\nmedian Fmax of 8.16 MHz gives about 18.2 iterations/s, a 50% gain.\\nCompare Gowin median Fmax and marker-to-marker cycles separately. T\n…[34036 of 37108 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:cca04dd2c54af816]…\nnclude\\nan older stalled load, simultaneous bypass matches, signed high-half\\nresults and x0. Check channel-0 data and order. With ready buses,\\nindependent multiplies should retire one clock apart and an immediate\\nconsumer should retire two clocks after its producer.\\n\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 143.67, \"delta_pct\": 12.79, \"vs_baseline\": 1085.4, \"fmax_mhz\": 65.052, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4527760, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 3219, \"ff\": 733, \"seeds\": [62.767, 65.052, 65.052], \"perturbations\": [[0, 62.767, 14], [1, 65.052, 14], [2, 65.052, 14]], \"lutram\": 8, \"bsram\": 6, \"dsp\": 2, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_ex/reg_q.alu_result_4_s0\", \"slack_ns\": -10.932, \"arrival_ns\": 21.226, \"logic_cells\": 14, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_id\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\", \"cpu/u_ex\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 14, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-19T15:46:42.570926Z\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 4}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
