{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cat formal/checks_si.cfg; rg -n 'gw_sh|placement|def .*timing|\"'^timing:|''^timing-'\"' Makefile tools/eval/gowin.py | head -130\"","aggregated_output":"[options]\nisa rv32im\nnret 1\nsolver bitwuzla\n\n[depth]\n# BMC depth per check. 2nd column (where present) is the k-induction prove\n# depth. Keep depths matched to the current pipeline so bugs within ~20\n# cycles of any symbolic instruction stream are exposed.\ninsn          20\nreg       10  20\npc_fwd    10  20\npc_bwd    10  20\ncausal    10  20\n# unique   — no two retirements share rvfi_order (catches double-retire)\n# cover    — sanity that the CPU retires (prevents vacuous-pass suites)\n# ill      — illegal instructions must trap; rvfi_trap from decoder.is_illegal\n# liveness — CPU makes forward progress under any symbolic stream\nunique     1 10 20\ncover      1    20\nill             20\nliveness   1 10 20\n\n[defines]\n`define RISCV_FORMAL_ALIGNED_MEM\n# RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS — fast mode. Same as checks.cfg. See checks.cfg for\n# the full rationale on what ALTOPS does and does not prove. M-extension\n# arithmetic correctness is covered by test/test_alu.py and `make formal-deep`.\n`define RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS\n\n[cover]\n# Sanity cover: the CPU must retire at least one non-trapping instruction.\nalways @* if (!reset) cover (rvfi_valid && !rvfi_trap);\n\n[verilog-files]\n# run_all.sh rebuilds this section from the actual rtl/ glob; the list\n# below is overwritten before genchecks runs. Kept as a placeholder so\n# the section is syntactically present for any reader inspecting the cfg.\n@basedir@/cores/@core@/core.sv\n@basedir@/cores/@core@/wrapper.sv\ntools/eval/gowin.py:8:Fmax is the median over Gowin's placement algorithms (PLACE_OPTIONS), each\ntools/eval/gowin.py:105:    \"\"\"Fmax and area from a finished build, or {'placement_failed': True}.\"\"\"\ntools/eval/gowin.py:109:        return {\"placement_failed\": True, \"fmax_mhz\": None}\ntools/eval/gowin.py:114:        return {\"placement_failed\": True, \"fmax_mhz\": None, \"reason\": \"no Fmax in timing report\"}\ntools/eval/gowin.py:116:        \"placement_failed\": False,\ntools/eval/gowin.py:128:def _run_gw_sh(outdir: Path, log: Path, env: dict) -> bool:\ntools/eval/gowin.py:133:        proc = subprocess.Popen([str(GOWIN_HOME / \"IDE/bin/gw_sh\"), \"build.tcl\"], cwd=outdir,\ntools/eval/gowin.py:158:    timed_out = _run_gw_sh(outdir, log, gowin_env(env, outdir))\ntools/eval/gowin.py:160:        return {\"place_option\": place_option, \"placement_failed\": True,\ntools/eval/gowin.py:164:    if res[\"placement_failed\"]:\ntools/eval/gowin.py:180:    \"\"\"Median Fmax over placement options; every option must fit (the flow\ntools/eval/gowin.py:182:    failed = [r for r in results if r[\"placement_failed\"]]\ntools/eval/gowin.py:184:        return {\"placement_failed\": True,\ntools/eval/gowin.py:189:        \"placement_failed\": False,\ntools/eval/gowin.py:209:                    help=\"build every placement option the evaluator uses (default: option 0 only)\")\ntools/eval/gowin.py:216:        if r[\"placement_failed\"]:\ntools/eval/gowin.py:226:    if len(res) > 1 and all(not r[\"placement_failed\"] for r in res):\ntools/eval/gowin.py:228:    return 0 if all(not r[\"placement_failed\"] for r in res) else 1\nMakefile:83:\t@echo \"  make timing TARGET=v1   — Gowin Fmax and worst paths (placement option 0)\"\nMakefile:140:timing:\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
