': 50, 'confidence': 'high'}, 'changes': [{'file': 'rtl/alu.sv', 'description': 'Replace the combinational / and % arms with a clocked divider and\\nrequest/result handshake. Each restoring step shifts in a dividend bit\\nand uses a widened trial subtraction to select the next remainder and\\nquotient bit. Preserve the dividend for REM by zero, return all ones\\nfor DIV by zero, and handle INT_MIN / -1 and its zero remainder.\\nUnder RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS carry the existing per-op substitute through\\nt\n…[9281 of 12353 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:9aba0c8d52e5e2d5]…\nn is_branch is set and all bits of\\nthe sign-extended B-immediate above bit 7 are one. Save the branch\\nPC's slot index as the loop tail. Wire effective fetch validity to the\\nhazard unit and ID. For a valid FENCE.I in EX, invalidate replay,\\ndiscard the younger slot and restart at the fence PC plus four, respecting older\\ndmem stalls. Keep ID/EX capture, bypass comparisons and single-channel\\nretirement synchronized with the existing stall and bubble controls.\\n\"}, {'file': 'test/test_pipeline.py', 'description': 'Run a counted loop with imemReady low on its second pass and poison\\nthe unaccepted bus word. Check the retirement PCs, changing register\\nvalues, and exactly one accepted store per iteration under dmem stalls.\\nExercise two loops with identical low PC bits and different code, a\\nmissing word after tag replacement, the untaken loop exit, and FENCE.I\\nfollowed by a changed instruction at a previously recorded PC.\\n'}]} 4106616 [73.518, 80.18, 80.18] [[0, 73.518, 17], [1, 80.18, 18], [2, 80.18, 18]]\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
