{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_3", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -n 'structural|hyp-20261119-003-r7s2' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | cut -c1-1250\"", "aggregated_output": "3:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261119-002-r1s1\", \"title\": \"Move divide and remainder into a six-round EX divider\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"At 5.442 MHz the baseline takes 4,491,485 cycles for ten timed iterations.\\nIts reported 199.837 ns path crosses forwarding and the EX ALU. The\\nsingle-cycle divide and remainder operators are the likely source of that\\ndepth. A reference-ISS run of the canonical 2K, -O3 binary counted\\n2,922,015 instructions strictly between the timing markers. It executed\\n93,960 MULs and zero DIV, DIVU, REM or REMU instructions. All five CRCs\\nmatched. Division can therefore take extra cycles with no direct stall\\ncost in the scored loop.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"At 5.442 MHz the baseline takes 4,491,485 cycles for ten timed iterations.\\nIts reported 199.837 ns path crosses forwarding and the EX ALU. The\\nsingle-cycle divide and remainder operators are the likely source of that\\ndepth. A reference-ISS run of the canonical 2K, -O3 binary counted\\n2,922,015 instructions strictly between the timing markers. It executed\\n93,960 MULs and zero DIV, DIVU, REM or REMU instructions. All five CRCs\\nmatched. Division can therefore take extra cycles with no direct stall\\ncost in the scored loop.\\n\", \"hypothes\n6:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261119-002-r2s1\", \"title\": \"Resolve two radix-8 quotient digits per divider clock\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"Gowin traces the champion's 27.849 ns worst path from the divider remainder\\nregister back to itself. Each update chains six full-width trial subtractions\\nand six dependent selections. Eight serial steps per clock achieved only\\n31.365 MHz, compared with 43.135 MHz for six. The timed CoreMark trace\\ncontains zero DIV or REM instructions, so shortening this feedback path\\ncan improve throughput across all 4,491,485 measured cycles.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"Gowin traces the champion's 27.849 ns worst path from the divider remainder\\nregister back to itself. Each update chains six full-width trial subtractions\\nand six dependent selections. \n…[6936 of 10008 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:327891e47fe90bb0]…\nnjump still discards a fetch slot, even when its target word is present.\\nThe round-two target buffer saved 313,598 cycles on a core without\\nreplay. On the current champion, a scratch target predictor with the\\noriginal short-loop replay policy took 3,815,187 cycles. Letting a\\ntrained branch also start replay along its predicted successor saved\\nanother 83,953 cycles with the same predictor and stall generators.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"Loop replay supplies words during imem waits, but every taken branch or\\njump still discards a fetch slot, even when its target word is present.\\nThe round-two target buffer saved 313,598 cycles on a core without\\nreplay. On the current champion, a scratch target predictor with the\\noriginal short-loop replay policy took 3,815,187 cycles. Letting a\\ntrained branch also start replay along its predicted successor saved\\nanother 83,953 cycles with the same predictor and stall generators.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Read a tagged 256-entry branch target buffer (BTB) at the regi\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
