{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_6", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\na=[json.loads(x) for x in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl')]\nprint(a[-1].keys())\nfor x in a[-3:]:\n for k,v in x.items():\n  if k not in ('hypothesis','motivation'): print(k,str(v)[:5500])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "dict_keys(['id', 'title', 'category', 'motivation', 'hypothesis', 'expected_impact', 'changes', 'outcome', 'fitness', 'delta_pct', 'vs_baseline', 'fmax_mhz', 'ipc_coremark', 'cycles', 'iterations', 'lut4', 'ff', 'seeds', 'perturbations', 'lutram', 'bsram', 'dsp', 'critical_path', 'logic_levels', 'formal_passed', 'cosim_passed', 'error', 'implementation_notes', 'timestamp', 'slot', 'round_id', 'lesson'])\nid hyp-20261119-001-r7s0\ntitle Shorten divider feedback by splitting on divisor magnitude\ncategory micro_opt\nexpected_impact {'fitness_delta_pct': 5, 'confidence': 'medium'}\nchanges [{'file': 'rtl/alu.sv', 'description': \"In phase 1 register the wide and zero flags and the existing odd\\nmultiples of D. Specialize the balanced radix8_digit function for\\n20-bit operands, 21-bit trial differences and a 17-bit remainder.\\nInitialize its remainder from prefix_rem. Initialize the full-width\\nremainder from dividend[31:15] and its 32-bit quotient shift register\\nfrom {dividend[14:0], 17'b0}, where dividend is the captured magnitude.\\nIn phases 2 through 6 advance both recurrences in parallel with\\nseparate remainder registers and separate 32-bit quotient registers.\\nSelect the mode at the result mux. This register organization matters\\nfor routing. A prototype with a 15-bit wide-mode quotient register\\nreached 76.478 MHz median. Capture the original rs1 on issue for\\nREM by zero and return all ones for DIV by zero. Preserve signed\\nresult correction, INT_MIN/-1 and the issue, busy and done timing\\nin both real and ALTOPS modes.\\n\"}, {'file': 'test/test_alu.py', 'description': 'Add exact quotient and remainder checks at divisor magnitudes\\n0x1ffff, 0x20000 and 0x20001. Exercise both signs, maximum dividends\\nand dividends one below, at and one above representable multiples.\\nAlternate widths on consecutive requests and check the existing\\nsixth-round completion edge.\\n'}]\noutcome regression\nfitness 204.41\ndelta_pct 4.69\nvs_baseline 1586.55\nfmax_mhz 83.943\nipc_coremark 2e-06\ncycles 4106616\niterations 10\nlut4 3974\nff 886\nse\n…[7021 of 10093 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:b8aa673d0e67f274]…\n Check accepted\\nstore counts, RVFI PCs and order, including across older dmem waits.\\n'}]\noutcome improvement\nfitness 215.87\ndelta_pct 10.56\nvs_baseline 1681.11\nfmax_mhz 80.546\nipc_coremark 3e-06\ncycles 3731234\niterations 10\nlut4 3969\nff 935\nseeds [69.995, 80.546, 80.546]\nperturbations [[0, 69.995, 14], [1, 80.546, 17], [2, 80.546, 17]]\nlutram 76\nbsram 5\ndsp 2\ncritical_path {'from': 'cpu/u_fwd/rs1_match_q_0_s0', 'to': 'cpu/u_if/use_target_s1', 'slack_ns': -9.287, 'arrival_ns': 19.581, 'logic_cells': 19, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_if']}\nlogic_levels 14\nformal_passed True\ncosim_passed True\nerror None\nimplementation_notes \ntimestamp 2026-11-19T17:46:27.422993Z\nslot 2\nround_id 7\nlesson - 2026-11-19 hyp-20261119-003-r7s2 (improvement, +10.56%): Starting replay at the target or fall-through predicted by a BTB hit let fetch serve resident words during instruction-bus waits, saving 83,953 cycles across ten CoreMark iterations versus the same predictor with replay triggered only by short backedges.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
