{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_24","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json\na=[json.loads(x) for x in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines()]\nprint(a[-1]['hypothesis']['hypothesis'])\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"Read a tagged 256-entry branch target buffer (BTB) at the registered\nfetch PC, in parallel with the bus and the existing 64-word replay\nstore. A hit predicts the cached target or PC+4 using a two-bit\nsaturating counter. Accepting either prediction enables replay at the\nsuccessor. Continue along resident words until an accepted word misses\nthe replay store or EX corrects the path. A fresh BTB hit can start\nanother run. On each fetch the live bus has priority, and replay on a\nbus wait requires both the full sector tag and that word's presence bit.\n\nTrain legal conditional branches in both directions, and remember the\nlast aligned target of JAL and JALR. Preserve the champion's replay\non a cold short backedge. In EX check the saved prediction against\nthe full resolved successor. Register the taken target and fall-through\nin parallel so a late miss drives a one-bit selector for each address.\nFeed the BTB from the normal PC register and suppress its lookup on a\nrecovery fetch. This keeps a late EX correction off the RAM read address.\n\nA scratch implementation ran ten stalled CoreMark iterations in\n3,731,234 marker-bracketed cycles, down 9.14% from 4,106,616, with all\nfive canonical CRCs matching. Gowin placements reached 72.078, 79.550\nand 79.550 MHz. The median gives 213.20 iterations/s, 9.19% above\n195.25. At this cycle count 76.204 MHz clears the acceptance margin.\nPlacement zero used 4,034 logic cells and one additional block RAM.\nThe prototype passed all 53 standard formal checks, 96 cocotb cases,\nand the selftest and three random ISS traces with ready and stalled buses.\nA second formal run enabled lookup immediately after reset over arbitrary\ninitial BTB contents to exercise warm predictions within the proof depth.\nAll 53 checks passed in that run as well.\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
