{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_142", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"cat > cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261119-002-r8s1.yaml <<'EOF'\nid: hyp-20261119-002-r8s1\ntitle: Read the next issued instruction one fetch ahead\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The champion takes 3,731,234 cycles for ten CoreMark iterations at\n  80.546 MHz. Its BTB can predict a frequently executed target whose\n  instruction has already been evicted from the 64-word replay store.\n  The preceding instruction's fetch cycle is available for a synchronous\n  RAM read, even across a correctly predicted jump.\nhypothesis: |\n  Record the next instruction observed after each advancing EX instruction.\n  When its predecessor is fetched again, read the record into a register.\n  On the following cycle, a match with the actual fetch PC can supply the\n  word during an imem wait. The existing BTB chooses the address. Only the\n  raw instruction is replayed, so decode, operand reads, forwarding and\n  retirement run anew. A changed branch outcome or an index collision\n  can lose a hit without issuing a word from a different address.\n\n  Keep the address comparison on the valid path. On a bus wait, select\n  the successor RAM output after initialization and the existing loop\n  replay word during initialization. Compare operand tags on each source\n  in parallel, then qualify the matching source for the load-use interlock.\n  Putting the successor-address comparison ahead of the instruction mux\n  extended the path from block RAM through hazard detection to the BTB.\n\n  A scratch prototype took 3,431,589 marker-bracketed cycles, 8.03% fewer\n  than the champion, with all five canonical CRCs. Gowin placements reached\n  78.078, 78.032 and 78.032 MHz. The median gives 227.39 iterations/s, a\n  5.34% gain over 215.87. The 4.6% acceptance margin requires more than\n  77.485 MHz at this cycle count.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Infer a synchronous 1024-by-51 block RAM. Hold the previous advancing\n      EX PC[11:2] across bubbles. On the next advance write one row at that\n      index with a valid bit, the new PC[19:2] and the new raw word. Mark the\n      row invalid for a destination outside the low 1 MiB. Read at the\n      current selected fetch PC[11:2] on every unstalled edge. Hold the\n      registered response across interlocks and suppress a response when\n      the read and write indices collide on that edge.\n\n      Reset and FENCE.I discard the predecessor and pending response and\n      start a one-row-per-clock validity sweep through the write port.\n      During the sweep use the existing exact loop/path replay rules and\n      allow live fetch to continue. Afterward grant a bus-wait issue only\n      for a usable valid response with matching PC[19:2] and PC[31:20]\n      zero. A ready bus always supplies the live word. Compute the two\n      source-tag comparisons against EX.rd separately for the live word,\n      the loop word and the synchronous response. Combine the matches\n      with the same source enables used by the instruction mux.\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: |\n      Pass EX.rd and a distinct training pulse into IF alongside issue_pc\n      and issue_instr. Pulse only for id_ex.valid && \"'!stall_ex_mem &&\n      !div_wait, so a held slot trains once. Route IF'\"'s source match to\n      the load/multiply-use interlock.\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: |\n      Use the selected source-match bit in the existing interlock with\n      the valid late-result producer and nonzero rd qualifiers. Keep\n      the hold and bubble priorities for bus stalls, redirects and FENCE.I.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Run beyond the successor sweep, then withhold a repeated jump's\n      target and its dependent load-use sequence after the small replay\n      sector has been evicted. Check consecutive RVFI order, operand\n      values and accepted stores. Force an index collision with predecessor\n      PCs 4 KiB apart, change a JALR target, exercise same-row read/write\n      and hold EX behind dmemReady. Check ready-bus priority and rewrite\n      a previously recorded word across FENCE.I.\nEOF\npython - <<'PY'\nimport json, yaml, jsonschema\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261119-002-r8s1.yaml'); jsonschema.validate(yaml.safe_load(p.read_text()),json.load(open('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json')));print('Validated',p.name)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
