{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_74", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"cat > cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261119-002-r9s1.yaml <<'YAML'\nid: hyp-20261119-002-r9s1\ntitle: Forward a candidate load word from EX and validate it in MEM\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  Ten iterations on the champion take 3,495,417 cycles. A bracketed\n  pipeline profile counted 237,530 load/multiply-use bubbles and 152,215\n  cycles waiting for reads on the data bus. Every load currently produces\n  its first usable result at the end of MEM. Returning a local word at\n  EX/MEM can overlap the dependent instruction with address verification.\nhypothesis: |\n  Build a two-stage load path around a 512-word on-chip copy of recently\n  accessed RAM words. In ID, use the low bits of the register-file base\n  plus the immediate to start a word lookup. EX still calculates the\n  architectural address from fully forwarded operands. Extend the candidate\n  word for the access width and register the value, raw word and complete\n  source word address alongside the actual effective address in EX/MEM.\n  Allow the next instruction to issue behind an aligned load. In MEM,\n  validate the candidate against the full actual RAM address in parallel\n  with the consumer executing. A second read indexed by the registered\n  actual address can serve a missed early lookup without a bus transaction.\n  Keep a single registered writeback result for the bypass network.\n\n  A dependent consumer may advance only when the early value is verified.\n  On a mismatch, hold it and suppress its redirect, training, divider\n  issue and side effects. Capture the correctly extended word from the\n  second read or an accepted external read into the held EX/MEM forwarding\n  slot, then release the consumer. An independent consumer advances on\n  the cycle the load completes. Fill from accepted RAM reads and aligned\n  whole-word stores, invalidate on accepted partial stores, and exclude\n  MMIO and misalignment traps. Guard both read ports against conflicting\n  writes. Preserve the original multiply-use interlock.\n\n  A scratch prototype completed ten stalled iterations in 3,274,201\n  bracketed cycles with all five CRCs matching, a 6.33% cycle reduction.\n  At that cycle count the acceptance margin requires a median above\n  80.05 MHz. Registering the final writeback selection is intended to\n  shorten the remaining WB-through-EX timing path.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: Capture the speculative word index from the register-file base and load displacement on each ID advance.\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: Carry the candidate source address, raw word, candidate validity and load repair state through EX/MEM.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Implement two registered-address reads of the tagged word RAM. Use\n      the early word to form an EX/MEM bypass value, and the actual MEM\n      address for the second probe. Keep stores write-through. Sweep the\n      valid bits on reset and keep ordinary bus loads working through the\n      sweep. Suppress colliding rows and bypass only aligned RAM hits.\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: |\n      Wire the probes and accepted fills. Use the registered forwarding\n      matches to identify an immediately dependent consumer. Hold its\n      operands and fetch state during repair, including redirects from\n      held branches. Complete each missed bus request exactly once.\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: Select verified local or accepted bus data for writeback and RVFI. Preserve normal lane masks, raw data and traps. Provide the extended repair value.\n  - file: rtl/wb_stage.sv\n    description: Forward the final value selected and registered by MEM directly to EX and the register file.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Warm the word store and check consecutive retirements for a load hit\n      followed by a dependent branch. Force a stale base index, an address\n      alias, and an accepted byte store before a load. Stall the external\n      refill and check branch recovery, RVFI raw data, sign extension,\n      retirement order and exactly one accepted memory transaction.\nYAML\npython - <<'PY'\nimport json,yaml,jsonschema\njsonschema.validate(yaml.safe_load(open('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261119-002-r9s1.yaml')),json.load(open('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json')))\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
