{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_114", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"cat > cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261119-002-r9s1.yaml <<'YAML'\nid: hyp-20261119-002-r9s1\ntitle: Read load candidates at the three registered operand sources\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The champion spends 3,495,417 cycles on ten iterations. A profile between\n  the markers counted 237,530 load/multiply-use bubbles and 152,215 cycles\n  waiting for data reads. A load currently makes its dependent instruction\n  wait even when the core recently read or wrote the addressed word. The\n  three possible base operands are already registered at ID/EX, EX/MEM\n  and MEM/WB. Each register can start a lookup before EX selects the base.\nhypothesis: |\n  Give the load pipeline parallel probes into a 512-word store of recent\n  RAM words. Use word-index bits [10:2] of the ID/EX rs1 value, EX/MEM\n  bypass value and final registered WB value as independent read addresses.\n  Select the returned row with the existing youngest-writer forwarding\n  priority. The base alone is an address hint. EX still adds the complete\n  displacement to the fully forwarded base, selects the correct byte or\n  halfword, and registers the candidate result and its full source tag.\n  An immediately dependent instruction can now enter EX behind the load.\n\n  In MEM compare the candidate tag with the actual effective word address\n  while the consumer executes. A valid match in ordinary RAM completes\n  the load. On a mismatch, probe the same store with the registered actual\n  address, falling back to the external bus. If EX depends on the missing\n  value, hold it, capture the extended result in the older EX/MEM slot,\n  then release it with corrected forwarding. An independent EX instruction\n  may advance as soon as the load completes. Qualify all control transfers,\n  training, divider requests and side effects with operand availability.\n\n  A scratch prototype using the three base-value probes completed ten\n  iterations in 3,209,818 bracketed cycles with both buses stalled and\n  all five CRCs correct. An otherwise similar design probing only from\n  the decode base plus displacement took 3,274,201. The three-probe\n  schedule needs a median above 78.48 MHz to clear the tournament margin.\n  Infer a separate, single-read block-RAM copy per probe with a common\n  write port, so a base forwarding mux never precedes the RAM address.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: Carry the candidate word address, validity, raw word and repaired-load flag with the actual EX/MEM address and result.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Start each RAM read at its source register boundary. Pack valid,\n      RAM word address [19:2] and 32 raw data bits per row. Fill all\n      copies together on accepted RAM reads or aligned whole-word stores.\n      Invalidate the addressed row on an accepted partial store. Exclude\n      MMIO, handle same-row read/write collisions conservatively, and\n      reject any candidate made stale by an intervening store. Sweep\n      validity on reset while cold loads continue on the existing path.\n      Capture forwarded, extended data on a repair exactly once.\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: |\n      Use the existing source matches to select the early probe and to\n      identify consumers that must wait for repair. Suppress external reads\n      only on validated aligned hits in the 1 MiB RAM. Keep a missed bus\n      request stable until accepted. Qualify fetch recovery and replay\n      state updates during a repair. Preserve the multiply-use interlock.\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Verify the early candidate, then select actual-address RAM data or\n      an accepted bus response for a miss. Drive RVFI with the actual raw\n      word and byte masks. Select and register the final architectural\n      writeback value here so the WB probe starts at a register.\n  - file: rtl/wb_stage.sv\n    description: Drive register-file writes and WB forwarding from the registered result, retaining write enable, valid and x0 handling.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      After warmup, exercise each producer distance, both forwarding matches\n      at once, a nonzero displacement, and distinct addresses at one index.\n      Force a held dependent branch on a miss and check its resolved PC,\n      RVFI order and exact bus transaction count. Immediately follow\n      partial stores with signed and unsigned loads and check the raw word,\n      extended value and masks. Include misalignment and MMIO bypass.\nYAML\npython - <<'PY'\nimport json,yaml,jsonschema\np='cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261119-002-r9s1.yaml';h=yaml.safe_load(open(p));jsonschema.validate(h,json.load(open('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json')));print(h['title'])\nPY\ndate -u\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
