{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_6", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor l in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n d=json.loads(l)\n if d.get('id','').endswith(('r9s0','r9s1','r9s2')): print(json.dumps(d,indent=2)[:28000])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "{\n  \"id\": \"hyp-20261119-001-r9s0\",\n  \"title\": \"Register load-to-branch equality alongside load writeback\",\n  \"category\": \"micro_opt\",\n  \"motivation\": \"In ten bracketed CoreMark iterations, 134,571 cycles interlocked a load\\nfollowed by a dependent BEQ or BNE. Both instructions need only one bit\\nof comparison result for control flow. A scratch implementation captured\\nthat bit at load completion and trained the BTB on the actual outcome.\\nIt took 3,363,206 cycles with both buses stalling and all five CRCs\\ncorrect, down from 3,495,417. At that count the acceptance threshold\\nrequires a median clock above 82.23 MHz.\\n\",\n  \"hypothesis\": {\n    \"motivation\": \"In ten bracketed CoreMark iterations, 134,571 cycles interlocked a load\\nfollowed by a dependent BEQ or BNE. Both instructions need only one bit\\nof comparison result for control flow. A scratch implementation captured\\nthat bit at load completion and trained the BTB on the actual outcome.\\nIt took 3,363,206 cycles with both buses stalling and all five CRCs\\ncorrect, down from 3,495,417. At that count the acceptance threshold\\nrequires a median clock above 82.23 MHz.\\n\",\n    \"hypothesis\": \"Issue a dependent BEQ or BNE directly behind its load. While the load is\\nin MEM and the branch is in EX, compare the returned value with the\\nbranch's other forwarded operand. Capture equality, the saved prediction\\nand the recovery information on the edge that accepts the load. Resolve\\nthis one dependency from registers in the following cycle. A correct\\nprediction lets the younger instruction continue. A wrong prediction\\nsquashes it before it can issue a request or change architectural state.\\n\\nFor the timing implementation, compare candidate byte and halfword lanes\\nin parallel with lane selection. Check the other operand's upper bits\\nagainst the required sign or zero extension. Compute the target-match\\nand alignment checks in EX and register both correction addresses.\\nThis puts a register between the memory comparison and fetch recovery.\\nA direct combinational equa\n…[24908 of 27980 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:1113218ba295ebf1]…\n   83.741,\n    83.741\n  ],\n  \"perturbations\": [\n    [\n      0,\n      81.36,\n      16\n    ],\n    [\n      1,\n      83.741,\n      10\n    ],\n    [\n      2,\n      83.741,\n      10\n    ]\n  ],\n  \"lutram\": 32,\n  \"bsram\": 11,\n  \"dsp\": 2,\n  \"critical_path\": {\n    \"from\": \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu/quotient_q_30_s1\",\n    \"to\": \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu/remainder_q_0_s0\",\n    \"slack_ns\": -7.291,\n    \"arrival_ns\": 17.585,\n    \"logic_cells\": 72,\n    \"modules\": [\n      \"clock_ibuf\",\n      \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"logic_levels\": 16,\n  \"formal_passed\": true,\n  \"cosim_passed\": true,\n  \"error\": null,\n  \"implementation_notes\": \"\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-19T19:23:10.131100Z\",\n  \"slot\": 2,\n  \"round_id\": 9,\n  \"lesson\": \"- 2026-11-19 hyp-20261119-003-r9s2 (improvement, +4.94%): Storing the instruction and predicted target in one PC-tagged row let fetch serve hits during instruction-bus waits and let EX validate a predicted-taken branch or JAL target with the same_word bit because the matching PC and instruction uniquely determine that target.\"\n}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
