{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_11", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor l in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n d=json.loads(l)\n if d['id'].endswith(('r10s1','r9s2','r9s1')):\n  print(d['id'],d['hypothesis'].get('hypothesis','') if isinstance(d['hypothesis'],dict) else d['hypothesis'])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261119-002-r9s1 Give the load pipeline parallel probes into a 512-word store of recent\nRAM words. Use word-index bits [10:2] of the ID/EX rs1 value, EX/MEM\nbypass value and final registered WB value as independent read addresses.\nSelect the returned row with the existing youngest-writer forwarding\npriority. The base alone is an address hint. EX still adds the complete\ndisplacement to the fully forwarded base, selects the correct byte or\nhalfword, and registers the candidate result and its full source tag.\nAn immediately dependent instruction can now enter EX behind the load.\n\nIn MEM compare the candidate tag with the actual effective word address\nwhile the consumer executes. A valid match in ordinary RAM completes\nthe load. On a mismatch, probe the same store with the registered actual\naddress, falling back to the external bus. If EX depends on the missing\nvalue, hold it, capture the extended result in the older EX/MEM slot,\nthen release it with corrected forwarding. An independent EX instruction\nmay advance as soon as the load completes. Qualify all control transfers,\ntraining, divider requests and side effects with operand availability.\n\nA scratch prototype using the three base-value probes completed ten\niterations in 3,209,818 bracketed cycles with both buses stalled and\nall five CRCs correct. An otherwise similar design probing only from\nthe decode base plus displacement took 3,274,201. The three-probe\nschedule needs a median above 78.48 MHz to clear the tournament margin.\nGowin mapped the inferred multi-read prototype to 448 distributed RAM\nprimitives across the design. Give each probe its own physical block\nRAM with a common write port. Code each read as a clocked read using\nthe low bits of that source register's next value at its update edge.\nThis moves RAM addressing ahead of bypass selection and aims to recover\ntiming lost to distributed RAM routing. Confirm the mapping in the\nsynthesis report.\n\nhyp-20261119-003-r9s2 Use a direct-mapped 1024-row predictor indexed by word PC. Each row\nholds a valid \n…[2040 of 5112 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:deb5ce2672a9bd3f]…\n load whose base comes from the immediately preceding aligned LW,\nforward the accepted raw word into address generation. Capture the sum\nwith the younger load's signed displacement in EX/MEM.mem_addr on the\nsame edge that sends the older word to WB. This sustains dependent pointer\nloads and gives the external data RAM a registered address. Other operations\nthat need an unavailable operand in EX use the existing interlock.\n\nA scratch prototype completed ten stalled iterations in 3,182,385 cycles,\n6.79% fewer than the champion, with all five canonical CRCs. Restricting\nload-address forwarding to zero displacement took 3,213,302 cycles.\nRegistering the LW producer class and selecting the address base before\na shared adder reached 80.399, 81.554 and 81.554 MHz on Gowin. The median\ngives 256.27 iterations/s. Acceptance requires more than 256.56, or\n81.6482 MHz at this cycle count. Fold the class and source match into a\nsingle registered handoff bit to remove the last select qualification\nfrom address generation.\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
