{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_55", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"cat formal/checks_si.cfg; python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor l in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n d=json.loads(l)\n if d['id'].endswith('r10s0'):print(d['hypothesis'])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "[options]\nisa rv32im\nnret 1\nsolver bitwuzla\n\n[depth]\n# BMC depth per check. 2nd column (where present) is the k-induction prove\n# depth. Keep depths matched to the current pipeline so bugs within ~20\n# cycles of any symbolic instruction stream are exposed.\ninsn          20\nreg       10  20\npc_fwd    10  20\npc_bwd    10  20\ncausal    10  20\n# unique   — no two retirements share rvfi_order (catches double-retire)\n# cover    — sanity that the CPU retires (prevents vacuous-pass suites)\n# ill      — illegal instructions must trap; rvfi_trap from decoder.is_illegal\n# liveness — CPU makes forward progress under any symbolic stream\nunique     1 10 20\ncover      1    20\nill             20\nliveness   1 10 20\n\n[defines]\n`define RISCV_FORMAL_ALIGNED_MEM\n# RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS — fast mode. Same as checks.cfg. See checks.cfg for\n# the full rationale on what ALTOPS does and does not prove. M-extension\n# arithmetic correctness is covered by test/test_alu.py and `make formal-deep`.\n`define RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS\n\n[cover]\n# Sanity cover: the CPU must retire at least one non-trapping instruction.\nalways @* if (!reset) cover (rvfi_valid && !rvfi_trap);\n\n[verilog-files]\n# run_all.sh rebuilds this section from the actual rtl/ glob; the list\n# below is overwritten before genchecks runs. Kept as a placeholder so\n# the section is syntactically present for any reader inspecting the cfg.\n@basedir@/cores/@core@/core.sv\n@basedir@/cores/@core@/wrapper.sv\n{'motivation': \"The champion's placement-0 worst path runs from quotient_q to\\nremainder_q through 72 cells. At its median placement a divider\\nfeedback path is within 0.001 ns of the worst fetch RAM path.\\nCoreMark executes no divides between its markers. A shorter divider\\npath can raise the clock for all 3,414,124 measured cycles. At that\\ncycle count the acceptance threshold is 87.594 MHz.\\n\", 'hypothesis': \"Estimate an unsigned quotient twice with the same conservative\\nreciprocal, first on the dividend and then on the residual. Two\\nregistered DSP products per estimate replace the pair of s\n…[2182 of 5254 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:bb003425569ec3c1]…\n or Q+1 and R or R-D. Precompute -A in phase 1 for the D=1 and\\nD=0 selections. Preserve signed truncation, INT_MIN/-1, DIV by\\nzero returning all ones, and REM by zero returning rs1. Retain the\\nexisting ALTOPS operations, operand capture and completion edge.\\n'}, {'file': 'test/test_alu.py', 'description': 'Compare all four DIV/REM results with an integer reference around\\npowers of two, ROM bucket endpoints and representable multiples of\\nD. Include maximum dividends, both correction outcomes, both signs,\\nand alternating consecutive requests, checking the exact done edge.\\n\\nCheck the one-correction bound for each ROM bucket with integer\\narithmetic. For 2 <= D < H/2, e=H-M*D is nonnegative and one\\nestimate leaves a residual less than x*e/H+D. Two estimates\\ntherefore leave R/D < 1+e*(e+D)/(H*D). The extra term decreases\\nwith D inside a bucket. Assert e*(e+D) < H*D at its smallest\\napplicable D. All 22,527 applicable buckets passed this check.\\nFor D >= H/2 the original A is already less than 2D.\\n'}]}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
