{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_106", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -n ' FAIL|failed|AssertionError|Error:|Traceback' \\\"\"'$TMPDIR/predict_r11/pipe8.log\" | head -24; cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261119-003-r11s2.yaml | head -18'", "aggregated_output": "2:=================================== FAILURES ===================================\n106:                                                        Traceback (most recent call last):\n109:                                                        AssertionError: assert [(64, 1, 0, 0), (68, 0, 15, 17), (72, 0, 15, 17)] == [(64, 1, 0, 0), (68, 0, 15, 17), (64, 1, 0, 0), (72, 0, 15, 17)]\n110: 22782.01ns WARNING  cocotb.regression                  test_pipeline.live_deferred_branch_changes_target failed\n230:                                                        ** test_pipeline.live_deferred_branch_changes_target                            FAIL       10451.00           0.01     962299.59  **\n279:                                                        ** TESTS=59 PASS=58 FAIL=1 SKIP=0                                                         363119.06           0.46     785207.13  **\n298:1 failed in 6.91s\nid: hyp-20261119-003-r11s2\ntitle: \"Predict the resident data page for dependent pointer loads\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The champion spent 151,744 of 3,182,385 timed cycles waiting for loads and only 6,210 replaying operands. One 4 KiB page accounted for 150,188 of those wait cycles. A first prototype with a full tag on every buffered word saved 147,739 cycles, but the RAM tag comparison on the pointer-forwarding and pipeline-hold paths reduced median Fmax to 70.274 MHz. Learning the active page lets one registered tag validate many words in parallel with the dependent address calculation.\nhypothesis: |\n  Predict that an initialized word offset refers to the currently resident 4 KiB ordinary-RAM page. Learn the page online from repeated accesses. Keep 1024 raw words and a separate one-bit presence RAM. When an aligned LW supplies the next load's base, use the unchecked buffered pointer plus the younger displacement to launch its word and presence lookups. For other loads use the forwarded base plus displacement. Register whether the predicted row is trustworthy: it is exact for an ordinary base, and for a pointer handoff when the older load actually uses its buffered word. Hold this information with the load across waits.\n\n  A present offset predicts a local completion in MEM. Use that source prediction to compute the dependent pointer address while independently verifying the page, row provenance, alignment and absence of a read/write collision. If verification fails, hold the older load and its consumer, latch a retry bit and obtain the word on the external bus. Keep the request stable to acceptance. A verified local load advances while the bus is unready. The same completing raw word feeds the pointer handoff, load formatting and RVFI.\n\n  A scratch prototype took 3,033,815 bracketed cycles for ten iterations and matched all five CRCs. Three Gowin placements reached 82.715, 83.077 and 83.077 MHz for 273.84 iterations/s, 2.58% above the champion. At that cycle count the acceptance threshold is just over 84.71 MHz. The remaining timing experiment is to reuse the low bits of the existing pointer and ordinary address sums for the speculative row and compute their alignment predicates in parallel with source selection.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: |\n      Track a resident page tag and a challenger among completed ordinary-RAM accesses. Switch after nine consecutive accesses to one challenger page. Disable prediction while a reset or page change clears the 1024 presence bits. On accepted reads fill the complete raw word. On accepted full stores install the word. On partial stores write the enabled bytes and preserve prior presence. Keep stores write-through and MMIO external. Retain a read/write collision flag or the prior write index with each response. Suppress the external request on a local attempt and enable it on the held retry. Preserve annul, ready/valid discipline and single retirement.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
