{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_75","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261119-003-r12s2.yaml')\np.write_text('''id: hyp-20261119-003-r12s2\ntitle: Predict the load source in decode and replay failed resident reads\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The champion retires 2,922,016 instructions in 3,033,815 timed cycles. Even perfect single-issue throughput would gain only 3.83% at the current clock. In a bracketed trace, 538,786 of 544,852 first load attempts could use the resident word. A 64-entry last-outcome table indexed by PC[7:2] XOR PC[13:8] misclassified 682 external and 726 resident accesses. All 59,260 advancing LW-to-load pointer handoffs used buffered data. These measurements support choosing the data path before the presence RAM returns.\nhypothesis: |\n  Read a 64-entry, one-bit load-source predictor alongside decode and carry its prediction with the load. A predicted resident LW supplies the buffered pointer directly to a dependent load's address adder. A predicted external LW interlocks that consumer until WB. This allows EX to drop the parallel bus-data-plus-displacement adder and moves the source selection off the presence RAM output. Train on the verified availability of the addressed word, including on completed external reads, so entries can learn both transitions.\n  \n  A resident prediction may advance the pipeline while MEM independently checks page identity, presence, index provenance and read/write collision. Register a failed check alongside the load PC at the WB boundary. Suppress its retirement and cancel younger work before a memory request, register write, predictor fill, FENCE.I or divider issue can escape. Restart at the saved load PC with a one-shot external override that persists through waits. The retry uses the architectural base and retires once. Register the retry PC independently of the failure bit so presence RAM drives neither the fetch address payload nor the global same-cycle hold. External loads and stores still observe the bus handshake, and only ordinary RAM may validate locally.\n  \n  Measure bracketed cycles and median Gowin Fmax. At the champion cycle count the acceptance threshold is 91.42 MHz. The expected gain comes from shortening the source-selection and address paths on every load. The main risk is that divider feedback limits the timing improvement.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: Add the PC-indexed source predictor and train it on surviving loads. Carry source predictions across holds, verify resident reads, and coordinate precise cancellation and forced external retry.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: Feed the registered pointer-source choice into address generation and remove combinational bus-data forwarding into the dependent load adder. Preserve exact effective addresses and alignment checks.\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: Capture the failed resident check with the retiring payload and inhibit WB for that attempt. Retain the original load PC for recovery.\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: Accept a registered load-retry redirect and retain its PC across fetch waits. Interlock a dependent load when its producer predicts an external read.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: Exercise PC aliases with alternating source outcomes, a stale pointer followed by a store, partial-store collisions, page replacement, and a forced external retry held through several wait cycles.\n''')\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
