{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_7", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nxs=list(map(json.loads,open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl')))\nfor i in [28,30,33,34,35,36]:\n x=xs[i]; print(x['id'], x.get('hypothesis'),x.get('critical_path'),x.get('seeds'),x.get('cycles'),x.get('bsram'))\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261119-001-r10s0 {'motivation': \"The champion's placement-0 worst path runs from quotient_q to\\nremainder_q through 72 cells. At its median placement a divider\\nfeedback path is within 0.001 ns of the worst fetch RAM path.\\nCoreMark executes no divides between its markers. A shorter divider\\npath can raise the clock for all 3,414,124 measured cycles. At that\\ncycle count the acceptance threshold is 87.594 MHz.\\n\", 'hypothesis': \"Estimate an unsigned quotient twice with the same conservative\\nreciprocal, first on the dividend and then on the residual. Two\\nregistered DSP products per estimate replace the pair of serial\\nradix-8 trial banks. A 2,048-word reciprocal ROM bounds the error\\ntightly enough that one final comparison gives the exact quotient\\nand remainder. Keep the eight-cycle EX handshake.\\n\\nLet H = 2^32 and let A and D be the operand magnitudes. For D >= 2,\\nchoose the smallest shift s such that j = (D-1) >> s fits in 11 bits.\\nRead floor(H/(j+1)) from ROM and shift the word right by s to obtain M.\\nThis equals floor(H/U) for U = (j+1) << s, the upper endpoint of D's\\nbucket. Each estimate q = high32(x*M) is a lower bound on floor(x/D).\\nApply it to x=A, subtract q0*D, then apply it to that residual and\\nsubtract q1*D. If the final residual is at least D, subtract D once\\nand increment q0+q1. Apply the architectural sign to the selected result.\\n\\nA scratch implementation reached 86.266, 92.151 and 92.151 MHz across\\nGowin's three placement options. Stalled CoreMark passed all five CRCs\\nin 3,414,124 bracketed cycles. The median gives 269.91 iterations/s,\\n10.04% above the champion. The design used 15 BSRAMs and six DSPs,\\nup from 11 and two. The median placement's worst path now runs from\\nwriteback to the EX/MEM ALU result. The ALU and pipeline suites and\\ndirected reciprocal-boundary tests passed on the scratch RTL.\\n\", 'expected_impact': {'fitness_delta_pct': 10, 'confidence': 'medium'}, 'changes': [{'file': 'rtl/alu.sv', 'description': 'Capture A, D-1 and the sign and remainder flags on iss\n…[22688 of 25760 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:76f93dc127197b91]…\nng completed RAM load. Measure first-attempt sector matches, timed cycles and median Gowin Fmax. At unchanged cycles, acceptance requires more than 91.42 MHz.\\n\", 'expected_impact': {'fitness_delta_pct': 6, 'confidence': 'low'}, 'changes': [{'file': 'rtl/core.sv', 'description': 'Implement the PC-indexed sector predictor, decode-stage mask snapshot, presence updates and invalidation. Register the candidate source with the data RAM read and integrate it with existing load validation, collision handling and bus retry.'}, {'file': 'test/test_pipeline.py', 'description': 'Cover PC aliases selecting different sectors, offsets that cross a sector boundary, a store racing a captured mask, and page replacement or reset during a held pointer load. Check RVFI data and accepted bus transactions.'}]} {'from': 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu/quotient_q_31_s1', 'to': 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu/quotient_q_0_s1', 'slack_ns': -6.934, 'arrival_ns': 17.228, 'logic_cells': 44, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu']} [83.797, 84.84, 84.84] 3035403 15\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
