{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_57", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261119-003-r2s2.yaml && rg -n 'name=\\\"(warm_loop_and_exit|changing_indirect_behind_load)\\\"' '/srv/hwebench/tmp/800f6bc6/a945fa9a/predictor.R04qjsIx/cores/bench/test' -g '*.xml'\"", "aggregated_output": "id: hyp-20261119-003-r2s2\ntitle: \"Predict the next fetch PC with a tagged branch target buffer\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  A taken transfer costs one fetch slot because IF feeds ID combinationally\n  and EX resolves the transfer one cycle later. The previous direct-branch\n  predictor cut the ten-iteration bracket from 4,491,485 to 4,193,225 cycles.\n  The six-round divider champion still takes 4,491,485 cycles at 43.135 MHz.\n  A scratch prototype of a 64-entry target buffer on the champion took\n  4,191,155 cycles with both bus stalls and passed CoreMark CRC validation.\n  Gowin measured 43.793, 42.883 and 42.883 MHz. The median gives 102.32\n  iterations/s, 6.54% above 96.04 and above the 100.46 acceptance threshold.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add one direct-mapped, 64-entry branch target buffer indexed by\n  PC[7:2] XOR PC[13:8]. Each entry holds PC[19:8] as its source tag,\n  an 18-bit word target in the 1 MiB RAM,\n  and a two-bit saturating taken counter. A valid tag hit with the counter\n  MSB set selects the cached target; every other lookup selects PC+4.\n  Use the same entry format for conditional branches, JAL and JALR.\n  Train on an advancing legal transfer in EX. Allocate on a taken outcome,\n  initialize conditional entries weakly taken, and set jumps strongly taken.\n  Refresh the target on taken outcomes and decrement a matching conditional\n  entry on an untaken outcome. Qualify speculation by source and target range\n  and alignment. Use resettable valid bits and unreset distributed RAM payloads.\n\n  Capture the prediction when ID accepts the instruction. EX checks target\n  equality in parallel with direction resolution. Flush on a direction\n  mismatch or a predicted-taken target mismatch. Recover to the resolved\n  target or PC+4, including fall-through on a trap or stale nonbranch hit.\n  A recovery squashes ID/EX directly. Drive the combinational instruction\n  bus with the raw fetched word during recovery so the redirect signal can\n  bypass load-use detection and register-file address selection. Instruction\n  wa\n…[2011 of 5083 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:3ffe2fa2e0f92523]…\nretirements on a warm taken loop, then check loop exit\n      with a wrong-path store. Exercise two source tags at the same index,\n      a changing JALR target, and recovery across imem and older dmem waits.\n      Check retired PCs, link data, trap behavior and single-channel order.\n/srv/hwebench/tmp/800f6bc6/a945fa9a/predictor.R04qjsIx/cores/bench/test/test_pipeline_runner.result.xml:16:    <testcase name=\"warm_loop_and_exit\" classname=\"test_pipeline\" file=\"/srv/hwebench/tmp/800f6bc6/a945fa9a/predictor.R04qjsIx/cores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py\" lineno=\"425\" time=\"0.0006043910980224609\" sim_time_ns=\"211.0\" ratio_time=\"349111.6938856016\" />\n/srv/hwebench/tmp/800f6bc6/a945fa9a/predictor.R04qjsIx/cores/bench/test/test_pipeline_runner.result.xml:17:    <testcase name=\"changing_indirect_behind_load\" classname=\"test_pipeline\" file=\"/srv/hwebench/tmp/800f6bc6/a945fa9a/predictor.R04qjsIx/cores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py\" lineno=\"438\" time=\"0.0006709098815917969\" sim_time_ns=\"271.0\" ratio_time=\"403929.0632551528\" />\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
