ts the instruction.\\nCarry the predicted-taken bit and counter snapshot with that instruction.\\nEX knows the exact direct target from the same PC and immediate, so a\\ndirection comparison suffices. On a miss, recover to the resolved target or\\nPC+4 as appropriate. Train once per advancing, valid, legal conditional\\nbranch on its actual outcome. Correct predictions let the successor enter\\nID/EX immediately. RVFI reports the resolved PC and existing trap semantics.\\n', 'expected_impact': {'fitness_delta_pct': 6, 'confidence': 'medium'}\n…[10999 of 14071 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:bb697e4e093abc92]…\nwith\\nvalid && !stall && !div_wait. Supply the source PC, resolved target\\nand saturated counter update. Preserve resolved RVFI pc_next and link data.\\n'}, {'file': 'rtl/core.sv', 'description': 'Connect the EX training signals to fetch and feed the qualified\\nmisprediction to the existing redirect and hazard inputs.\\n'}, {'file': 'rtl/hazard_unit.sv', 'description': 'Remove redirect from flush_if. Keep the advancing EX recovery on\\nflush_id so the younger word cannot execute. This breaks the measured\\nredirect-to-instruction-to-load-use path through the fetch address mux.\\n'}, {'file': 'test/test_pipeline.py', 'description': 'Check forward progress during initialization, then run beyond cycle 256\\nto exercise warm entries. Check consecutive retirements on a taken loop\\nand squash a wrong-path store at loop exit. Exercise source PCs 1 KiB\\napart, changing and misaligned JALR targets, and recovery across imem\\nand older dmem waits. Check retired PCs, link data, traps and RVFI order.\\n'}]}\nnotes: \ntiming: None\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
