 two-bit saturating counters indexed by fetch PC[9:2].\\nIn parallel with lookup, predecode the fetched word and compute its direct\\nB- or J-immediate target. Use the counter MSB for legal conditional branches\\nand predict JAL taken. A cold entry predicts backward branches taken and\\nforward branches untaken. Allow a speculative target only when word-aligned\\\n…[17619 of 20691 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:8867d05289455db3]…\nconsecutive retirements on a hit and fall-through on loop exit.\\nPut stores on both paths and check accepted writes, RVFI PCs and\\norder during a miss with an imem wait and an older dmem stall.\\nA forward branch at word address 80 and a backward branch at word\\naddress 147 share index 17. Train the first taken, then check that\\nthe second predicts untaken on its first visit. Also exercise an\\nuntaken out-of-range target, misaligned direct targets and JALR\\nlink and trap behavior.\\n'}]}, 'expected_impact': {'fitness_delta_pct': 11, 'confidence': 'high'}, 'changes': [{'file': 'rtl/if_stage.sv', 'description': 'Predecode valid B and J encodings from raw imem_data. Use instruction\\nbit 3 to select the J or B immediate layout while the opcode and\\nbranch funct3 are validated in parallel. Compute PC+4 and the full\\n32-bit direct target independently. Read the 64-by-2 counter array\\nasynchronously at the folded PC index. For a valid branch compare\\nits MSB to instruction bit 31 to predict taken. Initialize one row\\\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
