{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_40", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"date -u && git status --short && sed -n '1,100p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261119-003-r4s2.yaml\"", "aggregated_output": "Thu Nov 19 15:42:00 UTC 2026\nid: hyp-20261119-003-r4s2\ntitle: Predict direct transfers within an 8 KiB page using an 11-bit target adder\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The champion fetches PC+4 on every accepted instruction. A taken loop\n  branch discards one fetch slot when it resolves in EX. The earlier\n  64-entry agree predictor saved 301,155 cycles over ten CoreMark iterations\n  on the previous parent. At its 4,190,330-cycle count, this round needs a\n  median above 55.83 MHz to beat 127.38 iterations/s by 4.6%. The champion\n  runs at 57.213 MHz, which leaves little margin for fetch-path delay.\nhypothesis: |\n  Predict aligned conditional branches and JAL whose target is in the\n  same 8 KiB page as the fetch PC. Nearby loop branches can then supply\n  their successor on the very next fetch. Reuse PC[31:13] for the predicted\n  address and add only the word displacement to PC[12:2]. The carry out\n  must equal the displacement sign, and the high displacement bits must\n  be a sign extension from bit 13. These checks prove the full target is\n  on the same page. Require a legal direct opcode, target word alignment\n  and a source inside instruction RAM. Predict JAL taken and use a small\n  table of two-bit agreement counters for conditional branches.\n\n  On an accepted instruction, save the chosen direction. Because every\n  predicted target is exact, one direction bit suffices to detect a miss\n  in EX. On an advancing valid EX instruction compare this bit against the\n  resolved taken direction qualified by alignment. Recover to the full\n  architectural target or PC+4 and invalidate the younger ID/EX slot on\n  mismatch. A cross-page transfer or JALR can still reach any architectural\n  target through EX. Keep instruction data and register addresses independent\n  of recovery to retain the champion's timing improvement.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Compute PC+4 in parallel with the page-local target. Select the B or\n      J displacement from raw instruction bits. Predict a branch using\n      64 two-bit counters indexed by PC[7:2] XOR PC[13:8]. A set MSB\n      predicts agreement with the displacement sign. Initialize one row\n      per cycle to weak agreement and use the static sign prediction\n      during initialization. Advance the PC on acceptance, giving EX\n      correction priority over an instruction-memory wait.\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: Carry the chosen direction and counter snapshot in if_id_t and id_ex_t.\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: Latch the prediction with its instruction on the existing ID/EX enable. Keep bubble and reset control on valid.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Resolve branches using forwarded operands. Train once per advancing,\n      valid, legal nontrapping conditional branch by saturating its saved\n      count up on agreement with the sign and down on disagreement. Compare\n      the saved prediction to the effective direction for branches and\n      jumps. On a miss use the same full successor that feeds RVFI pc_next,\n      including PC+4 for trap fall-through. Retain existing jump link data.\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: Wire the EX training port to fetch and route the qualified miss to the existing PC redirect and ID bubble inputs. An older stalled memory operation holds EX and defers correction and training.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Check consecutive retirements on a warmed taken loop and squash a\n      store on loop exit. Exercise forward and backward page crossings,\n      a long JAL whose low bits resemble a local target, and a misaligned\n      target. Check accepted writes, retired PCs, jump links and order\n      with an imem wait on recovery and an older stalled load holding EX.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
