{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_4", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -i 'predict|r5s1' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"", "aggregated_output": "{\"id\": \"hyp-20261119-003-r1s2\", \"title\": \"Predict direct control transfers in fetch with a bimodal direction table\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"Fetch currently advances to PC+4 until EX resolves a taken branch or jump.\\nIF/ID is combinational, so a redirect discards one younger fetch opportunity.\\nA temporary RTL prototype reduced the ten-iteration CoreMark bracket from\\n4,491,485 to 4,193,225 cycles with both bus stalls enabled and matched all\\nfive canonical CRCs. That gives 7.11% more iterations per cycle. Gowin's\\nthree placement options yielded 5.058, 5.402, and 5.402 MHz. Combining the\\nmedian with the cycle count gives 12.88 iterations/s, 6.29% above 12.12.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"Fetch currently advances to PC+4 until EX resolves a taken branch or jump.\\nIF/ID is combinational, so a redirect discards one younger fetch opportunity.\\nA temporary RTL prototype reduced the ten-iteration CoreMark bracket from\\n4,491,485 to 4,193,225 cycles with both bus stalls enabled and matched all\\nfive canonical CRCs. That gives 7.11% more iterations per cycle. Gowin's\\nthree placement options yielded 5.058, 5.402, and 5.402 MHz. Combining the\\nmedian with the cycle count gives 12.88 iterations/s, 6.29% above 12.12.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Use a 256-entry table of two-bit saturating counters indexed by fetch PC[9:2].\\nIn parallel with lookup, predecode the fetched word and compute its direct\\nB- or J-immediate target. Use the counter MSB for legal conditional branches\\nand predict JAL taken. A cold entry predicts backward branches taken and\\nforward branches untaken. Allow a speculative target only when word-aligned\\nand inside instruction RAM. JALR uses the existing EX target calculation.\\n\\nAdvance to the predicted successor only when ID accepts the instruction.\\nCarry the predicted-taken bit and counter snapshot with that instruction.\\nEX knows the exact direct target from the same PC and immediate, so a\\ndirection comparison suffices. On a miss, recover to the resolved target or\\nPC+4 as appropriate. \n…[51390 of 54462 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:93d89abf1510dd10]…\n\"fmax_mhz\": 70.838, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4224275, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 3315, \"ff\": 881, \"seeds\": [68.703, 70.838, 70.838], \"perturbations\": [[0, 68.703, 14], [1, 70.838, 15], [2, 70.838, 15]], \"lutram\": 12, \"bsram\": 6, \"dsp\": 2, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_ex/reg_q.alu_result_5_s0\", \"slack_ns\": -9.555, \"arrival_ns\": 19.85, \"logic_cells\": 14, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_id\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 14, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-19T16:27:24.214967Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 5, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-11-19 hyp-20261119-003-r5s2 (regression, +13.67%): Registering the predicted and recovery PCs in parallel let the late EX branch comparison drive a one-bit fetch selector, raising median Fmax from 61.4 to 71.6 MHz at the same CoreMark cycle count in paired prototypes, though final throughput trailed the round winner at 167.69 versus 174.31 iterations/s.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
