{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_8", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor line in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n d=json.loads(line)\n if d['category']=='predictor' or 'r5s1' in d['id']:\n  print(d['id'],d['cycles'],d['fmax_mhz']); print(d.get('hypothesis',{}).get('motivation',''))\nPY\ncommand -v verilator gw_sh riscv64-unknown-elf-gcc || true\nls /opt\nls -A \\\"\"'$TMPDIR\" | head -50'", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261119-003-r1s2 4193225 5.478\nFetch currently advances to PC+4 until EX resolves a taken branch or jump.\nIF/ID is combinational, so a redirect discards one younger fetch opportunity.\nA temporary RTL prototype reduced the ten-iteration CoreMark bracket from\n4,491,485 to 4,193,225 cycles with both bus stalls enabled and matched all\nfive canonical CRCs. That gives 7.11% more iterations per cycle. Gowin's\nthree placement options yielded 5.058, 5.402, and 5.402 MHz. Combining the\nmedian with the cycle count gives 12.88 iterations/s, 6.29% above 12.12.\n\nhyp-20261119-003-r2s2 4177887 42.81\nA taken transfer costs one fetch slot because IF feeds ID combinationally\nand EX resolves the transfer one cycle later. The previous direct-branch\npredictor cut the ten-iteration bracket from 4,491,485 to 4,193,225 cycles.\nThe six-round divider champion still takes 4,491,485 cycles at 43.135 MHz.\nA scratch prototype on the champion completed ten iterations in 4,177,887\nbracketed cycles with both bus stalls and all five canonical CRCs. Gowin\nmeasured 42.627, 43.038 and 43.038 MHz. The median gives 103.01 iterations/s,\n7.26% above 96.04. At this cycle count the 4.6% acceptance margin requires\n41.971 MHz. The prototype used one additional block RAM and 30 additional\nregisters. The six-round divider remained the longest path. The prototype\npassed all 53 standard formal checks and all four stalled ISS cosim traces.\nAll 53 checks also passed in a supplemental run with prediction enabled\nimmediately over arbitrary initial table contents. Directed simulation\nexercised trained entries after the actual initialization sequence.\n\nhyp-20261119-003-r3s2 4190330 50.946\nEach taken transfer costs the radix-8 champion one fetch slot. An earlier\n256-entry direction predictor cut ten CoreMark iterations from 4,491,485\nto 4,193,225 cycles. A smaller table can share a counter between a usually\ntaken backward branch and a usually untaken forward branch if it records\nagreement with their displacement signs. The champion's worst setup path\nalso crosses EX, fetch and the load-use detector on its way back to ID.\n\nhyp-20261119-003-r4s2 4191292 58.683\nThe champion loses one fetch slot per taken transfer. A 64-entry agree\npredictor previously saved 301,155 cycles over ten CoreMark iterations.\nThe current champion's worst reported path ends at EX/MEM.alu_result,\nwhere every ALU result passes through the jump-link mux. A predictor\nthat already computes PC+4 in fetch can supply the link before EX and\nremove that mux from the result path.\n\nhyp-20261119-002-r5s1 4527760 78.925\nThe champion's placement-0 worst path starts at register-file BSRAM and\nends at EX/MEM.alu_result. EX also compares source and destination tags\nbefore selecting each operand. Moving just the register-file reads into\ndistributed RAM gave a scratch build a 70.000 MHz median, with bypass\ncomparisons on its worst path. Moving just the tag comparisons into ID\ngave 71.885 MHz, with a BSRAM read on its worst path.\n\nhyp-20261119-003-r5s2 4224275 70.838\nEach taken transfer on the champion discards one fetch slot. The round-3\nagree predictor saved 301,155 cycles on its parent. On the current champion,\na paired prototype with a single fetch PC register saved 303,485 of\n4,527,760 bracketed cycles. Its worst path ran from the register file\nthrough EX to the fetch PC. Median Fmax fell to 61.425 MHz, yielding\n145.41 iterations/s. Acceptance requires 154.31.\n\n/srv/hwebench/toolchain/oss-cad-suite/bin/verilator\ngowin\nhwe-python\nhwe-toolchain\n.agents\n.aws\n.codex\n.git\ncodex-bwrap-synthetic-mount-targets-1001\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
