{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_71", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261119-003-r6s2.yaml && cat \"$TMPDIR/predictor/table16-tests.log\" | tail -16 && date -u'", "aggregated_output": "id: hyp-20261119-003-r6s2\ntitle: Register both direct successors and select the predicted fetch with one bit\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  Each taken transfer costs this core one fetch slot. The round-five direct\n  predictor used 4,224,275 cycles for ten CoreMark iterations against the\n  parent's 4,527,760. The current champion still takes 4,527,760 cycles,\n  but now registers the operands and forwarding matches before EX. At the\n  earlier predictor's cycle count, median Gowin Fmax must exceed 77.021 MHz\n  to clear the tournament margin. The champion runs at 78.925 MHz.\nhypothesis: |\n  Separate target arithmetic from direction selection at the fetch edge.\n  On acceptance, clock PC+4 and the B/J immediate target into separate\n  registers. In parallel, clock the predicted direction into a single bit.\n  A 64-entry table of two-bit counters predicts agreement with the\n  displacement sign for legal conditional branches. Predict aligned JAL\n  taken and JALR sequentially. Restrict speculative direct fetches to the\n  1 MiB instruction RAM. A correct taken prediction supplies the target\n  word on the next cycle even for consecutive branches.\n\n  Hold both candidate registers and the direction bit together on a fetch\n  interlock. When the accepted instruction reaches EX, its two candidate\n  addresses are still available. On a direct miss, capture the opposite\n  candidate in a recovery register. For JALR use the existing forwarded\n  target. Let the EX mismatch drive a registered recovery selector and\n  squash the younger instruction at ID/EX. Recovery wins over an imem\n  wait on the edge EX advances. An older stalled memory operation holds\n  EX and defers recovery and training to its release edge. This keeps\n  the late branch comparison off the data inputs of the wide PC registers.\n\n  A scratch implementation on the current champion completed ten stalled\n  CoreMark iterations in 4,224,275 bracketed cycles with all five CRCs.\n  Gowin placement options 0, 1 and 2 reached 76.813, 78.732 and 78.732 MHz.\n  The median gives 186.38 iterations/s, 6.92% above the champion.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 7\n  confidence: high\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Generate the full fall-through and direct displacement sums in parallel.\n      Use separate clock-enabled registers for both sums and the predicted\n      direction. Select the active fetch address from these or the registered\n      correction. Hash PC[7:2] XOR PC[13:8] for the 64-entry agree table.\n      Reset to weak agreement using a valid bitmap and a cold default.\n      Set prediction only for an eligible accepted instruction, and write\n      a counter once per resolved legal conditional branch.\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: Carry the predicted-taken bit and two-bit counter snapshot with the instruction through IF/ID and ID/EX.\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: Capture prediction metadata on the same enable as the instruction and qualify its use with ID/EX valid.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Resolve directions from forwarded operands. A valid advancing transfer\n      recovers on a mismatch between predicted taken and actual aligned taken.\n      For a misaligned taken transfer the resolved next PC is fall-through.\n      Export JALR target and conditional training information. Preserve the\n      architectural pc_next, link value, trap and write suppression.\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: Connect EX recovery and counter training to fetch and use the qualified miss as the hazard unit's younger-slot squash.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Check back-to-back taken transfers, trained forward branches, loop\n      exits with a wrong-path store, and replay of a successor blocked by\n      load-use or bus waits. Cover an untaken out-of-range target, a\n      misaligned jump and a forwarded JALR. Check retired PCs, order, link\n      values and bus write strobes across recovery.\n....Thu Nov 19 16:39:50 UTC 2026\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
