{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_93", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'tail -4 \"$TMPDIR/splitmatch/formal.log\" | cut -c1-180 && git status --short --untracked-files=all && cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261119-003-r8s2.yaml'", "aggregated_output": "SBY 19:02:06 [insn_sw_ch0] summary: Elapsed clock time [H:MM:SS (secs)]: 0:00:01 (1)\nSBY 19:02:06 [insn_sw_ch0] summary: Elapsed process time [H:MM:SS (secs)]: 0:00:01 (1)\nSBY 19:02:06 [insn_sw_ch0] summary: engine_0 (smtbmc bitwuzla) returned pass\nSBY 19:02:06 [insn_sw_ch0] summary: engine_0 d\nid: hyp-20261119-003-r8s2\ntitle: Predict the next instruction word from the preceding fetch PC\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The champion's branch target buffer predicts where to fetch, but a correct\n  prediction still waits for imem when its successor has fallen out of the\n  64-word replay store. Extending replay to predicted paths already saved\n  83,953 cycles in round seven. A recurring sequence also tells us which\n  instruction word to read one clock before it is needed, including the first\n  word across a taken jump.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a last-successor instruction predictor in parallel with the BTB. On an\n  advancing fetch, use the source word PC to read a synchronous, direct-mapped\n  1,024-entry block RAM. Each row predicts the next instruction as a pair\n  consisting of its destination word address and its 32 instruction bits.\n  Read the row while the BTB chooses the next PC. On the next cycle, a live\n  bus word wins. During a bus wait, accept the predicted instruction only if\n  the destination matches the full current word PC in instruction RAM and\n  the response is valid. The existing replay store can still serve a miss.\n  This can sustain one word per clock through recurring sequences longer\n  than 64 words, including jumps between distant blocks.\n\n  Train from consecutive valid instructions advancing out of EX. The older\n  instruction supplies the table index and the younger supplies its actual\n  PC and word. Carry the predecessor across bubbles and train once per EX\n  advance. A source-index collision or changed branch outcome can waste a\n  prediction, but only a verified destination can supply instruction bits.\n  Invalidate rows, the saved predecessor and the outstanding response on\n  reset or FENCE.I. U\n…[1249 of 4321 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:c0410b87d12309f0]…\nncel the response\n      on redirect and let the existing tagged replay and bus provide fallback.\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: |\n      Supply a distinct EX advance qualifier for successor-pair training from\n      ID/EX valid, EX/MEM backpressure, and divider completion. Feed the EX\n      destination register number into IF and route the selected dependency\n      comparison to the hazard unit.\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: |\n      Consume IF's selected source-register match for the live bus word,\n      predicted successor or loop word. Interlock on that match when a valid\n      load or multiply in EX will write a nonzero register.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      After warm-up, withhold imem at a recurring jump successor evicted from\n      the 64-word store. Check its instruction and retirement cycle. Exercise\n      a changed successor, two sources with the same index, a held EX stage,\n      and replacement code after FENCE.I. Check RVFI order and store counts.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
