{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_6", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor s in open(\\\"cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\\\"):\n r=json.loads(s)\n if r['id'].endswith(('r8s0','r8s1','r8s2','r7s2')):\n  print(r.keys())\n  for k in ('hypothesis','implementation_notes','fpga','metrics','timing'):\n   if k in r: print(k,str(r[k])[:7000])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "dict_keys(['id', 'title', 'category', 'motivation', 'hypothesis', 'expected_impact', 'changes', 'outcome', 'fitness', 'delta_pct', 'vs_baseline', 'fmax_mhz', 'ipc_coremark', 'cycles', 'iterations', 'lut4', 'ff', 'seeds', 'perturbations', 'lutram', 'bsram', 'dsp', 'critical_path', 'logic_levels', 'formal_passed', 'cosim_passed', 'error', 'implementation_notes', 'timestamp', 'slot', 'round_id', 'lesson'])\nhypothesis {'motivation': 'Loop replay supplies words during imem waits, but every taken branch or\\njump still discards a fetch slot, even when its target word is present.\\nThe round-two target buffer saved 313,598 cycles on a core without\\nreplay. On the current champion, a scratch target predictor with the\\noriginal short-loop replay policy took 3,815,187 cycles. Letting a\\ntrained branch also start replay along its predicted successor saved\\nanother 83,953 cycles with the same predictor and stall generators.\\n', 'hypothesis': \"Read a tagged 256-entry branch target buffer (BTB) at the registered\\nfetch PC, in parallel with the bus and the existing 64-word replay\\nstore. A hit predicts the cached target or PC+4 using a two-bit\\nsaturating counter. Accepting either prediction enables replay at the\\nsuccessor. Continue along resident words until an accepted word misses\\nthe replay store or EX corrects the path. A fresh BTB hit can start\\nanother run. On each fetch the live bus has priority, and replay on a\\nbus wait requires both the full sector tag and that word's presence bit.\\n\\nTrain legal conditional branches in both directions, and remember the\\nlast aligned target of JAL and JALR. Preserve the champion's replay\\non a cold short backedge. In EX check the saved prediction against\\nthe full resolved successor. Register the taken target and fall-through\\nin parallel so a late miss drives a one-bit selector for each address.\\nFeed the BTB from the normal PC register and suppress its lookup on a\\nrecovery fetch. This keeps a late EX correction off the RAM read address.\\n\\nA scratch implementation ran ten stalled C\n…[16068 of 19140 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:6f1d610e67677849]…\n for successor-pair training from\\nID/EX valid, EX/MEM backpressure, and divider completion. Feed the EX\\ndestination register number into IF and route the selected dependency\\ncomparison to the hazard unit.\\n'}, {'file': 'rtl/hazard_unit.sv', 'description': \"Consume IF's selected source-register match for the live bus word,\\npredicted successor or loop word. Interlock on that match when a valid\\nload or multiply in EX will write a nonzero register.\\n\"}, {'file': 'test/test_pipeline.py', 'description': 'Warm past the sweep. Withhold imem at a recurring jump target evicted\\nfrom the 64-word store, hold an older store for three clocks, and check\\nconsecutive retirement of the jump and target when it releases. Train\\ntwo sources 4 KiB apart with different successors and require a bus\\nwait on a destination mismatch. Exercise a changed JALR target and a\\nmisaligned JALR, then check patched code after a full FENCE.I sweep.\\nCheck RVFI order, instruction words and accepted store counts.\\n'}]}\nimplementation_notes \n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
