{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_108","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261119-003-r9s2.yaml'","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261119-003-r9s2\ntitle: Predict the sequential successor word in parallel with the branch target lookup\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The champion's 512-word replay store serves a wait only after a short\n  backedge or along a resident path started by a BTB hit. A straight-line\n  suffix therefore loses fetch slots even when its words have already\n  executed. Round eight showed that reading a successor one cycle early\n  can cover such waits. Most instructions have a successor address that\n  can be predicted without waiting for a target lookup.\nhypothesis: |\n  Predict the word at PC+4 on every advancing normal fetch. In parallel\n  with the BTB lookup, read a synchronous 4096-row RAM using the current\n  word PC. Fill the table from actual issued instructions. Place the word\n  from address D in row (D/4 - 1) modulo 4096, together with its upper\n  address tag and a valid bit. Thus any visit to D trains the prediction,\n  including a first visit by a taken jump.\n\n  Use the registered result on the next imem wait if that fetch actually\n  advanced sequentially and the word belongs to the current instruction\n  RAM address. The registered sequential-advance bit proves the low\n  address bits, so only the upper tag needs comparing. Hold the response\n  across interlocks, discard it on either EX correction, and let the\n  existing BTB steer taken transfers. The ready bus has first priority.\n  This adds no lookup to the BTB-to-next-PC path. Evaluate against the\n  champion's 3,495,417 cycles and 81.702 MHz. At equal Fmax, fewer than\n  3.342 million cycles for ten iterations would clear the 4.6% margin.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Add a one-read, one-write block RAM with registered read data.\n      Store valid, destination PC[19:14] and instruction in one row.\n      Register the rotated fill index, tag and word before writing. Mask\n      read/write collisions. Invalidate pending fills and responses on\n      reset or FENCE.I and sweep the valid bits through the write port.\n      Retain the existing loop and BTB replay during initialization.\n      Align the response with the normal PC enable and sequential choice,\n      and qualify its tag with PC[31:20] zero. Prefer a ready bus word,\n      then a verified sequential prediction, then eligible existing replay.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      After initialization, train a word entered by a jump, then approach\n      it via PC+4 outside an active replay path with imemReady low.\n      Check its instruction, operands and RVFI order across a backend hold.\n      Force a 16 KiB alias, a taken redirect, a live-word override and a\n      code rewrite across FENCE.I. Check the accepted stores on each path.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
