{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_10", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nr=list(map(json.loads,open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl')))\nfor a in r[-6:]:\n print(a['id'],a['motivation'],a['hypothesis'],a['critical_path'],a['cycles'],a['dsp'],a['bsram'])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261119-001-r12s0 A fresh build of the champion at Gowin placement option 1 reproduced\n87.399 MHz. Its worst setup path runs from quotient_q[30] to\nquotient_q[0] through 45 cells in the divider. CoreMark takes 3,033,815\nbracketed cycles and executes no DIV or REM in that interval. At that\ncycle count the acceptance cutoff is 91.419 MHz. Forwarding and decode\npaths are within 0.005 ns of the divider, so the area and routing cost\nof the replacement matters as well as its arithmetic depth.\n {'motivation': 'A fresh build of the champion at Gowin placement option 1 reproduced\\n87.399 MHz. Its worst setup path runs from quotient_q[30] to\\nquotient_q[0] through 45 cells in the divider. CoreMark takes 3,033,815\\nbracketed cycles and executes no DIV or REM in that interval. At that\\ncycle count the acceptance cutoff is 91.419 MHz. Forwarding and decode\\npaths are within 0.005 ns of the divider, so the area and routing cost\\nof the replacement matters as well as its arithmetic depth.\\n', 'hypothesis': 'Replace the two dependent radix-8 trials with a synchronous reciprocal\\nROM and one fixed-point Newton iteration. Store each seed at its final\\nscale. In paired prototypes, a 2,048-word ROM with a barrel shifter\\nbetween RAM and DSP reached 78.917 MHz on placement 1. Moving the scale\\ninto the stored constants and using dedicated registered products\\nreached 89.342 MHz on the same placement.\\n\\nLet H = 2^32, A = unsigned dividend magnitude, D = unsigned divisor\\nmagnitude, and x = D-1. Give D from 2 through 2048 exact singleton\\nbuckets. For larger D select the band e = floor(log2(x)), from 11 to 31.\\nWithin those bands, respectively, discard k = [1,2,3,5,6,8,9,11,12,14,\\n15,17,18,20,21,23,24,26,27,30,31] low x bits. Assign each band its own\\nconsecutive rows after the singleton rows. For j = x >> k the endpoints\\nare L = j*2^k+1 and U = (j+1)*2^k. Store M = floor(H/U). The ROM has\\n7,162 words including the bypass slot.\\n\\nCompute E = H-D*M and M1 = M+high32(M*E), then q = high32(A*M1).\\nM1 equals floor(H/D - E^2/(H*D)\n…[22888 of 25960 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:22c10f3c1783f075]…\nonfidence bits as a\\nplain bit vector. Clear during the existing sweep. Train once per\\nvalid surviving backward conditional with a representable aligned\\ntarget. Set confidence to weak after one repeated nonzero bounded\\nlength and strong after the next match. On a confident forecast\\nwrite 00 for exit or 11 for taken. Retain exact PC tagging, live\\ninstruction priority and the existing target validation.\\n'}, {'file': 'test/test_pipeline.py', 'description': 'Exercise a counted backedge long enough to learn it, then shorten and\\nlengthen the loop. Check the predicted fetch after the last backedge,\\nin-order retirement, store counts and recovery from a wrong forecast.\\nInclude an index collision, a run beyond the representable range, a\\nload-dependent branch, imem and dmem waits, and FENCE.I invalidation.\\n'}]} {'from': 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu/quotient_q_30_s1', 'to': 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu/quotient_q_0_s1', 'slack_ns': -6.506, 'arrival_ns': 16.8, 'logic_cells': 44, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu']} 3018909 2 16\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
