{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor l in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n r=json.loads(l)\n if r.get('round_id',0)>=11 and r['category']\"'!='\"'predictor':\n  print(r['id'],r['category'],r['fitness'])\n  print(r['hypothesis'].get('hypothesis',str(r['hypothesis'])[:200]) if isinstance(r['hypothesis'],dict) else r['hypothesis'])\n  print('notes:',str(r.get('implementation_notes',''))[:4500])\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_8", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor l in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n r=json.loads(l)\n if r.get('round_id',0)>=11 and r['category']\"'!='\"'predictor':\n  print(r['id'],r['category'],r['fitness'])\n  print(r['hypothesis'].get('hypothesis',str(r['hypothesis'])[:200]) if isinstance(r['hypothesis'],dict) else r['hypothesis'])\n  print('notes:',str(r.get('implementation_notes',''))[:4500])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261119-001-r11s0 micro_opt 286.13\nInterpolate a reciprocal accurate enough to estimate the entire unsigned\nquotient with one multiply. Multiply the estimate by the divisor and subtract\nthe product from the dividend to obtain a signed residual.\nIts sign and its comparison with the divisor select one exact correction.\nThis leaves the sixth round free to register the corrected magnitude before\nit reaches the EX result mux. Keep the eight-cycle DIV/REM schedule.\n\nThe two products use the same unsigned 32x32 multiplier on successive\nclocks. On the current champion this scratch implementation passed the\nALU and pipeline suites and all five stalled CoreMark CRCs in 3,182,385\nbracketed cycles. Gowin placements reached 86.392, 91.493 and 91.493 MHz.\nThe median gives 287.50 iterations/s, 7.70% above 266.94. The median\nplacement's worst path runs from WB data to the EX/MEM ALU result. The\ndesign used 4,249 LUT4s, 1,116 flip-flops, 16 BSRAMs and four DSPs.\n\nAn integer check established -D < M*D-H <= D at both ends of all\n46,137,343 fractional bins covering divisor magnitudes from 2 through\n0xffffffff, where M is the integer reciprocal and H = 2^32. M is\nconstant within each bin and both inequalities are linear in D. Since\nthe dividend is below H, the quotient estimate is always within one.\n\nnotes: \nhyp-20261119-002-r11s1 structural 285.88\nGive the divider two operand-width-specific datapaths with a common\neight-cycle EX handshake. For unsigned divisor magnitude D >= 4096,\nthe upper 12 dividend bits already form a reduced remainder. Exactly\n20 dividend bits remain. Consume one radix-16 digit per cycle for five\ncycles. Each cycle tests fifteen multiples of D in parallel and selects\nthe remainder for the largest multiple that fits.\nThis removes the second dependent trial from the feedback loop.\n\nFor 2 <= D < 4096, read floor(2^32/D) from a synchronous 4096-word ROM.\nThe high half of its unsigned product with dividend magnitude A gives\na quotient estimate q. Since A < 2^32, reciprocal truncation loses\nless than one quotien\n…[13061 of 16133 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:40ccad0867b20197]…\nted all five CRCs in 3,033,815 marked cycles. Gowin\nplacements reached 87.292, 89.944 and 89.944 MHz with 18 BSRAMs and\ntwo DSPs on placement 1. That median gives 296.47 iterations/s, a 2.91%\ngain. All three placements ended their critical path at the register\nselecting the final medium-divisor result.\n\nRetain the single remainder subtractor for the recurring rounds. On the\nfinal medium-divisor round, register the trial window and selected\nmultiple separately along with the quotient digit. The next cycle is\nthe existing result-transfer slot. Compute both 16-bit differences there.\nZero-extend the low 16 bits of window-minus-multiple for a positive\nremainder. For a negative remainder use the low 16 bits of the reverse\nsubtraction, filling the upper 16 bits with ones iff the low words differ.\nForm the signed quotient independently. The last digit no longer drives\na subtraction and a quotient/remainder mux before that register. This\nretiming needs another 1.48 MHz over the prototype to clear acceptance.\n\nnotes: \n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
