products. Choose q+1 and\n  (A-D)-p when A>=D and A-D>=p, otherwise choose q and A-p.\n\n  All terms round down. Over a non-singleton bucket, z*(z-3/4)''^2<=1/16.\n  Bound the exact polynomial deficit using D>=U-w+1. Coefficient and\n  product truncations cost less than 5/8 reciprocal unit. For k>16 add\n  (B1+2*B2)/F for truncating z. An exact rational check of every bucket\n  places the combined upper bound below 0.982. Thus q is exact or one\n  low for every A<H. For D=1 store T=2''^35-1 and use the same correction.\n  For D=0 the multiply-back is zero, the correction always selects A\n  for the remainder, and the incremented quotient candidate is forced\n  to all ones. Restore the architectural sign after correction.\n\n  Capture operands on issue. Read the synchronous ROM in phase 1, do the\n  two narrow products in phases 2 and 3, and use the wide multiplier in\n  phases 4 and 5. Register the corrected magnitude in phase 6. Transfer\n  the signed word in phase 7 through a dedicated divider-result register.\n  Forward it to an immediate consumer on the ordinary EX/MEM bypass.\n  This keeps sign restoration off the single-cycle ALU result mux and\n  preserves the eight-cycle spacing of dependent divisions under stalls.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n    description: |\n      Implement the fixed-phase reciprocal datapath, exact coefficient\n      ROM, shared 18x16 and 32x35 products, single correction and signed\n      result output. Preserve standalone ALU behavior and ALTOPS formulas.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Latch the completed word separately from the ordinary ALU output.\n      Qualify the divider bypass with the completing instruction'\"'s slot,\n      hold through stalls, and treat a forwarded DIV result as ready in EX.\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: |\n      Connect the registered divider result to EX/MEM forwarding, including\n      the JALR source check, and to MEM for writeback.\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Select the registered DIV or REM value for writeback and the WB\n      JALR comparison. Preserve existing late-add, product and load paths.\n  - file: test/test_alu.py\n    description: |\n      Check quotient and remainder at ROM interval edges and exact multiples\n      and their neighbors, including both correction outcomes and RV32M sign\n      and zero cases. Retain the existing six-round timing assertions.\nYAML\npython - <<'PY'\nimport json,jsonschema,yaml\njsonschema.validate(yaml.safe_load(open('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261120-001-r15s0.yaml')),json.load(open('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json')))\nprint('Schema valid')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "Schema valid\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
