ion to MEM and forward the registered product from WB 143.67 4527760 A placement-1 Gowin run reproduced the champion's 57.213 MHz. Its worst\nsetup path starts at a register-file BSRAM output, crosses the rs2 bypass\nmuxes and the signed multiplier DSP, then crosses six LUTs to the EX/MEM\nresult register. The next path crosses the unsigned multiplier. The timed\nCoreMark trace has 93,960 MULs but only 35,640 are followed imm\n…[3243 of 6315 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:1ef194a8b92191cb]…\nlock\nfor all 3,182,385 bracketed cycles. A median above 88.86 MHz would\nclear the 4.6% acceptance margin at this cycle count.\n\nhyp-20261119-002-r12s1 Divide with a shared multiplier and one radix-8 residual correction 299.6 3033815 The champion runs ten CoreMark iterations in 3,033,815 bracketed cycles.\nPlacement 0 reports a branch-recovery path, but the scored 87.399 MHz\nmedian placement is limited by the two serial radix-8 divider stages.\nCoreMark executes no divisions inside the timing markers. At this cycle\ncount acceptance requires more than 91.4185 MHz.\n\nhyp-20261119-002-r13s1 Estimate a quotient prefix and restore three radix-8 digits 295.06 3033815 The champion's median Gowin placement is limited by two serial radix-8 trials. Its 3,033,815 marked CoreMark cycles contain no divisions. Acceptance at this cycle count takes 91.42 MHz. Round 12 reached 90.894 MHz using reciprocal interpolation. A coarser estimate leaves enough time to reuse one digit unit and needs only a 2,048 by 23-bit coefficient ROM.\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
