{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_7", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor l in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n r=json.loads(l)\n if r['id'].split('-')[-1] in ['r12s1','r13s1','r11s2','r12s0','r13s0','r11s1','r13s2']:\n  print(r['id'],r['hypothesis'],r['changes'],r['seeds'],r['cycles'])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261119-002-r11s1 {'motivation': \"The champion's reported worst path crosses 60 cells from quotient_q to\\nremainder_q. Its small-divisor mode resolves two dependent radix-8\\ndigits on that path. CoreMark executes zero DIV or REM instructions\\nbetween the markers, so a shorter feedback path can improve the clock\\nfor all 3,182,385 bracketed cycles. A median above 88.86 MHz would\\nclear the 4.6% acceptance margin at this cycle count.\\n\", 'hypothesis': 'Give the divider two operand-width-specific datapaths with a common\\neight-cycle EX handshake. For unsigned divisor magnitude D >= 4096,\\nthe upper 12 dividend bits already form a reduced remainder. Exactly\\n20 dividend bits remain. Consume one radix-16 digit per cycle for five\\ncycles. Each cycle tests fifteen multiples of D in parallel and selects\\nthe remainder for the largest multiple that fits.\\nThis removes the second dependent trial from the feedback loop.\\n\\nFor 2 <= D < 4096, read floor(2^32/D) from a synchronous 4096-word ROM.\\nThe high half of its unsigned product with dividend magnitude A gives\\na quotient estimate q. Since A < 2^32, reciprocal truncation loses\\nless than one quotient unit, so q is exact or one low. Form R = A - q*D.\\nIf R >= D, increment q and subtract D once. Place register boundaries\\nbetween the lookup, the two DSP products and correction. Both paths\\ndeliver their selected signed quotient or remainder at the existing\\ncompletion edge.\\n\\nA scratch implementation passed the ALU and pipeline suites and all\\nfive CoreMark CRCs with both buses stalled. A separate sweep checked\\n896,000 DIV, DIVU, REM and REMU results against integer arithmetic,\\nincluding every small divisor and both correction outcomes. CoreMark\\ntook 3,182,385 bracketed cycles. Gowin placements reached 83.749,\\n89.856 and 89.856 MHz, giving 282.35 iterations/s at the median,\\n5.77% above the champion. At the median placement, the worst path\\nran from EX/MEM.alu_op to MEM/WB.wb_data. Gowin used 4,764 logic\\ncells, 19 BSRAMs and five DSPs. Sharing the two reciprocal\n…[35104 of 38176 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:798530e8723eed95]…\n.\\n'}]} [{'file': 'rtl/if_stage.sv', 'description': 'Infer a 16 by 14-bit distributed RAM indexed by word PC bits [5:2].\\nPack the current phase, last exit phase and two confidence bits as a\\nplain bit vector. Clear during the existing sweep. Train once per\\nvalid surviving backward conditional with a representable aligned\\ntarget. Set confidence to weak after one repeated nonzero bounded\\nlength and strong after the next match. On a confident forecast\\nwrite 00 for exit or 11 for taken. Retain exact PC tagging, live\\ninstruction priority and the existing target validation.\\n'}, {'file': 'test/test_pipeline.py', 'description': 'Exercise a counted backedge long enough to learn it, then shorten and\\nlengthen the loop. Check the predicted fetch after the last backedge,\\nin-order retirement, store counts and recovery from a wrong forecast.\\nInclude an index collision, a run beyond the representable range, a\\nload-dependent branch, imem and dmem waits, and FENCE.I invalidation.\\n'}] [86.911, 87.09, 87.09] 3018909\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
