{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_8", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"git log -5 --oneline\nsed -n '1,220p' tools/eval/gowin.py\nls -la /opt/gowin\nls -la /opt/hwe-toolchain\"", "aggregated_output": "78e0fc8 log: hyp-20261119-003-r13s2 regression\n6791af7 log: hyp-20261119-002-r13s1 regression\n469637e log: hyp-20261119-001-r13s0 regression\nd107047 log: hyp-20261119-003-r12s2 regression\nf371521 log: hyp-20261119-002-r12s1 regression\n\"\"\"Vendor place-and-route and timing for the FPGA fitness (HWE Bench V2).\n\nV2 times designs with Gowin EDA (the FPGA vendor's own synthesis, place and\nroute and static timing analysis) instead of Yosys + nextpnr, whose timing\nmodel for this part misses whole classes of paths. The vendor flow is also\ndeterministic and insensitive to circuit-neutral netlist changes.\n\nFmax is the median over Gowin's placement algorithms (PLACE_OPTIONS), each\na full build of the same RTL; results are deterministic for a given input.\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nfrom concurrent.futures import ThreadPoolExecutor\nimport os\nimport re\nimport shutil\nimport statistics\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nfrom tools.eval._subprocess import remove_path\n\nGOWIN_HOME = Path(os.environ.get(\"GOWIN_HOME\", \"/opt/gowin\"))\nGOWIN_VERSION = \"1.9.11.03 Education\"\nPART = \"GW2AR-LV18QN88C8/I7\"      # Tang Nano 20K\nDEVICE_VERSION = \"C\"\nPLACE_OPTIONS = (0, 1, 2)\nCST = \"fpga/constraints/Tang_Nano_20K.cst\"\nSDC = \"fpga/constraints/clock.sdc\"\nSTALL_GEN = \"fpga/bench_stall_gen.sv\"\nBUILD_TIMEOUT_SEC = 2700\n\n\ndef gowin_env(base: dict | None, workdir: Path) -> dict:\n    env = dict(os.environ if base is None else base)\n    libs = [GOWIN_HOME / \"deps/root/usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu\", GOWIN_HOME / \"IDE/lib\"]\n    env[\"LD_LIBRARY_PATH\"] = \":\".join(map(str, libs))\n    env[\"QT_QPA_PLATFORM\"] = \"offscreen\"\n    xdg = workdir / \".xdg\"\n    xdg.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    os.chmod(xdg, 0o700)\n    env[\"XDG_RUNTIME_DIR\"] = str(xdg)\n    return env\n\n\ndef rtl_sources(rtl_dir: Path) -> list[Path]:\n    srcs = sorted(rtl_dir.glob(\"*.sv\"))\n    pkg = rtl_dir / \"core_pkg.sv\"\n    return ([pkg] if pkg in srcs else []) + [p for p in srcs if p != pkg]\n\n\ndef project_tcl(worktree: Path, rtl_dir: Path, bench_sv: str, place_option: int) -> str:\n    files = \n…[7457 of 10529 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:0eb51439e56e22c3]…\nns=opts)\n    for r in res:\n        if r[\"placement_failed\"]:\n            print(f\"place_option {r['place_option']}: FAILED ({r.get('reason')})\")\n            continue\n        print(f\"place_option {r['place_option']}: Fmax {r['fmax_mhz']} MHz, {r['levels']} logic levels; \"\n              f\"logic {r['logic']}, registers {r['regs']}, LUT-RAM {r['lutram']}, BSRAM {r['bsram']}, DSP {r['dsp']}\")\ntotal 24\ndrwxr-xr-x  5 nobody nogroup 4096 Sep 28 05:13 .\ndrwxr-xr-x  5 nobody nogroup 4096 Sep 28 05:13 ..\ndrwxr-xr-x 10 nobody nogroup 4096 Jul 10  2025 IDE\ndrwxr-xr-x  5 nobody nogroup 4096 Jul  5  2025 Programmer\ndrwxr-xr-x  4 nobody nogroup 4096 Sep 28 04:16 deps\n-rw-r--r--  1 nobody nogroup   76 Sep 28 04:15 gowin.tgz.sha256\ntotal 20\ndrwxr-xr-x  5 nobody nogroup 4096 Sep 28 02:44 .\ndrwxr-xr-x  5 nobody nogroup 4096 Sep 28 05:13 ..\ndrwxr-xr-x  2 nobody nogroup 4096 Sep 28 02:44 bin\ndrwxr-xr-x 12 nobody nogroup 4096 Apr 24  2026 oss-cad-suite\ndrwxr-xr-x 10 nobody nogroup 4096 Oct 23  2025 xpack-riscv-none-elf-gcc-15.2.0-1\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor l in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n r=json.loads(l)\n if r['id'].endswith(('r12s1','r12s0','r10s0')): print(r['id'],r['hypothesis']['hypothesis'])\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_9", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor l in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n r=json.loads(l)\n if r['id'].endswith(('r12s1','r12s0','r10s0')): print(r['id'],r['hypothesis']['hypothesis'])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261119-001-r10s0 Estimate an unsigned quotient twice with the same conservative\nreciprocal, first on the dividend and then on the residual. Two\nregistered DSP products per estimate replace the pair of serial\nradix-8 trial banks. A 2,048-word reciprocal ROM bounds the error\ntightly enough that one final comparison gives the exact quotient\nand remainder. Keep the eight-cycle EX handshake.\n\nLet H = 2^32 and let A and D be the operand magnitudes. For D >= 2,\nchoose the smallest shift s such that j = (D-1) >> s fits in 11 bits.\nRead floor(H/(j+1)) from ROM and shift the word right by s to obtain M.\nThis equals floor(H/U) for U = (j+1) << s, the upper endpoint of D's\nbucket. Each estimate q = high32(x*M) is a lower bound on floor(x/D).\nApply it to x=A, subtract q0*D, then apply it to that residual and\nsubtract q1*D. If the final residual is at least D, subtract D once\nand increment q0+q1. Apply the architectural sign to the selected result.\n\nA scratch implementation reached 86.266, 92.151 and 92.151 MHz across\nGowin's three placement options. Stalled CoreMark passed all five CRCs\nin 3,414,124 bracketed cycles. The median gives 269.91 iterations/s,\n10.04% above the champion. The design used 15 BSRAMs and six DSPs,\nup from 11 and two. The median placement's worst path now runs from\nwriteback to the EX/MEM ALU result. The ALU and pipeline suites and\ndirected reciprocal-boundary tests passed on the scratch RTL.\n\nhyp-20261119-001-r12s0 Replace the two dependent radix-8 trials with a synchronous reciprocal\nROM and one fixed-point Newton iteration. Store each seed at its final\nscale. In paired prototypes, a 2,048-word ROM with a barrel shifter\nbetween RAM and DSP reached 78.917 MHz on placement 1. Moving the scale\ninto the stored constants and using dedicated registered products\nreached 89.342 MHz on the same placement.\n\nLet H = 2^32, A = unsigned dividend magnitude, D = unsigned divisor\nmagnitude, and x = D-1. Give D from 2 through 2048 exact singleton\nbuckets. For larger D select the band e = floor(log2(x)), from 11 t\n…[1584 of 4656 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:bee72cc131f4b2d4]…\ndth with divisor magnitude so its output needs no\nvariable shift. Across 261,374 constant-output intervals covering every\nD from 2 to 0xffffffff, integer endpoint checks gave\n0 <= 2^32/D-M <= 20568/4417, below five. Since A < 2^32, the correction\nfits in one radix-8 digit even after quotient truncation. This leaves\nroom for inexpensive interpolation and lets operand capture occur before\nmagnitude conversion, away from the main forwarding path.\n\nA scratch prototype passed 61 pipeline tests, the ALU suite and 5,006\nadditional division cases. It matched all five stalled CoreMark CRCs\nin 3,033,815 bracketed cycles. Gowin placed\nit at 86.531, 91.067 and 91.067 MHz. The median gives 300.17 iterations/s,\nup 4.20%, or 1.16 iterations/s short of the acceptance threshold.\nThe design used 4,627 logic cells, 1,325 registers, 38 BSRAMs and five\nDSPs. Its median critical path ran from the data-page presence RAM to the\nfetch RAM. A prototype with\nseparate estimate and multiply-back paths reached 86.241 MHz on placement 1.\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
