{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor raw in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n d=json.loads(raw)\n if d['id'].endswith('r12s1'): print(d['changes'][0]['description'])\nPY\nrg 'module|assign' fpga/core_bench_si.sv | tail -35\nls -ld \\\"\"'$TMPDIR\"\nwhich python'","aggregated_output":"Capture the forwarded operands and sign flags on issue. Register\nunsigned A and D in phase 1. Bypass D=0 and D=1 in the final\nmagnitude selector. For D>=2 let e=floor(log2(D)) and use\nk=min(e,max(0,floor((3*e-31)/2))). In each power-of-two band\ngroup consecutive divisors into aligned buckets of width w=2^k.\nIn phase 2 read a synchronous packed block ROM at the band's base\nrow plus the bucket number. Pack bands consecutively starting at\nrow zero for e=0 (6,140 rows). For the inclusive bucket endpoint U\nstore C=floor(2^32/U) and S=floor(2^32*w/U^2), using S=0 for w=1.\nRegister F=floor(256*(U-D)/w) by selecting and complementing the\nwithin-bucket bits, padding on the right for k<8. Use wide unsigned\ninteger arithmetic to generate the table at elaboration. Emit the\n43-bit rows as constants or initialize in blocks of at most 1,024.\nRow zero is unused and can be zero. Size the coefficient arithmetic\nto represent U squared, including (2^32-1)^2, without signed overflow.\nIn phase 3 register M=C+((S*F)>>8). In phases 4 and 5 drive one\nunsigned 32x32 product with (A,M) and (q,D) on successive clocks.\nRegister the 32-bit residual. Compute the seven multiples of D in\nparallel with estimation and retain their overflow bits. In phase\n6 compare and subtract the seven candidates in parallel, rejecting\noverflowed multiples. Select a matched digit and difference with\na balanced tree. Register the requested magnitude and restore its\nsign in phase 7. Preserve signed remainder, signed overflow, zero\ndivisor results, reset cancellation and the ALTOPS completion edge.\n\nmodule core_bench (\n  assign dmem_rdata = dmem[dmem_addr[12:2]];\n  assign led = ^{imem_addr, dmem_addr, dmem_wdata, dmem_wen, dmem_ren, dmem_rdata};\nendmodule\ndrwxrwx---+ 7 nobody nogroup 4096 Nov 20 01:02 /srv/hwebench/tmp/800f6bc6/00b86c46\n/srv/hwebench/venv/bin/python\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
