{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_63", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"cat > cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261120-002-r14s1.yaml <<'YAML'\nid: hyp-20261120-002-r14s1\ntitle: \\\"Divide wide operands with a 16-bit divisor and one exact correction\\\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The champion's median placement reaches 87.399 MHz and is limited by two\n  serial radix-8 trials. CoreMark executes zero divides between its markers.\n  At 3,033,815 cycles for ten iterations, acceptance requires 91.42 MHz.\n  Round 11 used fifteen full-width trial subtractors for large divisors.\n  The largest divisors produce the shortest quotients, which makes it\n  possible to discard low divisor bits for digit selection and still correct\n  the final quotient with one product.\nhypothesis: |\n  Use a single radix-16 digit unit with a 16-bit remainder and 20-bit trial\n  differences. For unsigned magnitudes D >= 65536, choose shift s according\n  to the highest set bit e of D. Use s=1 for e=16, 2 for e=17, 4 for\n  e=18..19, 8 for e=20..23, and 16 for e=24..31. Divide A>>s by D>>s\n  in four nibble rounds. The quotient estimate q fits in 16 bits.\n\n  Let B=(D>>s)<<s. The estimate is exactly floor(A/B). For every band,\n  A/B - A/D = A*(D-B)/(B*D) < 2\"'^32*(2''^s-1)/2''^(2e) < 1.\n  Thus q is the true quotient or one high. Form the full product P=q*D.\n  When P>A, use q-1 and A+D-P. Otherwise use q and A-P. A 33-bit P\n  suffices since P <= A+D. Apply the architectural signs once.\n\n  For 1024 <= D < 65536 the same digit unit divides by D exactly. At the\n  opening edge divide the upper 12 bits of A by D using the four possible\n  prefix digits 0..3. Save that digit and its remainder. Five radix-16\n  rounds append the remaining 20 dividend bits. For 2 <= D < 1024,\n  a synchronous 1024-word ROM supplies floor(2''^32/D). The high word of\n  A times this reciprocal is exact or one low. One multiply-back and\n  comparison complete both quotient and remainder. Handle D=0 and D=1\n  explicitly. Keep issue, six arithmetic rounds and transfer on the\n  existing edges in real arithmetic and ALTOPS.\n\n  A scratch implementation with the 1024-word ROM passed the existing\n  ALU and pipeline suites. Timing depends on the physical placement of\n  the shared multiplier and the fetch memories. Measure median Gowin Fmax\n  and marked cycles together.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n    description: |\n      Capture signs and magnitudes at issue. In phase 1 select the two\n      operand slices, register the divisor multiples, and initialize the\n      partial remainder. Use one parallel trial bank and a balanced digit\n      selector. For wide D finish the fourth digit in phase 5 and register\n      q*D in phase 6. Prepare A+D and both signed quotient candidates in\n      parallel for transfer. For small D use the reciprocal in phase 3\n      and multiply back in phase 4. Keep standalone MUL behavior and all\n      four ALTOPS divide functions.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Feed ordinary M-unit operands from the forwarded register values.\n      Launch division only when its instruction survives annul and replay\n      and an older MEM instruction can advance. Hold the architectural\n      operand values for RVFI until transfer.\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: |\n      Carry the internal shared product from the M unit to MEM. Preserve\n      the ordinary pipeline interlock and single-channel retirement.\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Use the shared product for architectural MUL and the three high-half\n      variants with their respective operand signedness. Ordinary multiplies\n      retain one-per-cycle throughput and the existing WB bypass schedule.\n  - file: test/test_alu.py\n    description: |\n      Check both correction directions, exact multiples and their neighbors\n      at every shift boundary. Include A=0xffffffff and D=65537, cases\n      where q*D crosses 2''^32, both operand signs, zero, and INT_MIN/-1.\n      Keep the input-change and completion-edge assertions.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Exercise consecutive MULH, DIV and REM with a result dependency,\n      a held older store and an annulled divide. Verify the original\n      operands, writeback value, and exactly one in-order retirement each.\nYAML\npython - <<'\"'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json,jsonschema,yaml\nf=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261120-002-r14s1.yaml');jsonschema.validate(yaml.safe_load(f.read_text()),json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
