{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_77","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261120-002-r14s1.yaml')\ns=p.read_text().replace('  A scratch implementation with the 1024-word ROM passed the existing\\\\n  ALU and pipeline suites. Timing depends on the physical placement of\\\\n  the shared multiplier and the fetch memories. Measure median Gowin Fmax\\\\n  and marked cycles together.', '''  A prototype with one 16-way multiple selector and one remainder subtractor\n  passed the ALU and pipeline suites, including additional correction-boundary\n  vectors. CoreMark validated all five CRCs in 3,033,815 marked cycles. Gowin\n  placement 1 reached 89.944 MHz with 18 BSRAMs and two DSPs. Its limiting\n  path ran from the dividend digit register to the final medium-divisor result.\n\n  Group the sixteen thresholds in fours. Each group selects a multiple\n  locally and subtracts it from the trial window using one 16-bit\n  subtractor. In parallel, the tests at 4D, 8D and 12D select the group.\n  Register the digit and remainder independently. Select quotient versus\n  remainder on the transfer cycle. This removes the 16-way multiple mux\n  from in front of the final subtraction and gives a concrete timing target\n  of 1.48 MHz above the measured single-subtractor prototype.''').replace('      selector. For wide D finish','      selector with four parallel group remainders. Build the odd multiples\\\\n      with shifts and adds, including carry-save sums for 11D and 13D.\\\\n      Derive even multiples by shifts of the registered odd multiples so the\\\\n      multiply-back DSP stays available for architectural MUL. For wide D finish')\np.write_text(s)\nPY\npython - <<'PY'\nimport json,yaml,jsonschema\nfrom pathlib import Path\nf=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261120-002-r14s1.yaml')\nh=yaml.safe_load(f.read_text());jsonschema.validate(h,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nassert h['id']==f.stem and h['category']=='structural'\nprint('schema valid')\nPY\ntail -3 \\\"\"'$TMPDIR/mshare/pnrv13_1/gw.log\"'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
