{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_7", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor r in map(json.loads,open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl')):\n if r['id'].endswith(('r12s2','r13s2','r14s2','r11s2','r12s1')):\n  print(r['id'],r['hypothesis'],r['implementation_notes'], r['critical_path'])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261119-003-r11s2 {'motivation': 'The champion spent 151,744 of 3,182,385 timed cycles waiting for loads and only 6,210 replaying operands. One 4 KiB page accounted for 150,188 of those wait cycles. A first prototype with a full tag on every buffered word saved 147,739 cycles, but the RAM tag comparison on the pointer-forwarding and pipeline-hold paths reduced median Fmax to 70.274 MHz. Learning the active page lets one registered tag validate many words in parallel with the dependent address calculation.\\n', 'hypothesis': \"Predict that an initialized word offset refers to the currently resident 4 KiB ordinary-RAM page. Learn the page online from repeated accesses. Keep 1024 raw words and a separate one-bit presence RAM. When an aligned LW supplies the next load's base, use the unchecked buffered pointer plus the younger displacement to launch its word and presence lookups. For other loads use the forwarded base plus displacement. Register one bit certifying that the index came from an ordinary forwarded base or from a pointer that the older load actually supplied locally. Hold this information with the load across waits.\\n\\nA present offset predicts a local completion in MEM. Use that source prediction to compute the dependent pointer address while independently verifying the page, row provenance, alignment and absence of a read/write collision. If verification fails, hold the older load and its consumer, latch a retry bit and obtain the word on the external bus. Keep the request stable to acceptance. A verified local load advances while the bus is unready. The same completing raw word feeds the pointer handoff, load formatting and RVFI.\\n\\nA scratch prototype took 3,033,815 bracketed cycles for ten iterations and matched all five CRCs. Three Gowin placements reached 82.715, 83.077 and 83.077 MHz for 273.84 iterations/s, 2.58% above the champion. Starting with an empty page selector preserved the cycle count and passed all 59 pipeline tests. Its three placements reached 79.201, 80.966 and 80.966 MHz, yieldi\n…[17056 of 20128 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:3afa65928c27b70d]…\nget identity. Select the\\nregistered EX outcome or resolve equality using the required WB\\noperand. On a miss redirect to the architectural successor and\\nannul younger side effects before they reach memory or retirement.\\n'}, {'file': 'test/test_pipeline.py', 'description': 'Exercise one branch after two load values that demand opposite\\ndirections. Check both repair paths, PC and context aliases, a\\nreplaced instruction, FENCE.I and dmem waits. Assert exact RVFI\\norder, trap behavior and accepted store counts on recovery. In the\\nreplay/live-word case account for the sixth fetch at 0x140 and\\ninject all three exit waits on the corrected path. In the nonzero\\nJALR case distinguish its two issued visits from the later squashed\\nvisit that coincides with the older branch redirect to PC 44.\\n'}]}  {'from': 'cpu/u_if/gen_ram[0].rows_gen_ram[0].rows_0_0_s0', 'to': 'cpu/u_if/gen_ram[32].rows_gen_ram[32].rows_0_0_s', 'slack_ns': -7.01, 'arrival_ns': 17.305, 'logic_cells': 32, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_if']}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
